{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tg8zkKhbM89DPj51C4Yvcy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# researchPrime — Phase 1 PLAN (frozen)\n2\t\n3\t**Run:** Aurora Awareness Revamp research. **Mode:** ENGINE (node v26.1.0, import spike go:true).\n4\t**Sub-agent axis:** parallel-swarm (Agent tool present). **ISOLATION:** approximated→real (sub-agents are fresh-context).\n5\t\n6\t## AXIS (load-bearing win condition)\n7\tFor each of the 6 §5 questions, identify the patterns/techniques that are (a) genuinely USED vs merely admired, AND (b) serve John's North Star — awareness + adoption-decision + agent-feeding — AND (c) for build items, are dependency-light / offline / nightly-automatable on Aurora's existing stack.\n8\t\n9\t**FALSIFIER for any candidate recommendation:** it is pretty/popular but does NOT make John more aware or better-decided; OR it is not buildable dependency-light/offline/nightly; OR it depends on data Aurora cannot collect (e.g. live human-vote leaderboards it can't mirror). Any rec that trips a falsifier is downgraded or dropped.\n10\t\n11\t## Stakes VECTOR\n12\t- **Impact:** medium-high — informs a real dashboard+backend revision and ongoing ~$1/night spend + John's field-awareness/decisions.\n13\t- **Reversibility:** high — output is a research doc feeding a planning gate; nothing built yet; dashboard is read-only/evolvable. (Not irreversible → no forced floor from reversibility.)\n14\t- **Blast radius:** contained — Aurora project + John's attention/spend.\n15\t- **Projected tier:** MEDIUM → Phase-3 fires Synthesizer + context-free Judge + conditional debate.\n16\t\n17\t## Candidate branches (named, no winner declared)\n18\t- Q1 Awareness surfaces: tech-radar (ThoughtWorks) / leaderboard-board / newsletter-digest / \"state of AI\" annual / changelog-feed.\n19\t- Q2 Model intelligence: leaderboard-mirror vs curated-best-in-class-table vs price/perf-frontier; benchmark sources (which are machine-collectable + license-permitting).\n20\t- Q3 Adoption-decision UX: RFC/ADR-style card / tinder-swipe queue / scorecard-with-recommendation / dependabot-style PR.\n21\t- Q4 Knowledge map: concept-map / knowledge-graph / landscape-quadrant / force-directed / Sankey / Voronoi-treemap / UMAP-t-SNE projection / constellation — recommend ONE that is dependency-light+offline for ~hundreds of items.\n22\t- Q5 Collection targeting: source-list + ranking strategy to buy frontier signal not arxiv volume.\n23\t- Q6 Honest value framing: ROI/value metrics for a personal intelligence pipeline that avoid vanity metrics.\n24\t- Critique: blunt Fable-5-style verdict — is Aurora worth running; 3–5 changes to make it genuinely valuable.\n25\t\n26\t## Best-in-class baselines to beat\n27\tThoughtWorks Technology Radar; a16z/State-of-AI report; Artificial Analysis & LMArena & OpenRouter rankings; Hugging Face Open LLM Leaderboard; Dependabot/Renovate review UX; Obsidian/Roam graph view; concept-map pedagogy (Novak); Stripe/Linear \"changelog\" surfaces.\n28\t\n29\t## Oranges foresight receipt (required)\n30\t**Reordered:** Q5 (collection targeting) + Q6 (value framing) elevated AHEAD of Q4 (map aesthetics) in priority, because the load-bearing question John pressed hardest is \"am I wasting ~$1/night / are we pointed at the right sources,\" not viz polish.\n31\t**Dropped/down-weighted branch:** heavy embedding-projection maps (UMAP/t-SNE with interactive WebGL) as a *primary* recommendation — they are dependency-heavy and offline-hostile, tripping the §5-Q4 \"dependency-light + offline\" falsifier.\n32\t**Counterfactual cost of the drop:** if John specifically wanted a UMAP \"constellation,\" down-weighting it loses that option — mitigated by still surveying it and reporting it as a secondary/optional technique, not excluding it from the ledger.\n33\t\n34\t## Freeze\n35\tPlan frozen. Execution reads only this plan (quoted). STOP.\n36\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RiqtGSRiHPW8WJeLKyY94p","session_id