{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NRJxvBfQLnZrywBjhwUEhY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t<#\n2\t.SYNOPSIS\n3\t  Idempotent setup script for Aurora's 6 Windows Scheduled Tasks + the Windows\n4\t  Update Active-Hours / ScheduledInstallTime registry pin.\n5\t\n6\t.DESCRIPTION\n7\t  Bucket F4 (v4.3, 2026-05-19). Captures the live state of:\n8\t    - Aurora-Agents            (22:00 daily local)\n9\t    - Aurora-Skills            (23:00 daily local)\n10\t    - Aurora-Tools             (00:00 daily local)\n11\t    - Aurora-Models            (02:00 daily local)  [Bucket L M-10]\n12\t    - Aurora-Morning-Briefing  (08:30 daily local)\n13\t    - Aurora-Source-Push       (:30 hourly local)\n14\t  Each task: WakeToRun=True, StartWhenAvailable=True, RestartCount=2,\n15\t  RestartInterval=15min, ExecutionTimeLimit=1h, Priority=7,\n16\t  Principal=john / LogonType=S4U / RunLevel=Limited.\n17\t\n18\t  Also pins Windows Update:\n19\t    HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\WindowsUpdate\\UX\\Settings\n20\t        ActiveHoursStart = 4,  ActiveHoursEnd = 22,  IsActiveHoursEnabled = 1\n21\t    HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\WindowsUpdate\\AU\n22\t        ScheduledInstallTime = 3\n23\t\n24\t  S4U conversion (run-when-logged-off) was applied live by Bucket K3; this\n25\t  script now matches that reality with LogonType=S4U (was Interactive). S4U\n26\t  needs no stored password -- the task runs as $User without the credential\n27\t  prompt that a Password logon type would trigger.\n28\t\n29\t  Wave B5 (2026-05-29): model_smoke_tests writer.\n30\t  -----------------------------------------------\n31\t  The nightly smoke tests against the model catalog run as PART OF the\n32\t  Aurora-Models task above (orchestrator hook in walk_models_pipeline);\n33\t  there is NO new scheduled task. The writer is DEFAULT-OFF -- the curator\n34\t  opts in once they've reviewed cost behavior over a few nights:\n35\t\n36\t    setx AURORA_SMOKE_TESTS_ENABLED 1            # turn the writer on\n37\t    setx AURORA_SMOKE_TEST_CAP_USD 0.10          # cumulative USD cap / run\n38\t    setx AURORA_SMOKE_TEST_TIMEOUT_S 30          # per-call HTTP timeout\n39\t    setx AURORA_SMOKE_TESTS_DIRECT 1             # OPTIONAL: prefer direct\n40\t                                                 # provider keys over OpenRouter\n41\t\n42\t  Required keys for the default (OpenRouter) route: OPENROUTER_API_KEY.\n43\t  Direct-route fallbacks (when AURORA_SMOKE_TESTS_DIRECT=1): OPENAI_API_KEY,\n44\t  XAI_API_KEY, MISTRAL_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, GEMINI_API_KEY.\n45\t\n46\t  Manual / ad-hoc invocation (does NOT need the scheduled task):\n47\t    .\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -m aurora.roles.model_smoke_tester `\n48\t        --cap-usd 0.10 --limit 20 --force --only-provider anthropic,google\n49\t\n50\t.NOTES\n51\t  Re-running is safe: tasks are updated in place, registry writes are conditional.\n52\t  HKLM writes require admin elevation. If unelevated, the script reports what\n53\t  needs an admin pass and exits non-zero.\n54\t\n55\t.EXAMPLE\n56\t  # From an elevated PowerShell window:\n57\t  powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File C:\\dev\\aurora\\bin\\setup-tasks.ps1\n58\t\n59\t  # From a non-elevated shell (will skip registry, configure tasks only):\n60\t  powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File C:\\dev\\aurora\\bin\\setup-tasks.ps1\n61\t#>\n62\t[CmdletBinding()]\n63\tparam(\n64\t    [string]$AuroraRoot = \"C:\\dev\\aurora\",\n65\t    [string]$User = \"john\"\n66\t)\n67\t\n68\t$ErrorActionPreference = \"Stop\"\n69\t\n70\t# ---- Task definitions (declarative -- single source of truth) ----\n71\t# Mode: \"Daily\" (Time field is HH:mm local) or \"Hourly\" (Time field is\n72\t# minutes-past-the-hour, e.g. \"30\" means :30 of every hour).\n73\t$TASKS = @(\n74\t    # Bucket M-1 (v4.4, 2026-05-22): Staggered, odd-offset schedule to dodge API congestion.\n75\t    # We move the main sweeps into the early morning hours (01:00-06:00 local).\n76\t    @{ Name = \"Aurora-Agents\";            Mode = \"Daily\";  Time = \"01:07\"; Cmd = \"$AuroraRoot\\bin\\run-agents.cmd\" },\n77\t    @{ Name = \"Aurora-Skills\";            Mode = \"Daily\";  Time = \"02:19\"; Cmd = \"$AuroraRoot\\bin\\run-skills.cmd\" },\n78\t    @{ Name = \"Aurora-Tools\";             Mode = \"Daily\";  Time = \"03:41\"; Cmd = \"$AuroraRoot\\bin\\run-tools.cmd\" },\n79\t    @{ Name = \"Aurora-Models\";            Mode = \"Daily\";  Time = \"05:03\"; Cmd = \"$AuroraRoot\\bin\\run-models.cmd\" },\n80\t    @{ Name = \"Aurora-State-Reporter\";    Mode = \"Daily\";  Time = \"06:23\"; Cmd = \"$AuroraRoot\\bin\\run-state-reporter.cmd\" },\n81\t    @{ Name = \"Aurora-Morning-Briefing\";  Mode = \"Daily\";  Time = \"06:47\"; Cmd = \"$AuroraRoot\\bin\\run-morning-briefing.cmd\" },\n82\t    @{ Name = \"Aurora-Source-Push\";       Mode = \"Hourly\"; Time = \"47\";    Cmd = \"$AuroraRoot\\bin\\run-aurora-source-push.cmd\" }\n83\t)\n84\t\n85\t# Wave 3 (2026-06-10): two WEEKLY tasks. Same idempotent registration +\n86\t# WakeToRun/S4U/RestartCount=2 settings as the daily/hourly tasks above\n87\t# (Ensure-Task is the single registration path). Scheduled in the early-morning\n88\t# quiet band, AFTER the nightly sweeps + briefing finish (last sweep 05:03,\n89\t# briefing 06:47) so the link-health probe reads a freshly-written catalog and\n90\t# the digest reads the freshly-probed stars:\n91\t#   - Aurora-Link-Health:   Sundays 06:55 — probes active GitHub-linked\n92\t#                           artifacts; writes stargazers/staleness into the\n93\t#                           link_health satellite (idempotent: 7-day skip).\n94\t#   - Aurora-Weekly-Digest: Sundays 07:10 — runs 15 min AFTER the probe so the\n95\t#                           digest's notability signal reflects the same-day\n96\t#                           star readings.\n97\t$WEEKLY_TASKS = @(\n98\t    @{ Name = \"Aurora-Link-Health\";   Mode = \"Weekly\"; Time = \"Sunday 06:55\"; Cmd = \"$AuroraRoot\\bin\\run-link-health.cmd\" },\n99\t    @{ Name = \"Aurora-Weekly-Digest\"; Mode = \"Weekly\"; Time = \"Sunday 07:10\"; Cmd = \"$AuroraRoot\\bin\\run-weekly-digest.cmd\" }\n100\t)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01ACwxJodXAE6No2Hnb7B6TY","session_id":"a7fcfbf6-6e6f-495e-9c53-2f0602be6ffe","uuid":"f3b77242-37a1-4dfb-a972-2fececd1426b","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:01:35.902Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Map Aurora architecture & code"}
