{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018cmQZtNfrTATP8akbEYVJJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Build the helping-hand plugin in TWO flavors.\n2\t\n3\tBucket H1+H3 (v4.3, 2026-05-19). Promoted from `_build_plugin.py` per Bucket J #1.\n4\t\n5\tOutputs (both at C:\\\\dev\\\\aurora\\\\):\n6\t\n7\t  - helping-hand.plugin\n8\t      Curator flavor. plugin.json keeps the source-of-truth fields:\n9\t      hard-coded venv path, hard-coded args/cwd, AURORA_KB_MODE=read_write.\n10\t      Designed for John's local install at C:\\\\dev\\\\aurora.\n11\t\n12\t  - helping-hand-collab.plugin\n13\t      Portable flavor for collaborators. plugin.json is rewritten:\n14\t        - command: \"python\"            (from PATH; falls back to `py` via launcher)\n15\t        - args:    relative path to mcp-servers/aurora-kb/server.py\n16\t        - cwd:     omitted (defaults to plugin root)\n17\t        - env.AURORA_KB_PATH:  omitted (server.py:_discover_db_path probes)\n18\t        - env.AURORA_KB_MODE:  read_only\n19\t      Designed to install on any collaborator's machine that has python\n20\t      and the `mcp` package available.\n21\t\n22\tBoth flavors:\n23\t  - Exclude __pycache__/ recursively.\n24\t  - Strip UTF-8 BOM from any .json / .md / .toml / .yaml / .yml / .txt file\n25\t    before packing (Cowork's installer chokes on the leading U+FEFF that\n26\t    PowerShell's `Set-Content -Encoding UTF8` adds — see NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md\n27\t    Bucket B #5 for the debug story).\n28\t  - Get the H3 `contextCost` annotation inside their mcpServers entry,\n29\t    documenting expected I/O cost per call to surface in the Cowork\n30\t    marketplace UI.\n31\t  - Are verified post-build: plugin.json must start with `{` after packing.\n32\t\n33\tUsage:\n34\t    python C:\\\\dev\\\\aurora\\\\bin\\\\build-plugin.py [--curator-only | --collab-only]\n35\t\n36\tReturns exit code 0 on success, non-zero on validation failure.\n37\t\"\"\"\n38\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n39\timport argparse\n40\timport copy\n41\timport io\n42\timport json\n43\timport os\n44\timport sys\n45\timport zipfile\n46\tfrom pathlib import Path\n47\t\n48\tROOT = Path(r\"C:\\dev\\aurora\")\n49\tSRC = ROOT / \"helping-hand-plugin\"\n50\tCURATOR_OUT = ROOT / \"helping-hand.plugin\"\n51\tCOLLAB_OUT = ROOT / \"helping-hand-collab.plugin\"\n52\tPLUGIN_JSON_REL = \".claude-plugin/plugin.json\"\n53\t\n54\tBOM = b\"\\xef\\xbb\\xbf\"\n55\tSTRIP_EXTS = {\".json\", \".md\", \".toml\", \".yaml\", \".yml\", \".txt\"}\n56\t\n57\t# H3: per-call cost annotation (May 2026 Cowork marketplace convention).\n58\tCONTEXT_COST = {\n59\t    \"tokens_in_per_call\": 50,\n60\t    \"tokens_out_per_call\": 200,\n61\t    \"notes\": (\n62\t        \"Per kb.match_request / kb.recent_summary / kb.fetch_artifact call. \"\n63\t        \"Small JSON I/O; no LLM tokens spent unless Helping Hand actually loads \"\n64\t        \"a proposed skill (which is gated by user accept).\"\n65\t    ),\n66\t}\n67\t\n68\t\n69\tdef _load_source_manifest() -> dict:\n70\t    raw = (SRC / PLUGIN_JSON_REL).read_bytes()\n71\t    if raw.startswith(BOM):\n72\t        raw = raw[3:]\n73\t    return json.loads(raw.decode(\"utf-8\"))\n74\t\n75\t\n76\tdef _annotate_context_cost(manifest: dict) -> dict:\n77\t    \"\"\"Attach contextCost to each mcpServers entry, in-place safely (returns the\n78\t    same dict for chaining).\"\"\"\n79\t    for name, entry in (manifest.get(\"mcpServers\") or {}).items():\n80\t        entry.setdefault(\"contextCost\", CONTEXT_COST)\n81\t    return manifest\n82\t\n83\t\n84\tdef _make_collab_manifest(curator: dict) -> dict:\n85\t    \"\"\"Rewrite the curator manifest into the portable / collaborator flavor.\"\"\"\n86\t    m = copy.deepcopy(curator)\n87\t    aurora = (m.get(\"mcpServers\") or {}).get(\"aurora-kb\")\n88\t    if not aurora:\n89\t        raise RuntimeError(\"source plugin.json missing mcpServers.aurora-kb entry\")\n90\t    aurora[\"command\"] = \"python\"\n91\t    aurora[\"args\"] = [\"mcp-servers/aurora-kb/server.py\"]\n92\t    aurora.pop(\"cwd\", None)\n93\t    env = aurora.setdefault(\"env\", {})\n94\t    env.pop(\"AURORA_KB_PATH\", None)            # let _discover_db_path probe\n95\t    env[\"AURORA_KB_MODE\"] = \"read_only\"        # safe default for non-curator\n96\t    # H3 cost block (also applied to curator below)\n97\t    aurora[\"contextCost\"] = CONTEXT_COST\n98\t    # Mark provenance so future debugging can tell which flavor an install is\n99\t    m[\"_flavor\"] = \"collab\"\n100\t    return m"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01ACwxJodXAE6No2Hnb7B6TY","session_id":"a7fcfbf6-6e6f-495e-9c53-2f0602be6ffe","uuid":"edeb7ceb-101b-45bb-82b2-de6939ef13c2","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:01:36.369Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Map Aurora architecture & code"}
