{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012tJdPKibHKSncX9Zytjy2M","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Crucible Stage 1 — Master Plan: Aurora Awareness Revamp\n2\t\n3\t**Run:** 2026-06-11. **Status:** post Shark-Tank round 1 (converged; 3 BLOCKERs + 2 Judge-elevated findings resolved into the plan). **Awaiting your approval.**\n4\t**North Star:** LOCKED at Stage 0 (NS1 awareness · NS2 model+benchmark intelligence · NS3 adoption decision · NS4 right collection · NS5 honest value).\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## What the Shark Tank changed (so you can see the plan earned its shape)\n9\t1. **Resequenced** — collection fix moved ahead of the \"what moved\" awareness view; only the already-collected **model surface** precedes it. (Awareness of a feed showing 0 new finds isn't awareness.)\n10\t2. **Adoption shrunk** — no Helping-Hand decision plumbing built on n=7. Instead a **label-capture** mechanism starts early and an honest **decision log**; full adoption automation is gated behind n≥30 real labels.\n11\t3. **Delivery contract defined** — the **morning report + weekly email is the product**; the dashboard is the drill-down. Every wave states what renders where.\n12\t4. **Publisher safety is a cross-cutting hard rule** — new tables do NOT auto-publish; license/ToS-restricted cells are filtered from the nightly `aurora-library` push.\n13\t5. **Map deferred** (recommendation — your call at this gate; see §Decision-for-you).\n14\t\n15\t---\n16\t\n17\t## Cross-cutting hard rules (apply to EVERY wave — non-negotiable, from constraints + Shark findings)\n18\t- **CC1 — Publisher disposition.** Every new/changed table declares one of {scrub / publish-clean / publish-with-license-filter} and it is **tested in `publisher --dry-run`** before the wave is done. The snapshot SELECT must drop any cell whose `license` is null/unknown or whose `source` is OpenRouter-derived (ToS). Default-publish is treated as a defect.\n19\t- **CC2 — Live-pipeline safety.** Any change to the collection/ingestion path lands behind a **shadow/dry-run** (write to `*_shadow` or a fixture KB, no production writes, cost-capped, OFF the 01:07–06:47 cron) and is promoted only after the shadow diff is reviewed. Reuse `roles/shadow_diff.py` + the `validations_shadow` pattern.\n20\t- **CC3 — Honest-n.** No metric/ranking rate is shown below **n<30**; show raw counts + the window + sample size; name the open-loop state. Current adoption ground truth = n=7.\n21\t- **CC4 — Read-only KB** except the new `decisions` / `feedback` / benchmark-score tables. Never read `.env`. Never run the `migrate_to_kind_paper` delete step.\n22\t- **CC5 — Provenance at write time.** Benchmark/model-derived cells carry NOT-NULL `source` + `license` + `as_of` + `self_reported`; a null license is a write-time reject.\n23\t- **CC6 — Report-first delivery.** Each wave's user-facing value ships as **report/email content first**; dashboard surfaces are the optional drill-down, never the sole home of a North-Star deliverable.\n24\t- **CC7 — Reuse, don't rebuild.** Evolve the existing `dashboard/` package + `kb/aurora.db` schema. No rebuild.\n25\t\n26\t---\n27\t\n28\t## The phased plan (each wave independently shippable; ordered by value-per-effort × North-Star urgency)\n29\t\n30\t### Wave 1 — Model intelligence from data we already own  *(NS1, NS2)*\n31\tThe highest value-per-effort move: 352 priced rows already collected, currently invisible.\n32\t- Semantic + sentinel **junk-filter** (sentinels `-1000000`/`$0` AND stale/deprecated/preview rows); report post-filter per-category counts.\n33\t- **Sortable/filterable master table** (provider/family/version, price in/out, context, max-out, modalities, reasoning_mode, tool_use, license_class, cutoff, released_at).\n34\t- **Intelligence-vs-cost / price-performance frontier** as a static SVG (price-only axis until Wave 3 adds benchmarks).\n35\t- Delivery: a **\"Models\" report section + weekly-email model-delta block**; the full table/frontier live on the dashboard as drill-down.\n36\t- *Deferred to Wave 3:* \"best-for-X\" cards + any composite (benchmark-gated — must not ship on price alone).\n37\t- **Cross-cutting seed:** add the lightweight **label-capture hook** (👍/👎 on report items) here so labels start accruing immediately toward CC3's n≥30.\n38\t\n39\t### Wave 2 — Fix the collection engine  *(NS4 — the existential \"are we collecting the right thing\")*\n40\t- Add high-signal agentic sources: **HF Daily Papers**, **GitHub** new-repos by **star-velocity** (`topic:ai-agents/llm-agent/agent-framework`), **provider release feeds** (OpenAI/Anthropic/HF + trackers), **trusted-aggregator** mentions (Smol AINews / Latent Space) as a signal.\n41\t- **Keep a narrow raw-arxiv recall safety net** (specific cs.AI/cs.MA + keyword) — do NOT cut arxiv to zero.\n42\t- **`frontier_score` ranker** with an **authority-bypass lane** (strong code-linkage + benchmark-presence + recency bypasses the provider-authority requirement) so the obscure small-author find still surfaces.\n43\t- **Weights ship hand-set + flagged UNVALIDATED** (CC3 — no n≥30 labels yet); a later weight-validation step is gated on the labels Wave 1/Wave 5 accrue.\n44\t- Built entirely behind **CC2 shadow/dry-run**; promoted to cron only after a clean shadow diff.\n45\t\n46\t### Wave 3 — Benchmark thin-slice + decision-grade model view  *(NS2)*\n47\t- Ingest **OpenRouter `/models`** (specs/pricing, transient-enrich per CC1 — never redistributed) + **Epoch AI CC-BY** (GPQA Diamond / SWE-bench Verified / FrontierMath / MATH-L5 / AIME) into `model_benchmarks` with CC5 provenance.\n48\t- **Sparse-aware composite:** compute a transparent composite ONLY where component coverage exists; **show coverage/missing explicitly** (no false-authority score over missing cells); never present a single black-box index.\n49\t- Join into Wave 1's surface → unlock **\"best-for-X\" cards** (best coding / agentic / cheap-good / long-context / open-weights), each justified by the score + provenance + `as_of` staleness badge.\n50\t- Publisher: benchmark cells pass CC1's license filter (CC-BY publishes with attribution; Apache-2.0 rows tagged; OpenRouter-derived specs scrubbed from the push).\n51\t\n52\t### Wave 4 — Awareness + honest value, in the report  *(NS1, NS5)*\n53\tNow meaningful because collection is fixed (W2) and benchmarks exist (W3).\n54\t- **Per-category \"what moved + why it matters\"** momentum (promote existing sweep deltas) — skills/tools/templates/agents/models, each with an opinionated one-line \"why it matters,\" hard top-N cap, fade-after-N-nights.\n55\t- **Plain-English value+health**: RAG (red/amber/green) + the **4 questions** — *Is it working? / Is it worth it? / What's wrong? / What to think about?* — value-first, zero JSON. Metric set: useful-find rate (OMTM), cost-per-useful-find, precision, frontier-coverage, decisions-influenced, spend-vs-budget — **all CC3 n-gated**.\n56\t- Delivery: replaces the unreadable health page's role **inside the morning report + weekly email**; dashboard keeps a human-readable health panel as drill-down.\n57\t\n58\t### Wave 5 — Adoption decision (minimal, honest, label-building)  *(NS3 — deliberately small)*\n59\t- **Decision content in the report**: for top candidates, the card fields (what-it-is / fit / recommendation+confidence / advantages / risks / provenance / effort) rendered as report items — **recommendation is a non-authoritative suggestion, never a consensus verdict**.\n60\t- **`decisions` table** (CC1 disposition declared + dry-run tested) records accept/decline/snooze; this **doubles as the label source** feeding Wave 2's deferred weight-validation.\n61\t- **No Helping-Hand auto-plumbing yet** — when accepted-decisions cross n≥30, a follow-up (future run) wires accepts into Helping Hand and validates `frontier_score` weights. Stated explicitly as a future gate, not built now.\n62\t\n63\t### Wave 6 (DEFERRED — recommend OUT of this run) — Knowledge/relationship map\n64\tRecommendation: **defer to a later run.** Rationale: the validated research judged it the least decision-useful build and the same *class* of artifact you rejected (unsupervised projection), and John lives in the report, not a canvas. If kept, it is PCA/TruncatedSVD + plain `<canvas>`, non-authoritative, with UMAP/numba proven absent from the ingestion path (CC2). **This is a gate decision for you (§Decision-for-you).**\n65\t\n66\t---\n67\t\n68\t## How each wave serves the North Star (inclusion test)\n69\t| Wave | NS1 | NS2 | NS3 | NS4 | NS5 |\n70\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n71\t| W1 Model surface | ✓ | ✓ | | | |\n72\t| W2 Collection fix | ✓ | | | ✓ | |\n73\t| W3 Benchmarks | ✓ | ✓ | ✓(fit) | | |\n74\t| W4 Awareness+value | ✓ | | | | ✓ |\n75\t| W5 Adoption(min) | | | ✓ | (labels→NS4) | |\n76\t| W6 Map (deferred) | (weak) | | | | |\n77\t\n78\tEvery retained wave serves ≥1 criterion; W6 is the only weak server → deferred.\n79\t\n80\t---\n81\t\n82\t## 🚦 Stage 1 APPROVAL GATE — Decision-for-you\n83\t1. **Approve the resequenced 5-wave plan** (W1 model surface → W2 collection fix → W3 benchmarks → W4 awareness+value → W5 minimal adoption)? (yes / edit)\n84\t2. **The map (W6):** you locked it IN-but-optional at Stage 0; the Shark Tank recommends **deferring it out of this run**. Confirm **defer**, or **keep it IN** as a fenced optional final wave? (defer / keep)\n85\t3. **The adoption shrink:** OK that we do NOT build Helping-Hand auto-adoption now, and instead capture labels + log decisions until n≥30, then revisit in a future run? (yes / want more now)\n86\t4. Anything to reweight in the wave order, or any cross-cutting rule to add?\n87\t\n88\tOn approval, Stage 2 decomposes each wave into per-wave acceptance criteria (done-when + Given/When/Then), runs a second Shark-Tank pass on the implementation detail, clears Foreman's `locate-plan.mjs` well-formedness gate, and emits the doc-trio + `foreman.config.json` into `docs/foreman-handoff-awareness/`.\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RiqtGSRiHPW8WJeLKyY94p","session_id":"a7fcfbf6-6e6f-495e-9c53-2f0602be6ffe","uuid":"66a9b964-9553-43d0-a465-ccf21af87b50","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:01:44.366Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Map Aurora plans & strategy"}
