{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XcR992Z4WjrQNuxcCHzEW8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora — John's interest (taste) profile\n2\t\n3\t**Version:** 1\n4\t**Last edited by:** Aurora Wave 4 (seed) — 2026-06-10\n5\t**Owner thereafter:** John (this file is John-edited; the scorer only READS it).\n6\t\n7\t> This is the rubric `roles/taste.py` scores every find against to produce\n8\t> `artifacts.interest_score` (0..1) + `artifacts.interest_why`. The taste score\n9\t> drives what surfaces first in the morning briefing and the weekly digest.\n10\t> Edit this file to change what Aurora considers interesting — no code change is\n11\t> needed; the scorer reads the current text on every run. Bump the **Version**\n12\t> when you make a substantive edit so a future scored-against-which-profile audit\n13\t> is possible.\n14\t\n15\t## North star\n16\t\n17\tEverything Aurora surfaces should be **correctly classified, genuinely\n18\tinteresting, and worth John's attention** — a smaller, high-trust catalog over a\n19\tbig noisy one. Score interestingness as: *would John actually want to see this\n20\tnear the top of tomorrow's briefing?*\n21\t\n22\t## What scores HIGH (interesting)\n23\t\n24\t- **The Claude / agent ecosystem.** Skills, agents, tools, templates, and MCP\n25\t  servers that plug into Claude Code / Cowork / OpenClaw or the broader\n26\t  Anthropic agent stack. The closer to John's actual tooling, the higher.\n27\t- **Usable over academic.** A runnable, installable, GitHub-hosted artifact John\n28\t  could adopt this week beats a write-up, a survey, or a \"look what's possible\"\n29\t  demo. Papers are an opt-in stream, NOT a top-find (they have their own digest\n30\t  section) — never let a paper outrank a usable artifact here.\n31\t- **Novelty over volume.** A genuinely new capability, pattern, or approach beats\n32\t  the Nth variation on something Aurora already catalogs. Reward the thing that\n33\t  does something Aurora hasn't seen before; discount yet-another-wrapper.\n34\t- **Evidence of quality.** A confidence badge (verified > documented > lossy),\n35\t  real adoption (GitHub stars), and a clear, honest description that matches what\n36\t  the artifact does. A well-documented small tool beats a vague ambitious one.\n37\t- **Multi-agent / orchestration / evaluation craft.** Things that improve how\n38\t  agents are built, validated, scored, or coordinated — Aurora's own problem\n39\t  domain — are especially interesting.\n40\t\n41\t## What scores LOW (noise)\n42\t\n43\t- Vendor marketing, blog posts, and aggregator/\"awesome-list\" pointer entries —\n44\t  these should already be filtered upstream, but if one reaches the scorer, it is\n45\t  low-interest.\n46\t- Self-references / local-only artifacts (`local:` URLs) — never interesting.\n47\t- Duplicates and near-duplicates of already-cataloged artifacts.\n48\t- Models and raw papers as *top finds* (models are a reference table; papers go\n49\t  to the digest's papers section).\n50\t- Vague, undocumented, or quality-signal-free artifacts with no adoption and no\n51\t  badge — low trust, low interest.\n52\t\n53\t## Scoring guidance for the scorer\n54\t\n55\t- Output a single `interest_score` in `[0, 1]` and a one-line `interest_why`\n56\t  (<= ~160 chars) naming the concrete reason (e.g. \"usable Claude MCP server,\n57\t  documented badge, 1.2k★\" or \"narrow wrapper, no adoption signal\").\n58\t- Weight: ecosystem fit + usability first; then novelty; then quality/adoption\n59\t  evidence. A confidence badge and real stars should nudge the score up; their\n60\t  absence is not disqualifying but caps the ceiling.\n61\t- Be honest and calibrated — most finds are middling (0.3–0.6). Reserve > 0.8 for\n62\t  things John would genuinely want at the top of the briefing; reserve < 0.2 for\n63\t  noise that slipped through the upstream gates.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RiqtGSRiHPW8WJeLKyY94p","session_id":"a7fcfbf6-6e6f-495e-9c53-2f0602be6ffe","uuid":"538f65be-dfb7-4910-99d8-a5e4567315eb","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:01:47.723Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Map Aurora plans & strategy"}
