{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RAjy6Pf4P3ux4fad4Z4KX7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Model-surface queries over the read-only KB (Awareness Revamp — Wave 1).\n2\t\n3\tThe 352 already-collected, fully-priced ``models`` satellite rows are the\n4\thighest value-per-effort surface to expose: the cost is already paid, the data\n5\tis currently invisible. This module is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for *which*\n6\tmodel rows are fit to show John — every model surface (the ``/api/catalog/models``\n7\troute, ``catalog.models_summary``, the price-performance SVG, and the briefing's\n8\t``_models_block``) filters through :data:`USABLE_MODEL_PREDICATE`. There is never\n9\ta second, hand-inlined copy of the filter (CC7 reuse; the \"sentinel-as-cheapest\n10\tmodel\" trap is closed in exactly one place).\n11\t\n12\tThe junk we exclude (verified against the live KB 2026-06-12 — 352 rows total,\n13\t321 usable):\n14\t  * **price sentinels** — ``price_in_usd_per_mtok IS NULL OR <= 0`` covers both\n15\t    the ``-1000000`` \"unknown\" sentinel (3 rows) and the ``$0`` rows (27 rows).\n16\t    A ``$0`` price would otherwise masquerade as \"the cheapest model\".\n17\t  * **preview** — ``is_preview = 1`` (1 row): not a stable, adoptable model.\n18\t  * **past-deprecation** — keep only rows whose ``deprecation_date`` is null or\n19\t    today-or-later (0 rows live, but the guard must hold as deprecations land).\n20\t\n21\t**Staleness is DEFERRED in Wave 1 (intentionally).** The plan mentions filtering\n22\ton a stale ``last_metadata_verified_at`` but specifies NO threshold. Inventing a\n23\tcutoff here would silently drop *usable* rows and hurt awareness/recall — the\n24\tNorth-Star drift guard. So Wave 1 adds NO staleness clause; it is deferred until\n25\ta concrete window is specified (then add it to this single predicate only).\n26\t\n27\tLicense is mostly unknown (346 of 352 rows have ``license_class IS NULL``). We\n28\tNEVER hide unknown-license rows; we bucket them as ``\"unknown\"`` so the\n29\tdistribution is honest.\n30\t\"\"\"\n31\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n32\t\n33\tfrom pathlib import Path\n34\t\n35\tfrom . import db\n36\t\n37\t# The 5 frontier components the sparse composite averages over. Kept in step with\n38\t# roles.benchmark_ingest.COMPOSITE_COMPONENTS (the canonical write-side list);\n39\t# duplicated here as a plain constant so the portable data layer never imports\n40\t# sweep code (`roles`) at module-load time — the actual composite math is reused\n41\t# from roles.benchmark_ingest via a lazy import inside composite_leaders().\n42\t_COMPOSITE_COMPONENTS = [\n43\t    \"gpqa-diamond\", \"swe-bench-verified\", \"frontiermath\", \"math-l5\", \"aime\",\n44\t]\n45\t\n46\t# Awareness Revamp W3: the benchmark slugs that justify the benchmark-dependent\n47\t# best-for-X cards. Kept in step with roles.benchmark_ingest.COMPOSITE_COMPONENTS.\n48\t_CODING_BENCH = \"swe-bench-verified\"\n49\t_AGENTIC_BENCH = \"gpqa-diamond\"\n50\t# Open-weights license_class values (the model surface buckets unknown as\n51\t# \"unknown\"; these are the values we treat as open).\n52\t_OPEN_LICENSE_CLASSES = {\"open\", \"open-weights\", \"apache-2.0\", \"mit\", \"permissive\"}\n53\t\n54\t# ── the single reusable junk-filter ──────────────────────────────────────────\n55\t# A SQL WHERE-fragment over the `models` table (alias-free: reference bare\n56\t# column names, so callers can use it on `models m` as long as the join doesn't\n57\t# ambiguate these columns — they are unique to `models`). Used by EVERY model\n58\t# surface; do not inline a second copy.\n59\t#\n60\t# NOTE (Wave 1, deferred): a staleness clause on `last_metadata_verified_at` is\n61\t# intentionally NOT included — see module docstring. When a window is specified,\n62\t# extend THIS constant only.\n63\tUSABLE_MODEL_PREDICATE = (\n64\t    \"(price_in_usd_per_mtok IS NOT NULL AND price_in_usd_per_mtok > 0) \"\n65\t    \"AND (is_preview IS NULL OR is_preview = 0) \"\n66\t    \"AND (deprecation_date IS NULL OR deprecation_date >= date('now'))\"\n67\t)\n68\t\n69\t# The master-table columns a model surface exposes (provider/family/version\n70\t# uniquely identify the model; the rest are the decision-relevant specs/pricing).\n71\tMODEL_COLUMNS = [\n72\t    \"provider\", \"family\", \"version\", \"price_in\", \"price_out\",\n73\t    \"context_in_tokens\", \"max_output_tokens\", \"modalities\", \"reasoning_mode\",\n74\t    \"tool_use\", \"license_class\", \"knowledge_cutoff\", \"released_at\",\n75\t]\n76\t\n77\t\n78\tdef usable_model_rows(kb_path: str | Path) -> list[dict]:\n79\t    \"\"\"Usable model rows joined to ``artifacts`` (non-retired), junk-filtered.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01ACwxJodXAE6No2Hnb7B6TY","session_id":"a7fcfbf6-6e6f-495e-9c53-2f0602be6ffe","uuid":"7b8f6ea1-ffc4-4900-869c-e87cdab4fdc9","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:01:50.197Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Map Aurora architecture & code"}
