{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KK4UHEw4wVVvpgwewh4qF9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Awareness Revamp — Execution Log\n2\t\n3\tThis log is written by Foreman as it executes the waves in `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md`. It starts empty.\n4\t\n5\t**Handoff status (2026-06-12):** Crucible Stage 0 (North Star locked) + Stage 1 (Master Plan,\n6\tuser-approved, map deferred) + Stage 2 (this doc-trio) complete. Research base:\n7\t`docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/RESEARCH.md` (adversarially validated). Not yet started by Foreman.\n8\t\n9\t| Wave | Status | Commit | Notes |\n10\t|---|---|---|---|\n11\t| 1 — Surface models we own | ✅ GREEN | (this commit) | 321/352 usable surfaced; report+dashboard+SVG; +13 tests |\n12\t| 2 — Re-aim collector (shadow) | ✅ GREEN | (this commit) | frontier_ranker + authority-bypass; shadow-only, CC2 airtight; +19 tests |\n13\t| 3 — Benchmark slice + decision view | ✅ GREEN | (this commit) | Epoch CC-BY ingester + CC1 scrub (both directions verified); +12 tests |\n14\t| 4 — Awareness + value/health | ✅ GREEN | (this commit) | momentum + 4-question RAG; §B-3 n-gated (terminal not surfaced); +16 tests |\n15\t| 5 — Minimal adoption (decisions) | ✅ GREEN | (this commit) | decisions table + capture; CC1 scrub + §B-2 non-authoritative; +17 tests |\n16\t\n17\t**PROJECT COMPLETE — all 5 waves GREEN (2026-06-12).** Test baseline 1076 →\n18\t**1152 passed** (+76 additive; the lone failing `test_no_stale_running_runs_from_\n19\tyesterday` is a pre-existing, unrelated live-DB stale-`runs` artifact present\n20\tbefore W1, left untouched per CC4).\n21\t\n22\t### ✅ RESOLVED 2026-06-13 — the \"live-DB migration breakage\" was a FALSE ALARM\n23\tThe Wave-3 ⚠ escalation (apply_migrations \"fails on the live DB with no such\n24\ttable: helping_hand_log\") was a **measurement error, not a real bug.** Root\n25\tcause: `kb/aurora.db` runs in **WAL journal mode**, and I diagnosed it by\n26\t`cp kb/aurora.db /tmp/...` — which copies ONLY the main file, omitting the\n27\t`-wal`, producing an INCONSISTENT snapshot missing recently-committed objects\n28\t(`helping_hand_log`, fresh `schema_version` rows). `apply_migrations` then failed\n29\ton that broken copy. The real DB, read coherently (a `mode=ro` sqlite connection\n30\tor the `.backup()` API, both of which merge WAL+main), was always healthy.\n31\t**Verified 2026-06-13:** (1) the overnight nightly sweep applied `0026/0027/0028`\n32\tcleanly — live `schema_version` now holds 26, 27, 28; `artifacts.frontier_score`,\n33\t`model_benchmarks.source/license`, and the `decisions` table all exist in\n34\tproduction. (2) On a CONSISTENT copy (sqlite `.backup()`), `apply_migrations` is a\n35\tclean no-op (`[]` twice) with NO helping_hand_log error. (3) No version\n36\tcollisions — 26/27/28 are declared only by my three files; the migration version\n37\tnumbers are scrambled vs filename prefixes (e.g. `0001_hh_telemetry.sql` →\n38\tv32), and 1/2/29/30 are simply unused target numbers (benign). **Nothing to\n39\trepair. All W2–W5 schema is live.** Remaining activation is DATA, not schema:\n40\t`model_benchmarks` is empty until the Epoch ingester is run (then best-for-X\n41\tcards + composite light up); `decisions` accrue as the 👍/👎 control is used; the\n42\tfrontier ranker stays shadow-only by design until n≥30 labels.\n43\t\n44\t**Lesson (do not repeat):** never diagnose a WAL-mode SQLite DB by copying just\n45\tthe `.db` file. Use a `mode=ro` connection or `sqlite3 .backup()` for a coherent\n46\tsnapshot.\n47\t\n48\t---\n49\t\n50\t## Wave 5 — Minimal, honest adoption (decisions + labels) — GREEN (2026-06-12)\n51\t\n52\tEXECUTE → orchestrator-run gate → 2 reviewers (I = CC1/§B-2/anti-test-weakening;\n53\tJ = capture correctness + production-safety; **both GO**) → 1 bounded hardening\n54\tFIX → re-gate. **Gate: 1135 → 1152 passed** (+17 additive; same 1 pre-existing\n55\tunrelated `runs` failure). Deliberately small (n=7 forbids automation; NO\n56\tHelping-Hand auto-adoption — that's a FUTURE gate at n≥30).\n57\t\n58\t**Delivered:** migration `0028_decisions.sql` — `decisions(id, artifact_id FK,\n59\tdecision_type CHECK IN ('adopt','defer','reject','retire'), reason,\n60\texplicit_label, explicit_confidence, made_at, made_by_session_id, recorded_at)` +\n61\tindexes (idempotent; schema.sql mirrored). `/api/decisions/record` upgraded from\n62\tthe W1 graceful stub to a real insert (resolve slug→artifact_id, 👍→adopt /\n63\t👎→reject, validates decision_type in Python before insert so a bad type returns\n64\t200 `{ok:false}` not a 500; still 200 `{ok:false}` when the table is absent —\n65\tthe live state). `bin/record-decision.py` CLI for offline logging.\n66\t`_decisions_block` renders decision cards (what-it-is / fit / advantages / risks /\n67\tprovenance / effort) with a **non-authoritative \"model suggests: trial/assess\"**\n68\trecommendation — confidence caps at \"medium\" even at high interest_score; header\n69\t\"(suggestions — not verdicts)\"; NO authoritative ADOPT/consensus ring can render\n70\t(§B-2). Honest \"Decisions logged this week: N (need ≥30 to validate the ranker)\"\n71\tcounter (CC3): N raw, no rate below the floor; distinguishes present-empty\n72\t(\"0, need ≥30\") from table-absent (\"capture not yet provisioned\").\n73\t\n74\t**CC1 — decisions NEVER published (load-bearing):** `publisher.py` SCRUB adds\n75\t`DROP TABLE IF EXISTS decisions` before VACUUM (private adoption labels). Reviewer\n76\tI built a real snapshot with a seeded private-marker decision and confirmed the\n77\ttable AND the marker BYTES are absent from the post-VACUUM snapshot\n78\t(`secure_delete=ON`). Regression-locked in `test_snapshot_scrub.py` +\n79\t`test_decisions.py`.\n80\t\n81\t**Anti-test-weakening (Foreman §5) — cleared.** W5 added `decisions` to\n82\tschema.sql, so `build_kb` now creates it, which would have broken 4 W4-era\n83\t\"table-absent\" graceful-degrade tests. They were reconciled by ADDING\n84\t`DROP TABLE IF EXISTS decisions` to reproduce the live (migration-blocked)\n85\ttable-absent state — **no assertion removed/loosened** (orchestrator-diffed +\n86\tReviewer-I-verified line by line); total count rose 1135→1152, no skip/xfail.\n87\t\n88\t**FIX (review NITs, proportionate hardening for the unattended 06:47 job):**\n89\twrapped `_decisions_counter` in the same try/except guard as `_decisions_block`\n90\t(neither can crash the briefing; `None` is rendered-safe downstream) and pinned\n91\tthe present-but-empty counter path with a regression test.\n92\t\n93\t**No server.py / plugin change** (records via the dashboard endpoint, not the\n94\tMCP) — no plugin rebuild. KB writes scoped to the `decisions` table only (CC4).\n95\t\n96\t## Wave 4 — Awareness \"what moved\" + plain-English value/health — GREEN (2026-06-12)\n97\t\n98\tEXECUTE → orchestrator-run gate → 2 reviewers (G = CC3/§B-3 metric honesty; H =\n99\tCC6 report-first / no-JSON / crash-safety; **both GO**) → 1 bounded test-hardening\n100\tFIX → re-gate. **Gate: 1120 → 1135 passed** (+16 additive incl. the W3 carryover\n101\ttest below; same 1 pre-existing unrelated `runs` failure, untouched). No\n102\tmigration (0028 reserved for W5); KB read-only.\n103\t\n104\t**CC3/§B-3 (the load-bearing rule) — the surfaced-denominator vanity dodge is\n105\tprovably closed.** `morning_briefing.py::_awareness_metrics` gates useful-find\n106\trate / precision / cost-per-find on **terminal decisions (loaded+dismissed = 7\n107\tlive)**, NOT on surfaced (98). Reviewer G ran the discriminating case\n108\t(surfaced=50 ≥ floor, terminal=7) and the rate stayed suppressed; I added that\n109\texact case as a regression test (`test_rate_gates_on_terminal_decisions_not_\n110\tsurfaced`) so it can't silently regress to surfaced-gating. Every n<30 metric\n111\tsuppresses its rate and shows raw counts + window + sample_size + names the\n112\topen-loop state; floor `AWARENESS_N_FLOOR=30`.\n113\t\n114\t**Delivered:** `_momentum_block` (per-category \"what moved + why it matters\" over\n115\tskills/templates/tools/agents/models; `MOMENTUM_TOP_N=5` hard cap;\n116\t`MOMENTUM_FADE_NIGHTS=3`; \"why\" sourced from `artifacts.interest_why`, kind-\n117\ttemplate fallback). `_value_health_block` (plain-English **RAG + 4 questions** —\n118\tworking? worth it? what's wrong? what to think about? — value-first, zero JSON;\n119\tgreen is structurally unreachable while any signal is open-loop, so the live RAG\n120\tis honestly **AMBER**; \"what to think about\" frames suggestions as\n121\tnon-authoritative per §B-2). Metric set (useful-find rate/OMTM, cost-per-useful-\n122\tfind, precision, frontier-coverage, decisions-influenced, spend-vs-budget) all\n123\tn-gated; frontier-coverage (NULL on live) + decisions-influenced (table absent)\n124\tdegrade to honest \"pending Wave 2/5\", never a fake 0%. New dashboard\n125\t`/api/health/summary` (`{ok, alerts, signals}`, try/except → always 200 on the\n126\tlive KB) with `/api/health/detail` as drill-down. Momentum + value/health ship\n127\tin the morning report AND `build_weekly_note` (CC6 report-first), not\n128\tdashboard-only. Reviewers confirmed zero JSON leaks into John's rendered note.\n129\t\n130\t**Carryover fix:** the W3 BLOCKER-fix regression test (`/api/catalog/models/best`\n131\treturns 200 on a pre-0027 column shape, `_build_models_kb_pre0027`) had been\n132\tadded to `tests/test_dashboard_web.py` but was left UNCOMMITTED by the W3 commit\n133\t(I staged W3 by explicit path and omitted that file). Committed here with W4 so\n134\tthe W3 BLOCKER fix has its committed regression proof. (Process note: stage test\n135\tfiles added by FIX agents, not just the planned set.)\n136\t\n137\t## Wave 3 — Benchmark thin-slice + decision-grade model view — GREEN (2026-06-12)\n138\t\n139\tEXECUTE → orchestrator-run gate → 2 reviewers (E = CC1/CC5 provenance: **GO**;\n140\tF = ingester/composite/cards: **NO-GO**, 1 BLOCKER + 1 MAJOR with a failing\n141\trepro) → FIX → re-gate → orchestrator re-verify. **Gate: 1108 → 1120 passed**\n142\t(+12 additive; same 1 pre-existing unrelated `runs` failure, untouched).\n143\t\n144\t**CC1 no-leak (load-bearing) — verified BOTH directions through the real\n145\tpublisher.** Migration `0027_benchmark_provenance.sql` adds `source`+`license` to\n146\t`model_benchmarks` (idempotent; schema.sql mirrored). A single insert chokepoint\n147\t`roles/benchmark_ingest.py::insert_benchmark` enforces CC5 (null `source`/\n148\t`license`/`artifact_id`/`observed_at`/`source_url` = write reject); AA writes\n149\t(`benchmark_scraper.py`) route through it tagged `source='artificial-analysis'`.\n150\tEpoch ingester (hermetic CSV, `pip epochai` fallback) writes GPQA-Diamond /\n151\tSWE-bench-Verified / FrontierMath / MATH-L5 / AIME as `source='epoch'`,\n152\t`license='CC-BY-4.0'` (Aider-Polyglot / Terminal-Bench → `Apache-2.0` per §B-6;\n153\t**MMLU-Pro deliberately NOT assumed** → skipped). OpenRouter enrichment\n154\t(`openrouter_enrich.py`) is off-by-default, tolerates 401, stores derived facts\n155\tonly, tags `source='openrouter'` (§B-5). Publisher scrub before VACUUM —\n156\t`DELETE FROM model_benchmarks WHERE license IS NULL OR license NOT IN\n157\t(ALLOWED_BENCHMARK_LICENSES) OR source IN (EXCLUDED_BENCHMARK_SOURCES)` (named\n158\tauditable constants; guarded on column presence). **Orchestrator built a real\n159\tsnapshot with 5 provenance cases: only Epoch CC-BY-4.0 + Apache-2.0 survive; AA,\n160\tOpenRouter, and null-license all scrubbed.** Sparse composite computes over\n161\tpresent components only, shows coverage k/5, never zero-fills missing.\n162\t\n163\t**FIX (Reviewer F BLOCKER + MAJOR, both orchestrator-confirmed):** (1) the\n164\t`/api/catalog/models/best` route **500'd on the live KB** because it guarded on\n165\ttable-presence but selected the 0027 `source` column, which is absent on the\n166\tlive DB — added a `db.has_column` guard + `_benchmarks_ready()` so benchmark\n167\tcards degrade to \"pending benchmark data\" (cheap-good/long-context/open-weights\n168\tstill render from price/context/license); route now returns **200** on the live\n169\tKB (orchestrator-verified). (2) `sparse_composite` was correct but **wired into\n170\tnothing** — surfaced it via a `composite` block in the best route + a coverage\n171\t\"k/5\" element in `models.js`. +5 regression tests cover both.\n172\t\n173\t**⚠ ESCALATION → ✅ RESOLVED 2026-06-13 (FALSE ALARM — see the \"RESOLVED\" block\n174\tat the top of this file).** This was a WAL-mode copy artifact, not a real bug;\n175\tthe overnight sweep applied 0026/0027/0028 cleanly and all W2–W5 schema is live.\n176\tThe original (now-superseded) note is kept below for the record:**\n177\t\n178\t**~~⚠ ESCALATION (pre-existing, blocks feature activation in production — NOT\n179\tcaused by this build):~~** `apply_migrations` **fails on the live `kb/aurora.db`**\n180\t(`OperationalError: no such table: helping_hand_log` — an ordering bug in an\n181\tolder migration), so migrations **0026 and 0027 are NOT applied to production**\n182\t(live `model_benchmarks` lacks `source`/`license`; `artifacts` lacks\n183\t`frontier_score`). The live `schema_version` is non-standard (has 3-25 + 31-35,\n184\tmissing 26-30). Every W2/W3 reader degrades gracefully (nothing crashes), but the\n185\tbenchmark + frontier features stay **dormant** until the migration chain is\n186\trepaired. **This needs John's decision** — repairing it touches the live\n187\tproduction DB and is out of a wave's safe scope. W1's model surface is unaffected\n188\t(it added no migration; the `models` table pre-exists). [tracked debt from W2 (b)\n189\t— the benchmark signal that lights up frontier recall — is downstream of this.]\n190\t\n191\t## Wave 2 — Re-aim the collector, behind a shadow — GREEN (2026-06-12)\n192\t\n193\tSame orchestrator loop: EXECUTE → orchestrator-run gate → 2 independent reviewers\n194\t(C = CC2 shadow-safety, D = ranker correctness/§B-1; **both GO**) → 1 bounded FIX\n195\t→ re-gate. **Gate: 1089 → 1108 passed** (+19 additive; same 1 pre-existing\n196\tunrelated `runs` failure, untouched).\n197\t\n198\t**CC2 (the load-bearing contract) — airtight, empirically proven.** Reviewer C\n199\tran the real nightly entry point with the new flag against the **live**\n200\t`kb/aurora.db` (`python -m aurora.orchestrator --sweep skills --retarget-shadow`)\n201\tand the DB's **SHA-256 + mtime were byte-for-byte unchanged**. The default\n202\t(no-flag) cron path returns *before* the `_run_retarget_shadow` branch is reached\n203\t(`orchestrator.py` early-return guard), so nightly behavior is unchanged; the new\n204\tsources live in `seed_map/shadow_retarget.yaml` (every seed `enabled:false` +\n205\t`shadow_only:true`, never read by the nightly seed loader); the shadow harness\n206\topens the live KB `mode=ro`; the only `ranking_diffs` writer targets a SEPARATE\n207\tshadow DB; nothing writes `artifacts.frontier_score` (stays NULL).\n208\t\n209\t**Delivered:** migration `0026_frontier_score.sql` (idempotent — double-apply via\n210\t`kb/migrate.py` is a clean no-op; adds `frontier_score` col + `ranking_diffs`\n211\ttable; schema_version 26; `schema.sql` mirrored for fresh builds);\n212\t`roles/frontier_ranker.py` — `frontier_score(artifact, signals)` with **§B-1\n213\tdown-weighted authority(0.15)+stars(0.10)** (provably can't clear the 0.45 gate\n214\talone: 0.40 < 0.45) and an **authority-bypass lane** (code+benchmark+recency ≥ 0.7\n215\tfloor) so a non-famous high-signal repo surfaces; weights ship `validated=False`\n216\t(CC3); a **promotion gate** that blocks demoting any real `loaded` artifact\n217\t(proven `eligible=False` on the 3 live `hh_events` loaded rows);\n218\t`bin/run_ranker_shadow.py` (read-only, `--date` deterministic, writes\n219\t`reports/ranker_shadow/<date>.jsonl`); a narrow **raw-arxiv recall net** retained\n220\tin the retarget set (§B-1 — demoted, not cut). CC1: `ranking_diffs` scrubbed in\n221\t`publisher.py` before VACUUM (regression-tested); `frontier_score` declared\n222\tpublish-clean (NULL). Nothing promoted to cron — promotion is a documented manual\n223\tstep.\n224\t\n225\t**FIX (Reviewer D MAJOR):** the headline authority-bypass test was *vacuous* —\n226\tall-signals=1.0 surfaces via the normal lane (0.60 ≥ gate) regardless of the\n227\tbypass, so the §B-1 guarantee could silently regress. Added a test in the\n228\tload-bearing **[0.42, 0.45) band** (signals at the 0.7 floor) asserting the item\n229\tsurfaces ONLY via the bypass, plus a just-under-floor control that must NOT\n230\tsurface. Re-gate green (19 ranker tests).\n231\t\n232\t**Tracked debt (non-blocking, recorded for later waves):** (a) the `ranker_shadow`\n233\tbudget cell is a dead constant in W2 because the shadow path makes ZERO LLM calls\n234\t(cost-capped vacuously) — must be wired before live fetches light up; (b)\n235\t`benchmark_presence` is proxied off a name keyword in the harness — the real\n236\tsignal lands in W3 when `model_benchmarks` is joined, so true recall on obscure\n237\tfinds is not \"solved tonight\"; (c) NITs: unused `cfg` param, cosmetic arxiv-kind\n238\tlog-count filter.\n239\t\n240\t## Wave 1 — Surface the models we already own — GREEN (2026-06-12)\n241\t\n242\tDriven as the Foreman orchestrator (manual, because the dirty production tree\n243\twould trip the Node engine's dirty-tree HALT and the commit must be path-scoped\n244\tto avoid sweeping nightly `library/`/`reports/` churn): EXECUTE (1 fresh-context\n245\tcoder) → orchestrator-run gate (`python -m pytest`, never sub-agent-pasted) → 2\n246\tindependent adversarial reviewers (both **GO**) → 1 bounded FIX → re-gate.\n247\t\n248\t**Gate (orchestrator-run, `.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -m pytest`):** baseline\n249\t**1076 passed**, after **1089 passed** (+13 additive). The 1 failing test\n250\t(`test_no_stale_running_runs_from_yesterday`) is a **pre-existing, unrelated**\n251\tlive-DB stale-`runs`-row artifact (row 134), present at baseline; CC4 makes\n252\t`runs` read-only so it was left untouched. No test weakened/skipped (count rose,\n253\tnone skipped) → no vacuous GREEN (new tests exercise the changed files).\n254\t\n255\t**Delivered (done-when + all 4 Given/When/Then satisfied, verified live):**\n256\t- `dashboard/data/models.py` — `USABLE_MODEL_PREDICATE` (single source of truth):\n257\t  excludes price sentinels (`<=0` covers `-1000000`+`$0`+`NULL`), `is_preview=1`,\n258\t  past-`deprecation_date`. **Live: 352 total → 321 usable, 0 junk leaking.**\n259\t  Staleness clause **deliberately deferred** (plan gave no threshold; filtering\n260\t  on an invented cutoff would drop usable rows → North-Star recall guard).\n261\t- `catalog.models_summary()` + routes `/api/catalog/models`,\n262\t  `/api/catalog/models/frontier.svg` (server-rendered, dependency-free,\n263\t  price-axis-only, labeled \"performance axis lands in Wave 3\"); `models.js`\n264\t  sortable/filterable master table (no JS charting dep, CC7).\n265\t- Report-first (CC6): `_models_block()` extended (usable counts +\n266\t  license_distribution, NULL→\"unknown\"); `\"models\"` key folded into `bridge_data`\n267\t  → `reports/morning/latest_summary.json`; `build_session_note()` renders a\n268\t  \"Models — {total} tracked\" headline (+ weekly model-delta block). Cross-package\n269\t  import of the predicate is guarded so an ImportError can't crash the 06:47\n270\t  briefing — and was empirically confirmed to resolve in the real prod path\n271\t  (`python -m aurora.morning_briefing`), so models DO appear (not silent-degrade).\n272\t- Label-capture seed: 👍/👎 on top-find items → `/api/decisions/record`, which\n273\t  graceful-degrades (HTTP 200 `{ok:false,…}`) when the `decisions` table is\n274\t  absent — no `decisions` table/migration added (that is Wave 5).\n275\t\n276\t**FIX (review finding, Reviewer A MINOR):** the briefing's \"new today by provider\"\n277\tquery did not route through `USABLE_MODEL_PREDICATE`, so