{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MRJnLSqdU9M6UhHFYnhHBe","type":"tool_result","content":"420\t# would force a parallel code path; the cost-metering block below reads\n421\t# `resp.usage` / `resp.content` UNCHANGED.\n422\t#\n423\t# So Wave L3 uses the PORTABLE strict-tool-use equivalent: a single tool whose\n424\t# `input_schema` IS the caller's `output_schema`, forced via\n425\t# `tool_choice={\"type\":\"tool\",\"name\":...}` and `strict:true`. The model is then\n426\t# OBLIGED to emit exactly one tool_use block whose `.input` is schema-conformant\n427\t# JSON — no prose, no code fences, no parse failure. We serialize that\n428\t# `.input` dict back to a JSON string and return it, so every existing caller\n429\t# (which does `json.loads(text)`) keeps working WITHOUT ever taking a\n430\t# strip_fences path. Metering is byte-for-byte identical: same\n431\t# `_anthropic_create(client, **kw)`, same `resp.usage` read, same\n432\t# `CostRecorder.record(...)` incl. the L1/L2 cache fields. The Sonnet→Haiku\n433\t# fallback reuses the same `kw` (tools + tool_choice ride along), so the\n434\t# degraded Haiku call is ALSO schema-guaranteed and metered identically.\n435\t_STRUCTURED_TOOL_NAME = \"emit_result\"\n436\t\n437\t\n438\t# ---- Wave L4 (2026-06-07): adaptive thinking via `effort` ----\n439\t#\n440\t# Anthropic deprecated the fixed-budget thinking knob: on 4.6+ `budget_tokens`\n441\t# is deprecated and on Opus 4.7/4.8 it is REMOVED — sending\n442\t# `thinking={\"type\":\"enabled\",\"budget_tokens\":N}` returns a 400. The modern\n443\t# replacement is ADAPTIVE thinking (`thinking={\"type\":\"adaptive\"}`) whose depth\n444\t# is steered by the GA `effort` parameter, which lives inside `output_config`\n445\t# (NOT top-level): `output_config={\"effort\": \"low\"|\"medium\"|\"high\"|...}`. Source:\n446\t# the bundled claude-api skill — SKILL.md \"Thinking & Effort\" + the python\n447\t# claude-api README \"Extended Thinking\" section (Anthropic docs, cached 2026):\n448\t#\n449\t#     thinking={\"type\": \"adaptive\"}\n450\t#     output_config={\"effort\": \"high\"}   # low | medium | high (| xhigh | max, Opus)\n451\t#\n452\t# So when a caller passes `effort=`, call_anthropic attaches exactly that shape\n453\t# and NEVER a `budget_tokens` field. Default (`effort=None`) attaches NEITHER —\n454\t# the request is byte-for-byte the pre-Wave-L4 path, so the default path is\n455\t# cost-neutral and behaviour-preserving.\n456\t#\n457\t# Aurora-allowed effort values. We don't hard-enforce the Opus-only `max` here\n458\t# (the API gates that per-model); these are the documented levels.\n459\t_EFFORT_LEVELS = (\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\", \"xhigh\", \"max\")\n460\t\n461\t# The deprecated/removed key that must NEVER appear in an assembled Anthropic\n462\t# request. Opus 4.8 returns a 400 if it does; the guard below fails loudly so a\n463\t# regression is caught in-process rather than as a live 400 mid-sweep.\n464\t_FORBIDDEN_ANTHROPIC_KEY = \"budget_tokens\"\n465\t\n466\t\n467\tdef _find_forbidden_key(obj, key: str) -> bool:\n468\t    \"\"\"Recursively True iff `key` appears anywhere in a nested dict/list `obj`.\"\"\"\n469\t    if isinstance(obj, dict):\n470\t        if key in obj:\n471\t            return True\n472\t        return any(_find_forbidden_key(v, key) for v in obj.values())\n473\t    if isinstance(obj, (list, tuple)):\n474\t        return any(_find_forbidden_key(v, key) for v in obj)\n475\t    return False\n476\t\n477\t\n478\tdef _assert_no_budget_tokens(kw: dict) -> None:\n479\t    \"\"\"Wave L4 GUARD: fail LOUDLY if a `budget_tokens` field is present anywhere\n480\t    in an assembled Anthropic request dict.\n481\t\n482\t    `budget_tokens` is deprecated on 4.6+ and REMOVED on Opus 4.7/4.8 (the live\n483\t    API returns a 400). Adaptive thinking via `effort` is the only supported\n484\t    path. This guard runs at the single dispatch funnel — immediately before\n485\t    every `_anthropic_create(...)` call (the initial call, the Haiku fallback,\n486\t    and the structured->plain degrade all go through it) — so NO assembled\n487\t    request can ever carry the forbidden key, with `effort` set OR unset. It\n488\t    raises rather than silently stripping: a `budget_tokens` appearing here means\n489\t    a code path tried to send the deprecated shape, which is a bug to surface,\n490\t    not paper over.\"\"\"\n491\t    if _find_forbidden_key(kw, _FORBIDDEN_ANTHROPIC_KEY):\n492\t        raise AssertionError(\n493\t            \"Wave L4 guard: an Anthropic request carried the deprecated/removed \"\n494\t            f\"`{_FORBIDDEN_ANTHROPIC_KEY}` field (400 on Opus 4.7/4.8). Use \"\n495\t            \"adaptive thinking via `effort` instead — see the call_anthropic \"\n496\t            \"`effort` parameter and the Wave-L4 note in llm.py.\"\n497\t        )\n498\t\n499\t\n500\tdef _fold_thinking_into_output(usage) -> int:\n501\t    \"\"\"Wave L4: return the usage's output token count WITH any SEPARATELY-reported\n502\t    thinking/reasoning tokens folded in, so adaptive-thinking spend is never\n503\t    silently dropped from metering.\n504\t\n505\t    This mirrors the Gemini `thoughts_token_count` fold in `call_gemini` — the\n506\t    root cause of the prior $118 incident was thinking tokens billed but never\n507\t    recorded. On the Anthropic Messages API, `usage.output_tokens` ALREADY\n508\t    includes thinking tokens (thinking is emitted as output content blocks), so\n509\t    in the common case there is nothing extra to add and the returned value\n510\t    equals `usage.output_tokens` — the default/no-effort path is unchanged.\n511\t\n512\t    But the SDK/usage shape can evolve to surface thinking separately (and some\n513\t    response shapes expose a distinct reasoning/thinking-token field). To be\n514\t    DEFENSIVELY correct — and to honour the Wave-L4 invariant that thinking\n515\t    tokens are always metered into output — we look for a separately-reported\n516\t    thinking-token field and add it to `output_tokens` if (and only if) it is\n517\t    present and non-zero. We never double-count: only a SEPARATE field is added;\n518\t    if the API ever moves thinking out of `output_tokens` into its own field,\n519\t    this keeps metering whole automatically.\"\"\"\n520\t    out = int(getattr(usage, \"output_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n521\t    # Probe the known/plausible separate-thinking field names, newest-first.\n522\t    # If a future SDK reports thinking tokens separately under any of these,\n523\t    # they get folded into the metered output rather than dropped.\n524\t    for fld in (\"output_thinking_tokens\", \"thinking_output_tokens\",\n525\t                \"thinking_tokens\", \"reasoning_tokens\", \"reasoning_output_tokens\"):\n526\t        extra = getattr(usage, fld, None)\n527\t        if extra:\n528\t            out += int(extra)\n529\t    return out\n530\t\n531\t\n532\tdef _structured_text_from_resp(resp) -> Optional[str]:\n533\t    \"\"\"Return a JSON string from the forced tool_use block of a structured\n534\t    response, or None if no tool_use block is present (the model declined / the\n535\t    response was empty). Callers treat None like an unparseable response —\n536\t    their existing field-default / fail-closed degradation applies.\"\"\"\n537\t    import json as _json\n538\t    for b in getattr(resp, \"content\", None) or []:\n539\t        if getattr(b, \"type\", None) == \"tool_use\" or hasattr(b, \"input\"):\n540\t            inp = getattr(b, \"input\", None)\n541\t            if isinstance(inp, dict):\n542\t                return _json.dumps(inp)\n543\t    return None\n544\t\n545\t\n546\tdef call_anthropic(prompt: str, *, model: Optional[str] = None, max_tokens: int = 600,\n547\t                   cost_recorder: Optional[CostRecorder] = None,\n548\t                   role_hint: str = \"anthropic\",\n549\t                   system: Optional[str] = None,\n550\t                   cache_system: bool = False,\n551\t                   output_schema: Optional[dict] = None,\n552\t                   effort: Optional[str] = None) -> str:\n553\t    \"\"\"Call Anthropic Messages API with G1 retry + Haiku-fallback.\n554\t\n555\t    Records cost via `cost_recorder`. On exhausted transient retries against a\n556\t    non-Haiku model (typically Sonnet for runner/critic_a), degrades to Haiku\n557\t    once. On Haiku failure, raises — caller decides to mark `runs.status='partial'`.\n558\t\n559\t    Wave L3 (2026-06-07): when `output_schema` (a JSON Schema dict) is supplied,\n560\t    the call uses STRICT FORCED TOOL USE to schema-guarantee the JSON response —\n561\t    a single tool named `emit_result` whose `input_schema` IS `output_schema`,\n562\t    forced via `tool_choice` + `strict:true`. The returned string is the\n563\t    `json.dumps(...)` of that tool's validated `.input`, so a caller's\n564\t    `json.loads(text)` parses cleanly and NEVER needs `strip_fences`. If the\n565\t    model somehow returns no tool_use block, the returned text is `\"\"` — the\n566\t    caller's existing field-default / fail-closed path then degrades exactly as\n567\t    on a malformed response (no unearned pass; no silent crash). The\n568\t    cost-metering path (resp.usage / CostRecorder.record incl. cache fields) is\n569\t    UNCHANGED, and the Sonnet→Haiku fallback carries the same `output_schema`"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01ACwxJodXAE6No2Hnb7B6TY","session_id":"a7fcfbf6-6e6f-495e-9c53-2f0602be6ffe","uuid":"6632b2d2-8974-40c4-a335-0fc6e3f15150","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:01:53.455Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Map Aurora architecture & code"}
