{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0186T91LjvR2Ky9CwAYLZt7B","type":"tool_result","content":"./.pm/memory.md:Get-ScheduledTask | ? { $_.TaskName -like 'Aurora-*' } | % { $i = Get-ScheduledTaskInfo $_; [PSCustomObject]@{Name=$_.TaskName; State=$_.State; LastRun=$i.LastRunTime; LastResult=('0x{0:X}' -f $i.LastTaskResult); NextRun=$i.NextRunTime} } | ft -a\n./CLAUDE.md:| `bin/setup-tasks.ps1`     | Idempotent registration of all 5 Aurora scheduled tasks + WU registry pin |\n./docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/HANDOFF.md:  `.env`; real schedules 01:07–06:47; working tree is production).\n./docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/RESEARCH.md:**The cheapest thing that prevents quiet failure:** push **one weekly email** — model-board delta (new/cheaper models), benchmark movement, the single best non-paper find, and one honest line \"Aurora fed your sessions N times.\" If that email isn't worth 30 seconds, that *is* the verdict — and it's cheaper to learn from one cron job than six more months of $1 nights.\n./docs/AURORA_DISCOVERY_QUALITY_PLAN.md:| E13 | Real schedule: Agents 01:07, Skills 02:19, Tools 03:41, Models 05:03, Briefing 06:47; publisher chained inside sweep + briefing `.cmd`s (runs ~01:30 too). **Scheduled tasks execute `C:\\dev\\aurora` directly — the dirty working tree IS production** | Get-ScheduledTask + setup-tasks.ps1:76-82 |\n./docs/AURORA_GOLD_STANDARD_REVIEW.md:*   **Helping Hand:** A proactive recommender agent (a skill) that sits inside your active coding environment (like Cowork). It is supposed to monitor your session context and silently query the Aurora KB. If you are struggling with a problem or starting a new agent task, it should proactively suggest the exact tool, skill, or framework from the Aurora library that solves your problem.\n./docs/AURORA_GOLD_STANDARD_REVIEW.md:*   **The \"So What?\" Problem:** The nightly sweeps produce thousands of tokens of data, but there is no scheduled task that forces Aurora to answer the hard questions. It builds a database, but it doesn't build *knowledge*.\n./docs/foreman-handoff-awareness/DESCRIPTION.md:  (write to `*_shadow`/fixture KB, no production writes, cost-capped, OFF the 01:07–06:47 cron),\n./docs/foreman-handoff-awareness/STAGE0-FRAMING.md:- **[Confirmed]** Nightly sweeps real schedule 01:07–06:47; publisher pushes scrubbed snapshot to `aurora-library`.\n./docs/foreman-handoff-awareness/STAGE0-FRAMING.md:- Dirty working tree **IS production**; changes are live. Real schedule 01:07–06:47.\n./docs/foreman-handoff-awareness/STAGE1-MASTER-PLAN.md:- **CC2 — Live-pipeline safety.** Any change to the collection/ingestion path lands behind a **shadow/dry-run** (write to `*_shadow` or a fixture KB, no production writes, cost-capped, OFF the 01:07–06:47 cron) and is promoted only after the shadow diff is reviewed. Reuse `roles/shadow_diff.py` + the `validations_shadow` pattern.\n./docs/foreman-handoff-quality/EXECUTION-LOG.md:- **DEFERRED (environmental, needs elevation):** the 2 weekly scheduled tasks (`Aurora-Link-Health`\n./docs/foreman-handoff-quality/EXECUTION-LOG.md:  Sun 06:55, `Aurora-Weekly-Digest` Sun 07:10) — `setup-tasks.ps1` must be re-run from an ELEVATED\n./docs/NEXT_STEPS.md:# Aurora — Next Steps Schedule\n./docs/NEXT_STEPS.md:- Add AgentDojo as a dev-dependency. Wire `bin/test.cmd` to run the subset of AgentDojo tasks relevant to Aurora's threat model (~10 tasks: scout-shaped indirect injection, no tool execution).\n./docs/NIGHTLY_SWEEP_HISTORY.md:- **Scheduled tasks** — `WakeToRun=True` + `StartWhenAvailable=True` on all four Aurora tasks so missed windows catch up.\n./docs/NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md:| 20 | **Add `setup-tasks.ps1`** capturing Windows Task Scheduler config (WakeToRun, StartWhenAvailable, Active Hours 04:00→22:00, ScheduledInstallTime=3). Currently only in `NOTES.md`. Without this, machine rebuild loses the schedule. Closes §18.2.bis #17. **✅ DONE 2026-05-19 PM (Bucket F4, commit `eacdca9`; extended in F5 to include the hourly Aurora-Source-Push task).** Smoke test passed: unregister/re-run produces byte-identical task state. | **M** | 1.5h | me | Write the script idempotently; smoke-test it doesn't double-create tasks; commit to repo. |\n./docs/NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md:| F4 | `bin/setup-tasks.ps1` — captures all 4 task settings (WakeToRun, StartWhenAvailable, S4U) + `ScheduledInstallTime=3` registry pin (audit found this **never landed** despite §18.3 claiming it did) | 1.5h | next session (me) | idempotent PS script; commit to aurora-source; test by un-registering one task and re-running the script | **✅ DONE 2026-05-19 PM (commit `eacdca9`, then extended in F5).** Live state captured (all 4 tasks already had `WakeToRun=True StartWhenAvailable=True RestartCount=2 ExecTimeLimit=PT1H`; WU registry already had `ActiveHoursStart=4 ActiveHoursEnd=22 IsActiveHoursEnabled=1 ScheduledInstallTime=3` — so the audit was wrong about this never landing — but it had only been set ephemerally, with no replay path for a machine rebuild). Script idempotently `Set-ScheduledTask`s an existing task or `Register-ScheduledTask`s a missing one. S4U deferred to Bucket K3 per the §22 default (\"Leave Interactive for now\"). HKLM\\…\\WindowsUpdate writes guarded by elevation check — non-elevated runs configure tasks and skip registry with clear admin-instruction note. **Test path executed**: unregistered Aurora-Tools, re-ran script, verified Aurora-Tools recreated with byte-identical settings (WakeToRun/RestartCount/ExecTimeLimit/UserId/Action all match pre-delete snapshot). **Closes §20 row 20.** |\n./docs/NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md:| F5 | Hourly auto-push of aurora-source repo as a 5th scheduled task | 30min | next session (me) | new task `Aurora-Source-Push` every hour `:30` (off-cycle from sweeps); use the new credential-manager auth from F3 | **✅ DONE 2026-05-19 PM (commit `49cec58`).** New action: `bin/run-aurora-source-push.cmd` (push only — does NOT auto-commit working-tree dirt; logs to `logs/aurora