{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gw9XWXMS8wFtFJuiJX5Bni","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora briefing — 2026-06-23\n2\t\n3\t**New finds today:** 2  (skills 0 · tools 1 · agents 1)\n4\t_Catalog: 307 total (skills 49 · tools 212 · agents 46)_\n5\t\n6\t**Top finds:**\n7\t- archive-crawler (agent) — Usable agent for multi-source archive synthesis; strong adoption (22k★), security-first design, solves real orchestration problem John likely faces. [verified · 23625★]\n8\t- benchmark-due-diligence (skill) — Usable agent skill for competitive analysis & debunking; 1.2k★, documented sandbox warnings, fits multi-agent orchestration domain. [verified · 1197★]\n9\t- academic-verify (agent) — Usable agent for Claude ecosystem, solves real multi-agent orchestration problem (claim verification via tool chaining). High adoption (22k★), but needs securit [verified · 23625★]\n10\t- debugging-network-issues (skill) — Usable diagnostic skill for Claude agents; practical network debugging pattern. 1.2k★ adoption signal; fits agent tooling ecosystem. [1197★]\n11\t- deep-research (skill) — Usable Claude skill for multi-pass research synthesis with evidence tracking & citations. 1.2k★, documented governance controls, addresses agent evaluation/qual [verified · 1197★]\n12\t\n13\t**Models — 326 tracked** (usable, junk-filtered)\n14\t\n15\t**What moved + why it matters (last 3 nights):**\n16\t_Tools — 3 new_\n17\t- computer-use — Usable cross-platform tool, but unclear adoption/maintenance. No stars, vague incorporation status, incomplete description. Moderate ecosystem fit.\n18\t- himalaya — General-purpose CLI tool, no Claude/agent ecosystem fit. No adoption signal (stars unknown), unclear quality badges or documentation.\n19\t- imsg — Local macOS messaging utility. No ecosystem fit (not Claude/agent-related), no adoption signal, narrow use case outside John's tooling stack.\n20\t_Agents — 2 new_\n21\t- github — Useful tooling but lacks ecosystem fit (not Claude/MCP), no adoption signal, unclear if novel or documented.\n22\t- gifgrep — Narrow utility tool (GIF search/download), no adoption signal, no ecosystem fit with Claude/agent stack or orchestration craft.\n23\t\n24\t**Value & health — AMBER:** value signals are open-loop — too few logged decisions (n<30) to trust an adoption rate yet.\n25\t- Is it working? Too early to say — only 7 decision(s) logged so far, below the 30 needed to trust a rate. Raw so far: 6 kept of 7 decided (1 dismissed) — open-loop (n=7, need >=30 to trust a rate).\n26\t- Is it worth it? Can't honestly price it yet — $33.02 spent over 6 useful find(s) — open-loop (n=6, need >=30 to trust a per-find cost).\n27\t- What's wrong? frontier coverage isn't measured yet (Wave 2 ranker pending); decision-logging isn't capturing labels yet (Wave 5 pending); every learned signal runs open-loop until n>=30.\n28\t- What to think about? The bootstrap: 0 decision(s) logged vs the 30 needed before any adoption rate, precision figure, or ranker weight can be trusted. Until then, treat every suggestion as a non-authoritative prompt, not a verdict.\n29\t\n30\t**Should I adopt? (suggestions — not verdicts):**\n31\t- **archive-crawler** (agent) — model suggests: trial · confidence: low-medium\n32\t  - What it is: Universal archivist for personal file archives (Dropbox/B2/Gmail-takeout/local-mount/hard-drive-dump). Filters for high-value content (the user's own writing, ideas, relationships) and surfaces it interactively. REFUSES TO RUN without an explicit gbrain.yml `archive-crawler.scan_paths:` allow-list.\n33\t  - Fit: Usable agent for multi-source archive synthesis; strong adoption (22k★), security-first design, solves real orchestration problem John likely faces.\n34\t  - Advantages: carries an evidence badge (verified); taste score 0.78\n35\t  - Risks: security status: clean-with-notes\n36\t  - Source: https://github.com/garrytan/gbrain/blob/HEAD/skills/archive-crawler/SKILL.md\n37\t- **benchmark-due-diligence** (skill) — model suggests: trial · confidence: low-medium\n38\t  - What it is: Runs adversarial due-diligence on a benchmark the user envies — a founder, KOL, company, or product whose claimed success looks inflated — splitting marketing bubble from real signal, then mapping the validated playbook onto the user's own resources. Use whenever the user wants to 尽调/对标/拆解 a competi\n39\t  - Fit: Usable agent skill for competitive analysis & debunking; 1.2k★, documented sandbox warnings, fits multi-agent orchestration domain.\n40\t  - Advantages: carries an evidence badge (verified); taste score 0.72\n41\t  - Risks: security status: clean-with-notes\n42\t  - Source: https://github.com/daymade/claude-code-skills/blob/HEAD/benchmark-due-diligence/SKILL.md\n43\t- **academic-verify** (agent) — model suggests: trial · confidence: low-medium\n44\t  - What it is: Verify a research claim or academic citation by tracing it through publication → methodology → raw data → independent replication. Routes through perplexity-research for the actual web lookup, then formats results as a citation-checked brain page. Use when a book/article/conversation cites a study a\n45\t  - Fit: Usable agent for Claude ecosystem, solves real multi-agent orchestration problem (claim verification via tool chaining). High adoption (22k★), but needs securit\n46\t  - Advantages: carries an evidence badge (verified); taste score 0.72\n47\t  - Risks: security status: clean-with-notes\n48\t  - Source: https://github.com/garrytan/gbrain/blob/HEAD/skills/academic-verify/SKILL.md\n49\t\n50\t_Decisions logged this week: 0 (need >=30 to validate the ranker)._\n51\t\n52\t**Suggestion adoption:** 24% (window all-time, n=21)\n53\t\n54\t**Spend (MTD):** anthropic $22.03 · gemini $0.00\n55\t\n56\t_Full briefing: reports/morning/2026-06-23.md_"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y16vzRsaFa4WCzXfR89u1q","session_id":"a7fcfbf6-6e6f-495e-9c53-2f0602be6ffe","uuid":"c24e0cc1-8893-4969-9aab-c14ba92326bb","tim