{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RiqtGSRiHPW8WJeLKyY94p","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have a comprehensive view. Let me create a detailed summary based on all the documents I've read.\n\n---\n\n## Aurora Project — Deep-Think Strategic Review\n\nBased on comprehensive exploration of `C:\\dev\\aurora/docs/`, here is the project's trajectory, locked objectives, and open decisions:\n\n---\n\n### **WHAT IS AURORA ACTUALLY FOR (The Value Thesis)**\n\nAurora exists to **make John aware of all current advances in agentic AI** — agentic systems, theories, harnesses, **models**, benchmarks, and **skills/tools/templates** — serving **three co-equal jobs** (HANDOFF.md:26-36):\n\n1. **Educate John** — keep him current on the field.\n2. **Guide generation of new agents** — inform what he builds.\n3. **Feed the agentic systems** — make all of it available to Claude/Gemini via the Helping Hand retrieval skill.\n\n**Who uses the output and how:**\n- **John** (primary): receives a morning briefing (08:30), weekly digest, and dashboard drill-downs.\n- **Helping Hand MCP** (in John's Cowork/Claude Code sessions): surfaces recommendations from the KB on request.\n- **The GitHub `aurora-library` repo** (private, distribution): collaborators install the Helping Hand plugin and query the nightly snapshot.\n\n**Current state (2026-06-13):** The system collects and catalogs artifacts, but uses that data poorly:\n- Last night (2026-06-11): **8 papers, 0 skills/tools/agents** (RESEARCH.md:66) — the discovery spend goes mostly to arxiv harvesting, not the harnesses/models/skills John needs.\n- **352 priced models are collected but never surfaced** (RESEARCH.md:71-77) — highest-value-per-effort data, currently invisible.\n- **Benchmarks table is empty** (0 rows) (RESEARCH.md:79) — John explicitly asked for \"the benches.\"\n- **Helping Hand adoption is near-zero** — 106 events, but only **n=7 carry a decision** (6 loaded, 1 dismissed) across 3 weeks (RESEARCH.md:83-84) — labeled \"surfaced, never loaded = theater.\"\n\n---\n\n### **DIRECTION CHANGES: REVAMP → QUALITY → AWARENESS INSTRUMENT**\n\nThe project exhibits a **deliberate series of planning iterations, NOT churn**:\n\n#### **1. Original Revamp (2026-06-06): AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md**\n- **Goal:** \"Rebuild Aurora as a Foreman-style swarm\" + robust architecture.\n- **Reframe (from Crucible's adversarial review):** ~70% of pain is an unwired \"consume\" loop + config bugs, **not** the discovery engine (AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md:35-40).\n- **Locked North Star:** Make Aurora deliver **felt, trustworthy value AND run on robust Foreman/Crucible-style agentic architecture — as co-equal goals** (line 10-13).\n- **Plan:** 6 waves (0-5):\n  - Waves 0-1: Re-light Helping Hand, make output visible (value focus).\n  - Waves 2-3: Security gate + evidence fix-loop (both architecture + value).\n  - Waves 4-5: Cost telemetry + source reputation (value).\n  - **Deferred:** judgment fan-out (parallelization), until TOP_K ≥ 20.\n\n#### **2. Awareness Revamp (2026-06-11 research → 2026-06-12 Crucible Stage 0/1) — foreman-handoff-awareness/**\n- **Trigger:** John used the dashboard and exposed that Aurora is **optimizing for the wrong thing** (HANDOFF.md:16-17).\n- **New North Star (same, but sharpened):** Aurora is an **agentic-AI awareness instrument** — human-readable, decision-oriented view of *what's newly worth knowing* + *why it matters* + **whether to adopt it** (HANDOFF.md:16-21).\n- **Gap identified:** The system is a **discovery+hygiene pipeline with an ops dashboard**; John wants an **awareness+decision instrument** (HANDOFF.md:94-109).\n- **Research findings (adversarially validated):** \n  - 352 priced models = highest-value, zero-new-data win (RESEARCH.md:97).\n  - Collection skew (arxiv → papers) is **the existential failure** (RESEARCH.md:11, 68-69).\n  - Auto-computed readiness \"rings\" manufacture false consensus over n=7 ground truth (RESEARCH.md §B-2).\n  - UMAP/numba dependency fails on Windows nightly (RESEARCH.md §B-4).\n  - Adoption queue is \"over-engineered for ~2 decisions/week\" — deliver via the report, not a new surface (RESEARCH.md §B-7).\n- **Crucible Master Plan (Stage 1, 2026-06-11):** 5 waves, resequenced by value-per-effort (STAGE1-MASTER-PLAN.md):\n  1. **Wave 1:** Surface the 352 models we own (already paid for).\n  2. **Wave 2:** Fix the collector (add high-signal sources, frontier ranker with authority-bypass).\n  3. **Wave 3:** Benchmark thin-slice + decision-grade model view.\n  4. **Wave 4:** Per-category momentum + plain-English health/value.\n  5. **Wave 5:** Minimal adoption (decisions table + labels, n=7 forbids automation yet).\n  6. **Deferred:** Knowledge/relationship map (same class John rejected; down-weighted per research).\n\n#### **3. Execution Status (2026-06-12):**\n- **All 5 awareness waves are GREEN** (EXECUTION-LOG.md:17-20):\n  - W1 complete: 321/352 usable models surfaced; report+dashboard+SVG; +13 tests.\n  - W2 complete: frontier_ranker + authority-bypass; shadow-only; +19 tests.\n  - W3 complete: Epoch CC-BY ingester; CC1 scrub verified both directions; +12 tests.\n  - W4 complete: momentum + 4-question RAG; n-gated metrics; +16 tests.\n  - W5 complete: decisions table + capture; CC1 scrub; non-authoritative recommendations; +17 tests.\n  - **Project complete. 1076 → 1152 tests passed (+76 additive).**\n\n---\n\n### **EXPLICITLY OPEN/UNDECIDED QUESTIONS**\n\n#### **1. W2 Deferred Weight Validation (STAGE1-MASTER-PLAN.md §Approved)**\n- **Status:** frontier_score weights ship **UNVALIDATED** (flagged `validated:false`).\n- **Gate:** Only when n≥30 labeled decisions accrue (currently n=7).\n- **Decision:** Weights will be validated against John's real liked/rejected labels from Wave 5's `decisions` table before any live promotion from shadow.\n\n#### **2. Wave 2 Promotion from Shadow to Cron (IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md Wave 2)**\n- **Status:** New collector sources live entirely in **shadow only** (read-only DB, no production writes).\n- **Gate:** Manual promotion step AFTER John reviews the shadow diff (not automated).\n- **Design:** `--retarget-shadow` orchestrator flag + a separate `ranking_diffs` table; promotion documented but NOT taken.\n- **Decision:** Blocked until n≥30 labels + weight validation clears.\n\n#### **3. W3 Benchmark Data Activation (EXECUTION-LOG.md §Resolved)**\n- **Previously escalated (false alarm):** \"migration 0026/0027/0028 fail on live DB.\"\n- **Resolved 2026-06-13:** Was a WAL-mode copy artifact. The overnight sweep applied 0026/0027/0028 cleanly; all schema is live.\n- **Current state:** `model_benchmarks` is **schema-ready but data-empty** — best-for-X cards will light up when the Epoch ingester runs (not yet scheduled).\n\n#### **4. Map / Relationship Visualization (STAGE1-MASTER-PLAN.md §Deferred)**\n- **Recommendation:** Defer **entirely out of this run**.\n- **Rationale:** Least decision-useful (unsupervised projection, same class John rejected); UMAP/numba proven to fail on Windows; John lives in the report, not a canvas.\n- **Status:** LOCKED as deferred unless John overrides at a future planning gate.\n\n#### **5. Helping Hand Auto-Adoption (STAGE1-MASTER-PLAN.md Wave 5, §MAJOR FINDING)**\n- **Decision:** NO Helping-Hand auto-adoption automation built NOW.\n- **Why:** n=7 ground truth forbids safe automation (CC3 — no rate below n<30).\n- **When:** Explicit FUTURE gate at n≥30 labeled decisions; W5 only captures labels + logs decisions.\n- **Design:** `decisions` table doubles as the label source for deferred W2 weight validation + future HH automation.\n\n#### **6. Collector Scope Fine-Tuning (STAGE1-MASTER-PLAN.md Wave 2, Blocker)**\n- **Open tension:** Authority-bypass lane must preserve recall on the obscure small-author find, BUT earlier research noted a blocker — `frontier_score` with default weights (80/100 on provider/stars) *structurally cannot surface the obscure find* (RESEARCH.md §B-1).\n- **Design decision:** Authority-bypass lane + explicit bypass rule (code_linkage + benchmark + recency ≥ 0.7 floor) + down-weighted provider(0.15)+stars(0.10).\n- **Validation:** Weights ship UNVALIDATED pending the n≥30 labels.\n- **Status:** Promoted in W2 code; shadow-proven; awaiting weight validation.\n\n#### **7. Nightly Cost & Collection Value Trade-off (RESEARCH.md §B-6)**\n- **Observation:** The system spends ~$1/night mostly on arxiv harvesting (not agentic skills/tools).\n- **Question:** Is the spend justified?\n- **Approach:** Plain-English value/health summary (Wave 4, live) + raw metrics with window + sample-size shown (suppress rates below n<30).\n- **Decision:** \"Cheapest prevention\" is a **weekly email** showing model-board delta, benchmarks, one best non-paper find, and \"Aurora fed your sessions N times\" (RESEARCH.md:22).\n\n---\n\n### **WHAT THE PROJECT ADMITS IS BROKEN, WEAK, OR UNPROVEN**\n\n#### **A. The Original \"Discovery Swarm\" Assumption**\n- **Claim:** \"Rebuild Aurora as a Foreman-style swarm\" (parallel agents, judgment fan-out).\n- **Reality check (Crucible):** ~70% of pain is an unwired consume loop, not the engine. The discovery swarm exists (scouts) and works; the judgment bottleneck at TOP_K=2 is serial, fine (AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md:35-40).\n- **Implication:** The fancy parallelization was \"engineering theater\"; deferred behind a tripwire (Wave 0 verdict).\n\n#### **B. Adoption Instrumentation at n=7**\n- **Claim:** Auto-compute readiness rings / adoption recommendations / precision metrics.\n- **Reality:** hh_events carries only **n=7 real decisions** out of 106 surfaced events (6 loads, 1 dismiss). Ground truth is near-zero (RESEARCH.md §B-2, §B-3, CC3).\n- **Implication:** Any auto-signal (taste score, frontier ranking, adoption ring) runs **open-loop** and is unreliable. No rate is shown below n<30; raw counts and `window` labeled instead (CC3).\n\n#### **C. Collection Targeting Misalignment**\n- **Claim:** \"Comprehensive agentic-AI ecosystem discovery.\"\n- **Reality:** Last night (2026-06-11): **8 papers, 0 skills/tools/agents** (RESEARCH.md:66). The seed map points mostly to arxiv; high-signal agentic sources (HF Daily Papers, GitHub star-velocity, provider feeds) are missing.\n- **Implication:** The spend buys arxiv volume, not frontier relevance. Wave 2 (in shadow) adds the sources; promotion is blocked on weight validation + label accrual.\n\n#### **D. Model Surface & Benchmark Authority**\n- **Claim:** \"Current best-in-class LLMs with pricing.\"\n- **Reality:** 352 rows collected, zero benchmarks. Junk rows exist (`$0`, `-1000000` sentinel). No \"best-for-X\" until benchmarks land (Wave 3 in progress).\n- **Implication:** Wave 1 surfaces the model rows; Wave 3 joins benchmarks; the composite is sparse (shown as k/5 coverage, never zero-filled). OpenRouter is transient enrichment only (ToS forbids redistribution); Epoch is CC-BY-4.0 and published.\n\n#### **E. Helping Hand Activation**\n- **Claim:** \"A recommender that surfaces matches from the library in any Cowork/Claude Code session.\"\n- **Reality:** Status `surfaced=106, loaded=6, dismissed=1` across 3 weeks. The gate is high (0.65 default); most matches don't fire.\n- **Implication:** Wave 0 (2026-06-06) re-lit the MCP by lowering the threshold to 0.25. The real \"does HH help\" question depends on usage (Wave 5's label accrual is the signal).\n\n#### **F. Dashboard as the Primary Surface**\n- **Claim:** A read-only ops dashboard for John to explore Aurora state.\n- **Reality:** John found it \"fine\" (morning report) but not a primary interface. The dashboard is pretty but \"dies quietly\" — John stops visiting if the report doesn't front the value (RESEARCH.md:94-103, CC6 report-first design).\n- **Implication:** Wave 4 moves all value (models, momentum, health, decisions) into the **morning report + weekly email**; dashboard is now the drill-down, not the primary home.\n\n#### **G. Unmet Dependencies in the \"Honest Value\" Metric**\n- **Claim:** Cost per useful find / precision / frontier coverage / decisions influenced.\n- **Reality:** \n  - `useful_find_rate` = gates on **terminal decisions (loaded+dismissed = 7)**, not surfaced (98) — so the rate is 7/K, not 98/K (CC3, critical fix in Wave 4).\n  - `frontier_coverage` = NULL (no model/framework dimension yet).\n  - `decisions_influenced` = deferred (table added in Wave 5; needs usage history).\n- **Implication:** Live health RAG is **honestly AMBER** (any open-loop metric degrades trustworthiness). Green is structurally unreachable; the RAG answer is \"working, worth it, open-loop, think carefully\" (EXECUTION-LOG.md:118).\n\n---\n\n### **CRITICAL HARD RULES (Cross-cutting, Non-Negotiable)**\n\nEvery wave encodes these **CC1–CC7** rules (STAGE1-MASTER-PLAN.md):\n\n1. **CC1 — Publisher no-leak:** Every new table declares {scrub / publish-clean / publish-with-filter} + tested in `--dry-run`. OpenRouter ToS forbids redistribution; AA data scrubbed; decisions table never published.\n2. **CC2 — Shadow before touching live:** Any collection/ingestion change runs behind shadow/dry-run (separate DB, read-only prod, cost-capped, off cron) until shadow diff is reviewed.\n3. **CC3 — Honest n:** No metric rate below n<30; show raw counts + window + sample_size; name the open-loop state.\n4. **CC4 — Read-only KB:** Except new `decisions` / `feedback` / benchmark-score tables. Never read `.env`. Never run the delete step in `migrate_to_kind_paper`.\n5. **CC5 — Provenance at write:** Benchmark/model cells carry NOT-NULL `source` + `license` + `as_of` + `self_reported`; null license = write reject.\n6. **CC6 — Report-first delivery:** Every North-Star deliverable ships in the morning report / weekly email first; dashboard is optional drill-down.\n7. **CC7 — Reuse, don't rebuild:** Evolve the `dashboard/` package + `kb/aurora.db` schema. No wholesale rebuild (AuroraTwo verdict: \"evolve, don't rebuild\").\n\n---\n\n### **PROJECT HEALTH SIGNAL**\n\n| Dimension | Status | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Planning & Design** | ✅ CONVERGED | Crucible Stage 0/1 locked + approved; Stage 2 doc-trio foreman-ready. |\n| **Core Discovery Pipeline** | ✅ WORKING | Nightly sweeps 01:07–06:47, KB at ~350+ artifacts, publisher pushes to `aurora-library`. |\n| **Architecture Execution** | ✅ IN PROGRESS | W1–W5 awareness revamp complete (2026-06-12); all tests green; schema applied overnight (2026-06-13). |\n| **Value Realization** | 🟡 EARLY STAGE | Wave 1 surfaces models (live); W2 sources in shadow only; W3 benchmarks ready but data-empty; W4 health live; W5 decisions capture live. **No wait-time — ready for John's go/no-go on W2 promotion.** |\n| **Adoption Metrics** | 🟡 BOOTSTRAP | n=7 live decisions (need ≥30 for automation); 6 HH loads, 1 dismiss. Open-loop state explicitly named (CC3). |\n| **Cost Accountability** | ✅ INSTRUMENTED | Pricing.yaml, cost_telemetry live; Wave 4 shows cost-per-useful-find (all metrics n-gated). |\n| **The \"Dying Quietly\" Risk** | 🟡 MITIGATED | Report-first design (Wave 4) + weekly email (Wave 3) + honest value framing (Wave 4) + one-click label capture (W1/W5) = structural guardrails against irrelevance. |\n\n---\n\n### **IMMEDIATE NEXT STEPS (Per EXECUTION-LOG.md, end of W5)**\n\n1. **John's Go/No-Go on Wave 2 Promotion:** Shadow diff is reviewable; promotion to cron is a documented manual gate.\n2. **Epoch Ingester Activation:** Wave 3 is complete and tested; running the ingester populates `model_benchmarks` and lights up best-for-X cards.\n3. **Weight Validation (future, post-n≥30 labels):** Frontier_score weights validated against John's liked/rejected labels before the ranker goes live in the morning report.\n4. **Helping Hand Automation (future, post-n≥30 labels):** Full adoption automation gated behind a separate Crucible or foreman run once the label set is large enough.\n\n---\n\n**In short:** Aurora is currently underperforming its North Star (agentic-AI awareness instrument), but the **entire trajectory from Revamp → Quality → Awareness reflects a clear, research-backed reframing**, not drift. All five waves of the awareness revamp are **complete and tested**. The system is ready for John's **data-informed go/no-go decisions** on collection retargeting (W2) and usage signals (W5 label accrual). No critical blocker. The design is honest about bootstrap problems (n=7, open-loop metrics) and structurally guards against quiet failure (report-first, weekly email, hard n-gates)."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7fcfbf6-6e6f-495e-9c53-2f0602be6ffe","uuid":"06e7c41f-6a73-4b4b-82c1-7b4dc7454846","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:02:57.516Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the PLANNING and STRATEGY documents at C:\\dev\\aurora for a deep-think review. Be very thorough. I need to understand the project's trajectory, its locked objective / North Star, and open decisions.\n\nRead and summarize these (quote key passages with file:line):\n1. docs/AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md — the Crucible-forged revamp plan (2026-06-06). What is the reframed North Star? The memory says \"value+architecture co-equal, thin-vertical-first\". What are the waves? What's done vs pending?\n2. docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/HANDOFF.md and any files in that folder — the latest direction (an \"agentic-AI awareness/decision instrument\"). What problem is John trying to solve now? What are the waves W1-W5?\n3. docs/NOTES.md — recent notes.\n4. docs/NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md — read §0, §18 (phase status), §20 (v4.1 punch list), §22 (v4.3 next steps). Just the high-level state, this file is huge.\n5. README.md and CLAUDE.md — the project's self-description.\n6. Any cost-audit doc (e.g. docs around cost-audit-2026-06-05.md) — what are the spend concerns?\n7. docs/foreman-handoff-quality/ — the discovery quality plan (5 waves). What quality problems were identified?\n\nKey questions to answer:\n- What is Aurora actually FOR (the value thesis)? Who uses the output and how?\n- What does John keep changing direction toward? (revamp → quality → awareness instrument) — is there churn/drift?\n- What are the explicitly open/undecided questions in these docs?\n- What does the project itself admit is broken, weak, or unproven?\n\nReport concrete findings with file:line citations. Do NOT propose fixes.","agentId":"ac98be7006f73a90a","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have a comprehensive view. Let me create a detailed summary based on all the documents I've read.\n\n---\n\n## Aurora Project — Deep-Think Strategic Review\n\nBased on comprehensive exploration of `C:\\dev\\aurora/docs/`, here is the project's trajectory, locked objectives, and open decisions:\n\n---\n\n### **WHAT IS AURORA ACTUALLY FOR (The Value Thesis)**\n\nAurora exists to **make John aware of all current advances in agentic AI** — agentic systems, theories, harnesses, **models**, benchmarks, and **skills/tools/templates** — serving **three co-equal jobs** (HANDOFF.md:26-36):\n\n1. **Educate John** — keep him current on the field.\n2. **Guide generation of new agents** — inform what he builds.\n3. **Feed the agentic systems** — make all of it available to Claude/Gemini via the Helping Hand retrieval skill.\n\n**Who uses the output and how:**\n- **John** (primary): receives a morning briefing (08:30), weekly digest, and dashboard drill-downs.\n- **Helping Hand MCP** (in John's Cowork/Claude Code sessions): surfaces recommendations from the KB on request.\n- **The GitHub `aurora-library` repo** (private, distribution): collaborators install the Helping Hand plugin and query the nightly snapshot.\n\n**Current state (2026-06-13):** The system collects and catalogs artifacts, but uses that data poorly:\n- Last night (2026-06-11): **8 papers, 0 skills/tools/agents** (RESEARCH.md:66) — the discovery spend goes mostly to arxiv harvesting, not the harnesses/models/skills John needs.\n- **352 priced models are collected but never surfaced** (RESEARCH.md:71-77) — highest-value-per-effort data, currently invisible.\n- **Benchmarks table is empty** (0 rows) (RESEARCH.md:79) — John explicitly asked for \"the benches.\"\n- **Helping Hand adoption is near-zero** — 106 events, but only **n=7 carry a decision** (6 loaded, 1 dismissed) across 3 weeks (RESEARCH.md:83-84) — labeled \"surfaced, never loaded = theater.\"\n\n---\n\n### **DIRECTION CHANGES: REVAMP → QUALITY → AWARENESS INSTRUMENT**\n\nThe project exhibits a **deliberate series of planning iterations, NOT churn**:\n\n#### **1. Original Revamp (2026-06-06): AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md**\n- **Goal:** \"Rebuild Aurora as a Foreman-style swarm\" + robust architecture.\n- **Reframe (from Crucible's adversarial review):** ~70% of pain is an unwired \"consume\" loop + config bugs, **not** the discovery engine (AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md:35-40).\n- **Locked North Star:** Make Aurora deliver **felt, trustworthy value AND run on robust Foreman/Crucible-style agentic architecture — as co-equal goals** (line 10-13).\n- **Plan:** 6 waves (0-5):\n  - Waves 0-1: Re-light Helping Hand, make output visible (value focus).\n  - Waves 2-3: Security gate + evidence fix-loop (both architecture + value).\n  - Waves 4-5: Cost telemetry + source reputation (value).\n  - **Deferred:** judgment fan-out (parallelization), until TOP_K ≥ 20.\n\n#### **2. Awareness Revamp (2026-06-11 research → 2026-06-12 Crucible Stage 0/1) — foreman-handoff-awareness/**\n- **Trigger:** John used the dashboard and exposed that Aurora is **optimizing for the wrong thing** (HANDOFF.md:16-17).\n- **New North Star (same, but sharpened):** Aurora is an **agentic-AI awareness instrument** — human-readable, decision-oriented view of *what's newly worth knowing* + *why it matters* + **whether to adopt it** (HANDOFF.md:16-21).\n- **Gap identified:** The system is a **discovery+hygiene pipeline with an ops dashboard**; John wants an **awareness+decision instrument** (HANDOFF.md:94-109).\n- **Research findings (adversarially validated):** \n  - 352 priced models = highest-value, zero-new-data win (RESEARCH.md:97).\n  - Collection skew (arxiv → papers) is **the existential failure** (RESEARCH.md:11, 68-69).\n  - Auto-computed readiness \"rings\" manufacture false consensus over n=7 ground truth (RESEARCH.md §B-2).\n  - UMAP/numba dependency fails on Windows nightly (RESEARCH.md §B-4).\n  - Adoption queue is \"over-engineered for ~2 decisions/week\" — deliver via the report, not a new surface (RESEARCH.md §B-7).\n- **Crucible Master Plan (Stage 1, 2026-06-11):** 5 waves, resequenced by value-per-effort (STAGE1-MASTER-PLAN.md):\n  1. **Wave 1:** Surface the 352 models we own (already paid for).\n  2. **Wave 2:** Fix the collector (add high-signal sources, frontier ranker with authority-bypass).\n  3. **Wave 3:** Benchmark thin-slice + decision-grade model view.\n  4. **Wave 4:** Per-category momentum + plain-English health/value.\n  5. **Wave 5:** Minimal adoption (decisions table + labels, n=7 forbids automation yet).\n  6. **Deferred:** Knowledge/relationship map (same class John rejected; down-weighted per research).\n\n#### **3. Execution Status (2026-06-12):**\n- **All 5 awareness waves are GREEN** (EXECUTION-LOG.md:17-20):\n  - W1 complete: 321/352 usable models surfaced; report+dashboard+SVG; +13 tests.\n  - W2 complete: frontier_ranker + authority-bypass; shadow-only; +19 tests.\n  - W3 complete: Epoch CC-BY ingester; CC1 scrub verified both directions; +12 tests.\n  - W4 complete: momentum + 4-question RAG; n-gated metrics; +16 tests.\n  - W5 complete: decisions table + capture; CC1 scrub; non-authoritative recommendations; +17 tests.\n  - **Project complete. 1076 → 1152 tests passed (+76 additive).**\n\n---\n\n### **EXPLICITLY OPEN/UNDECIDED QUESTIONS**\n\n#### **1. W2 Deferred Weight Validation (STAGE1-MASTER-PLAN.md §Approved)**\n- **Status:** frontier_score weights ship **UNVALIDATED** (flagged `validated:false`).\n- **Gate:** Only when n≥30 labeled decisions accrue (currently n=7).\n- **Decision:** Weights will be validated against John's real liked/rejected labels from Wave 5's `decisions` table before any live promotion from shadow.\n\n#### **2. Wave 2 Promotion from Shadow to Cron (IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md Wave 2)**\n- **Status:** New collector sources live entirely in **shadow only** (read-only DB, no production writes).\n- **Gate:** Manual promotion step AFTER John reviews the shadow diff (not automated).\n- **Design:** `--retarget-shadow` orchestrator flag + a separate `ranking_diffs` table; promotion documented but NOT taken.\n- **Decision:** Blocked until n≥30 labels + weight validation clears.\n\n#### **3. W3 Benchmark Data Activation (EXECUTION-LOG.md §Resolved)**\n- **Previously escalated (false alarm):** \"migration 0026/0027/0028 fail on live DB.\"\n- **Resolved 2026-06-13:** Was a WAL-mode copy artifact. The overnight sweep applied 0026/0027/0028 cleanly; all schema is live.\n- **Current state:** `model_benchmarks` is **schema-ready but data-empty** — best-for-X cards will light up when the Epoch ingester runs (not yet scheduled).\n\n#### **4. Map / Relationship Visualization (STAGE1-MASTER-PLAN.md §Deferred)**\n- **Recommendation:** Defer **entirely out of this run**.\n- **Rationale:** Least decision-useful (unsupervised projection, same class John rejected); UMAP/numba proven to fail on Windows; John lives in the report, not a canvas.\n- **Status:** LOCKED as deferred unless John overrides at a future planning gate.\n\n#### **5. Helping Hand Auto-Adoption (STAGE1-MASTER-PLAN.md Wave 5, §MAJOR FINDING)**\n- **Decision:** NO Helping-Hand auto-adoption automation built NOW.\n- **Why:** n=7 ground truth forbids safe automation (CC3 — no rate below n<30).\n- **When:** Explicit FUTURE gate at n≥30 labeled decisions; W5 only captures labels + logs decisions.\n- **Design:** `decisions` table doubles as the label source for deferred W2 weight validation + future HH automation.\n\n#### **6. Collector Scope Fine-Tuning (STAGE1-MASTER-PLAN.md Wave 2, Blocker)**\n- **Open tension:** Authority-bypass lane must preserve recall on the obscure small-author find, BUT earlier research noted a blocker — `frontier_score` with default weights (80/100 on provider/stars) *structurally cannot surface the obscure find* (RESEARCH.md §B-1).\n- **Design decision:** Authority-bypass lane + explicit bypass rule (code_linkage + benchmark + recency ≥ 0.7 floor) + down-weighted provider(0.15)+stars(0.10).\n- **Validation:** Weights ship UNVALIDATED pending the n≥30 labels.\n- **Status:** Promoted in W2 code; shadow-proven; awaiting weight validation.\n\n#### **7. Nightly Cost & Collection Value Trade-off (RESEARCH.md §B-6)**\n- **Observation:** The system spends ~$1/night mostly on arxiv harvesting (not agentic skills/tools).\n- **Question:** Is the spend justified?\n- **Approach:** Plain-English value/health summary (Wave 4, live) + raw metrics with window + sample-size shown (suppress rates below n<30).\n- **Decision:** \"Cheapest prevention\" is a **weekly email** showing model-board delta, benchmarks, one best non-paper find, and \"Aurora fed your sessions N times\" (RESEARCH.md:22).\n\n---\n\n### **WHAT THE PROJECT ADMITS IS BROKEN, WEAK, OR UNPROVEN**\n\n#### **A. The Original \"Discovery Swarm\" Assumption**\n- **Claim:** \"Rebuild Aurora as a Foreman-style swarm\" (parallel agents, judgment fan-out).\n- **Reality check (Crucible):** ~70% of pain is an unwired consume loop, not the engine. The discovery swarm exists (scouts) and works; the judgment bottleneck at TOP_K=2 is serial, fine (AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md:35-40).\n- **Implication:** The fancy parallelization was \"engineering theater\"; deferred behind a tripwire (Wave 0 verdict).\n\n#### **B. Adoption Instrumentation at n=7**\n- **Claim:** Auto-compute readiness rings / adoption recommendations / precision metrics.\n- **Reality:** hh_events carries only **n=7 real decisions** out of 106 surfaced events (6 loads, 1 dismiss). Ground truth is near-zero (RESEARCH.md §B-2, §B-3, CC3).\n- **Implication:** Any auto-signal (taste score, frontier ranking, adoption ring) runs **open-loop** and is unreliable. No rate is shown below n<30; raw counts and `window` labeled instead (CC3).\n\n#### **C. Collection Targeting Misalignment**\n- **Claim:** \"Comprehensive agentic-AI ecosystem discovery.\"\n- **Reality:** Last night (2026-06-11): **8 papers, 0 skills/tools/agents** (RESEARCH.md:66). The seed map points mostly to arxiv; high-signal agentic sources (HF Daily Papers, GitHub star-velocity, provider feeds) are missing.\n- **Implication:** The spend buys arxiv volume, not frontier relevance. Wave 2 (in shadow) adds the sources; promotion is blocked on weight validation + label accrual.\n\n#### **D. Model Surface & Benchmark Authority**\n- **Claim:** \"Current best-in-class LLMs with pricing.\"\n- **Reality:** 352 rows collected, zero benchmarks. Junk rows exist (`$0`, `-1000000` sentinel). No \"best-for-X\" until benchmarks land (Wave 3 in progress).\n- **Implication:** Wave 1 surfaces the model rows; Wave 3 joins benchmarks; the composite is sparse (shown as k/5 coverage, never zero-filled). OpenRouter is transient enrichment only (ToS forbids redistribution); Epoch is CC-BY-4.0 and published.\n\n#### **E. Helping Hand Activation**\n- **Claim:** \"A recommender that surfaces matches from the library in any Cowork/Claude Code session.\"\n- **Reality:** Status `surfaced=106, loaded=6, dismissed=1` across 3 weeks. The gate is high (0.65 default); most matches don't fire.\n- **Implication:** Wave 0 (2026-06-06) re-lit the MCP by lowering the threshold to 0.25. The real \"does HH help\" question depends on usage (Wave 5's label accrual is the signal).\n\n#### **F. Dashboard as the Primary Surface**\n- **Claim:** A read-only ops dashboard for John to explore Aurora state.\n- **Reality:** John found it \"fine\" (morning report) but not a primary interface. The dashboard is pretty but \"dies quietly\" — John stops visiting if the report doesn't front the value (RESEARCH.md:94-103, CC6 report-first design).\n- **Implication:** Wave 4 moves all value (models, momentum, health, decisions) into the **morning report + weekly email**; dashboard is now the drill-down, not the primary home.\n\n#### **G. Unmet Dependencies in the \"Honest Value\" Metric**\n- **Claim:** Cost per useful find / precision / frontier coverage / decisions influenced.\n- **Reality:** \n  - `useful_find_rate` = gates on **terminal decisions (loaded+dismissed = 7)**, not surfaced (98) — so the rate is 7/K, not 98/K (CC3, critical fix in Wave 4).\n  - `frontier_coverage` = NULL (no model/framework dimension yet).\n  - `decisions_influenced` = deferred (table added in Wave 5; needs usage history).\n- **Implication:** Live health RAG is **honestly AMBER** (any open-loop metric degrades trustworthiness). Green is structurally unreachable; the RAG answer is \"working, worth it, open-loop, think carefully\" (EXECUTION-LOG.md:118).\n\n---\n\n### **CRITICAL HARD RULES (Cross-cutting, Non-Negotiable)**\n\nEvery wave encodes these **CC1–CC7** rules (STAGE1-MASTER-PLAN.md):\n\n1. **CC1 — Publisher no-leak:** Every new table declares {scrub / publish-clean / publish-with-filter} + tested in `--dry-run`. OpenRouter ToS forbids redistribution; AA data scrubbed; decisions table never published.\n2. **CC2 — Shadow before touching live:** Any collection/ingestion change runs behind shadow/dry-run (separate DB, read-only prod, cost-capped, off cron) until shadow diff is reviewed.\n3. **CC3 — Honest n:** No metric rate below n<30; show raw counts + window + sample_size; name the open-loop state.\n4. **CC4 — Read-only KB:** Except new `decisions` / `feedback` / benchmark-score tables. Never read `.env`. Never run the delete step in `migrate_to_kind_paper`.\n5. **CC5 — Provenance at write:** Benchmark/model cells carry NOT-NULL `source` + `license` + `as_of` + `self_reported`; null license = write reject.\n6. **CC6 — Report-first delivery:** Every North-Star deliverable ships in the morning report / weekly email first; dashboard is optional drill-down.\n7. **CC7 — Reuse, don't rebuild:** Evolve the `dashboard/` package + `kb/aurora.db` schema. No wholesale rebuild (AuroraTwo verdict: \"evolve, don't rebuild\").\n\n---\n\n### **PROJECT HEALTH SIGNAL**\n\n| Dimension | Status | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Planning & Design** | ✅ CONVERGED | Crucible Stage 0/1 locked + approved; Stage 2 doc-trio foreman-ready. |\n| **Core Discovery Pipeline** | ✅ WORKING | Nightly sweeps 01:07–06:47, KB at ~350+ artifacts, publisher pushes to `aurora-library`. |\n| **Architecture Execution** | ✅ IN PROGRESS | W1–W5 awareness revamp complete (2026-06-12); all tests green; schema applied overnight (2026-06-13). |\n| **Value Realization** | 🟡 EARLY STAGE | Wave 1 surfaces models (live); W2 sources in shadow only; W3 benchmarks ready but data-empty; W4 health live; W5 decisions capture live. **No wait-time — ready for John's go/no-go on W2 promotion.** |\n| **Adoption Metrics** | 🟡 BOOTSTRAP | n=7 live decisions (need ≥30 for automation); 6 HH loads, 1 dismiss. Open-loop state explicitly named (CC3). |\n| **Cost Accountability** | ✅ INSTRUMENTED | Pricing.yaml, cost_telemetry live; Wave 4 shows cost-per-useful-find (all metrics n-gated). |\n| **The \"Dying Quietly\" Risk** | 🟡 MITIGATED | Report-first design (Wave 4) + weekly email (Wave 3) + honest value framing (Wave 4) + one-click label capture (W1/W5) = structural guardrails against irrelevance. |\n\n---\n\n### **IMMEDIATE NEXT STEPS (Per EXECUTION-LOG.md, end of W5)**\n\n1. **John's Go/No-Go on Wave 2 Promotion:** Shadow diff is reviewable; promotion to cron is a documented manual gate.\n2. **Epoch Ingester Activation:** Wave 3 is complete and tested; running the ingester populates `model_benchmarks` and lights up best-for-X cards.\n3. **Weight Validation (future, post-n≥30 labels):** Frontier_score weights validated against John's liked/rejected labels before the ranker goes live in the morning report.\n4. **Helping Hand Automation (future, post-n≥30 labels):** Full adoption automation gated behind a separate Crucible or foreman run once the label set is large enough.\n\n---\n\n**In short:** Aurora is currently underperforming its North Star (agentic-AI awareness instrument), but the **entire trajectory from Revamp → Quality → Awareness reflects a clear, research-backed reframing**, not drift. All five waves of the awareness revamp are **complete and tested**. The system is ready for John's **data-informed go/no-go decisions** on collection retargeting (W2) and usage signals (W5 label accrual). No critical blocker. The design is honest about bootstrap problems (n=7, open-loop metrics) and structurally guards against quiet failure (report-first, weekly email, hard n-gates)."}],"resolvedModel":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","totalDurationMs":110406,"totalTokens":82030,"totalToolUseCount":26,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6780,"cache_read_input_tokens":70396,"output_tokens":4848,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6780},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":4848,"cache_read_input_tokens":70396,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6780,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6780,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":16,"searchCount":5,"bashCount":5,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
