{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ACwxJodXAE6No2Hnb7B6TY","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have gathered comprehensive information. Let me compile the architectural report:\n\n## Aurora Codebase: Rigorous Architectural Map\n\n### CORE PYTHON SYSTEM\n\n---\n\n## 1. **orchestrator.py** — Sweep Entry Point\n\n**File:** `C:\\dev\\aurora\\orchestrator.py`\n**Lines:** 1,456\n**Functions:** 32 named functions\n\n#### Entry Point & CLI Interface\n```\nUsage: python -m aurora.orchestrator --sweep {skills,tools,agents,models}\n       --dry-run    # Walk pipeline, no LLM calls\n       --no-swarm   # Skip runner+critics (static-only mode)\n       --retarget-shadow  # Fixture-only shadow runs\n```\n\n#### Pipeline Architecture (8 stages)\n\nThe `walk_pipeline()` function (line 614) implements the core orchestration:\n\n1. **[0/8] Embeddings drain** — `embedder.drain_pending()` — clears stuck embedding queue\n2. **[2/8] Scout → fetch** — `scout.fan_out()` discovers seeds; `source_reputation.compute_yield()` yields prioritization\n3. **[2.5/8] Discovery queue flush** — `scout.drain_discovery_queue()` (max 200/sweep) \n4. **[3/8] Quarantine wrap** — `quarantine_role.wrap()` — sandboxes fetched content\n5. **[3.5/8] Sanitizer pass** — `sanitizer_role.sanitize()` — PromptArmor-style injection scrubbing (Haiku, cost-metered)\n6. **[4/8] Static screener** — `static_screener.screen()` — cheap heuristic filter\n7. **[5/8] Split & swarm** — Top-K (default 2, env `AURORA_SWARM_TOP_K`) → full swarm; tail → static-only\n8. **[6/8] Swarm loop** — **runner** → **critic_a + critic_b** → **critic_c** (optional third family) → **reconciler**\n9. **[7/8] Embed + file** — `embedder.run()` + `librarian.upsert_artifact()`\n\n**Async dispatch:** Runners/critics run via `asyncio.run()` but individual role functions are synchronous.\n\n#### Key Subsystems\n\n**Cost Tracking (Bucket J4, O-12)**\n- Per-sweep cap: `PER_SWEEP_BUDGET_USD = MONTHLY_CAPS[\"anthropic\"] / 30 / 3 = $0.55/sweep`\n- Per-role cells (proportional): runner 35%, critics_a/b/c 15/15/5%, reconciler 10%, etc.\n- Functions: `_sweep_cost_so_far()`, `_role_cost_so_far()`, `_role_budget_exceeded()` (line 98-123)\n- If exceeded: skip remaining candidates, mark run as `'partial'`\n\n**Batch Sweep Mode (Wave L6, default OFF)**\n- `batch_sweep_enabled()` returns False unless env set\n- When ON: pre-collect critic_a Anthropic calls → submit as Message Batch (50% discount) → prefetch text\n- Metered via `batch_sweep.submit_critic_a_batch()` with per-item failure degrade path\n\n**Evidence Loop (Wave 2/H2)**\n- `_select_shadow_score_fn()` (line 150) picks score function:\n  - **DEFAULT (PRIMARY):** `evidence.make_precomputed_score_fn()` — replays legacy verdict (ZERO new LLM cost)\n  - **LIVE-RESCORE (opt-in via `AURORA_EVIDENCE_LIVE_RESCORE=1`):** `evidence.make_live_score_fn()` — metered under \"evidence_shadow\" cell\n- Verdict adoption gated by `_verdict_is_more_lenient()` (line 126) — only adopt if stricter\n\n**Lock & Heartbeat (Bucket O-10)**\n- v2: JSON payload `{pid, last_heartbeat_unix}`\n- Daemon thread updates heartbeat; staleness detected by next run\n- Path: `C:\\dev\\aurora\\lock\\sweep.lock`\n\n**Degrade Counter (Bucket G4)**\n- Global `_DEGRADE_COUNT[run_id]` — incremented when Sonnet/Gemini fall back to Haiku\n- Read + cleared at run close via `get_and_clear_degrade_count()`\n- Triggers `runs.status = 'partial'`\n\n#### Main Control Flow (line 1281)\n\n```python\ndef main():\n  args = parse(--sweep, --dry-run, --no-swarm, --retarget-shadow, --providers, --top-k)\n  \n  if args.retarget_shadow:\n    return _run_retarget_shadow(cfg, ...)  # Returns BEFORE live-run open\n  \n  with sweep_lock():\n    conn = _connect_with_fallback(DB_PATH)\n    run_id = open_run(...)\n    \n    if cfg.name == \"models\":\n      notes = asyncio.run(walk_models_pipeline(...))\n    else:\n      notes = asyncio.run(walk_pipeline(...))\n    \n    advisor_role.run_advisor(conn, run_id)  # Wave-C: lit_reviewer → advisor\n    \n    # Close run with status: 'dry_run' | 'partial' | 'ok' | 'failed'\n    close_run(conn, run_id, status=final_status, notes=notes)\n    write_summary(REPORTS_ROOT, ...)\n```\n\n#### Error Handling & Telemetry\n\n- **Fail-open patterns:** 9 places with `except Exception as e: log.warning(...)` (BLE001 no-block semantics)\n  - Scout yield (line 649), evidence loop (898), sanitizer persist (605), taste score (991)\n  - Never breaks the sweep; degradation surface in final `runs.notes`\n  \n- **Final exception handler (line 1446):** Catches any unhandled exception, closes run as `'failed'`, returns exit code 1\n\n#### Code Smells & Observations\n\n1. **Global mutable state** — `_BUDGET_EXCEEDED` and `_DEGRADE_COUNT` dicts (lines 177, 97 in llm.py)\n   - Pattern: set in pipeline, popped at close\n   - **Risk:** If close_run() never executes (process crash), state persists into next run\n   - **Mitigated by:** Finally block (line 1450) ensures `_close_with_fallback(conn)`\n\n2. **Timestamp inconsistency** — Mixed use of `datetime.now(timezone.utc)` vs naive `datetime.now()`\n   - All `recorded_at` values use `.isoformat()` from UTC now (llm.py:312)\n   - But seed_map/prompt SHAs are untracked (line 108-109, stored as TEXT columns)\n\n3. **Hardcoded environment variables** — 12+ env keys consumed\n   - `AURORA_SWEEP_TOP_K`, `AURORA_DISCOVERY_DRAIN_MAX`, `AURORA_SWARM_TOP_K`, `AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP`, `AURORA_EVIDENCE_LIVE_RESCORE`, `AURORA_DRAIN_MAX_ITEMS`, `AURORA_SCOUT_BUDGET`, `AURORA_DISABLE_GEMINI`, `AURORA_ENGINE`, etc.\n   - No centralized registry; scattered throughout\n\n4. **Missing validation** — Model pipeline args `--providers` (line 1349) is a comma-separated list parsed inline with no validation that provider names are known\n   - Silent no-op if typo in provider name\n\n5. **Unreachable code path deleted** — Line 669-679 comment: \"drained discovery_queue rows are... never a link-list README (no re-fetch happens here). A drain-time re-enqueue branch was thus unreachable ... and has been removed\"\n   - Indicates prior dead code; keep this pattern in mind for regression testing\n\n---\n\n## 2. **llm.py** — LLM Call Funnel\n\n**File:** `C:\\dev\\aurora\\llm.py`\n**Lines:** ~2,200 (82,999 bytes)\n**Functions:** 54 named functions\n**Imports:** anthropic, google.generativeai, openai (DeepSeek/Groq), tenacity\n\n#### Retry Architecture (Bucket G1, O-23)\n\n**Transient Error Classifiers:**\n- `_is_retryable_anthropic()` (line 36) — timeouts, 429/5xx/529\n- `_is_retryable_genai()` (line 47) — ServiceUnavailable, timeout, rate-limit keywords\n\n**Retry Config (Wave L5, O-23):**\n```python\n_RETRY_KW = dict(\n    wait=wait_exponential_jitter(initial=1, max=60),\n    stop=stop_after_attempt(5) | stop_after_delay(60),  # NEW: max 60s wall-clock\n    reraise=True,\n    before_sleep=before_sleep_log(...)\n)\nHAIKU_FALLBACK_DEADLINE_S = 120.0  # Outer wall-clock (60s + 60s = 120s worst case)\n```\n\n- Decorator `@retry(retry=retry_if_exception(_is_retryable_*), **_RETRY_KW)` on:\n  - `_anthropic_create()` (line 83)\n  - `_gemini_generate()` (line 88)\n\n#### Cost Recording System\n\n**`CostRecorder` class (line 257):**\n\n```python\ndef record(self, vendor, model, tokens_in, tokens_out,\n           cache_read_tokens=0, cache_write_tokens=0, batch_mode=False) -> float:\n  # (1) Look up in_rate / out_rate from pricing.yaml\n  # (2) Compute base usd = tokens_in/1M * in_rate + tokens_out/1M * out_rate\n  # (3) Wave L1: add cache spend if present\n  #     cache_usd = cache_read_tokens/1M * cache_read_rate + cache_write_tokens/1M * cache_write_rate\n  # (4) Wave L1: apply batch discount if batch_mode=True\n  #     usd *= batch_discount(pricing)  # ~0.5x multiplier\n  # (5) INSERT into costs table (includes cache/batch columns)\n  # (6) return usd_estimate\n```\n\n**Price sources:**\n- `kb/pricing.yaml` (line 32) — single YAML file, ~100 lines\n  - `vendors.anthropic.*`, `vendors.gemini.*`, `vendors.deepseek.*`, `vendors.groq.*`\n  - Per-model: `tokens_in_per_million_usd`, `tokens_out_per_million_usd`\n  - Wave L1 additions: `cache_read_per_million_usd` (~0.1x input), `cache_write_per_million_usd` (~1.25x input)\n  - Wave L5 addition: `tokenizer_factor` (1.35 for Opus 4.8, accounting for 35% more tokens)\n\n**WARNING: Cost-Audit Finding (2026-06-05)**\n- Gemini embedding path recorded `models/gemini-embedding-2` but pricing.yaml keyed it without `models/` prefix\n- `lookup_rates()` (line 126) now strips prefix **but** this was the root cause of silent $0 charges\n- Every embedding was priced at $0 for an entire month, making `gemini_mtd` reporting fictional\n- **Fixed via:** `lookup_rates()` strips `models/` prefix and warns once per (vendor, model) pair (line 144)\n\n#### Default Models (pricing.yaml, line 79-100)\n\n```yaml\ndefault_models:\n  scout:       gemini / gemini-3.5-flash\n  runner:      anthropic / claude-sonnet-4-6\n  critic_a:    anthropic / claude-sonnet-4-6\n  critic_b:    gemini / gemini-2.5-flash-lite (Wave G2: swapped from Sonnet)\n  critic_c:    [DeepSeek / Groq] (third-family judge)\n  reconciler:  anthropic / claude-sonnet-4-6\n  embedder:    gemini / gemini-3.5-flash\n  librarian:   gemini / gemini-3.5-flash\n```\n\n#### Structured Outputs (Wave L3)\n\n**Not a full schema system — a tool-use workaround:**\n```python\ndef call_anthropic(..., output_schema=None):\n  if output_schema:\n    # (1) Build a single tool named \"emit_result\"\n    # (2) Set tool's input_schema = output_schema\n    # (3) Force tool_choice = {\"type\":\"tool\", \"name\":\"emit_result\"}\n    # (4) Set strict=true (Anthropic API guarantees schema compliance)\n    # (5) Parse resp.content[].input as JSON, serialize back to string\n    # (6) Return that JSON string (caller does json.loads(...) as before)\n  # On no tool_use block: return \"\"\n  # Fallback to Haiku carries same output_schema, so both paths are schema-guaranteed\n```\n\n**Implementation:** `_structured_text_from_resp()` (line 532), `_STRUCTURED_TOOL_NAME = \"emit_result\"` (line 435)\n\n#### Prompt Caching Gate (Wave L2)\n\n**Problem:** Anthropic caching only activates for cached prefixes ≥ model-specific minimum (1024–4096 tokens). Smaller prefixes trigger silent no-op (no error, no warning).\n\n**Solution:** `cache_prefix_clears_minimum(system, model)` (line 390)\n- Estimates system prefix size as `len(text) // 4` (chars-per-token)\n- `MODEL_CACHE_MIN_TOKENS` dict (line 351) per-model minimums\n- Only attach `cache_control` marker if prefix clears threshold\n\n**Status:** Prefixes are currently small (~170 tokens), so caching is a **documented no-op**. Plumbing is correct and ready for larger prompts.\n\n#### Model Defaults & Globals\n\n```python\nHAIKU_DEFAULT = \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\"    # fallback model\nGEMINI_DEFAULT = \"gemini-3.5-flash\"            # scout/embedder default\n```\n\n#### Adaptive Thinking (Wave L4)\n\n**Replaces deprecated `budget_tokens`:**\n```python\n# OLD (deprecated, removed on Opus 4.8):\nthinking={\"type\":\"enabled\", \"budget_tokens\":5000}\n\n# NEW (adaptive):\nthinking={\"type\":\"adaptive\"}\noutput_config={\"effort\":\"low|medium|high|xhigh|max\"}\n```\n\n**Guard:** `_assert_no_budget_tokens(kw)` (line 478) — raises AssertionError if deprecated key found anywhere in request dict. Runs immediately before every `_anthropic_create()` call.\n\n**Thinking token metering:** `_fold_thinking_into_output()` (line 500) — probes for separately-reported thinking fields (`output_thinking_tokens`, `reasoning_tokens`, etc.) and adds to metered output if present.\n\n#### Call Functions (Models & Error Handling)\n\n| Function | Provider | Default Model | Retry | Fallback |\n|----------|----------|---------------|-------|----------|\n| `call_anthropic()` | Anthropic | Sonnet 4.6 | Yes (5 attempts, 60s) | Haiku (once) |\n| `call_gemini()` | Google | Gemini 3.5 Flash | Yes | (none; raises) |\n| `call_gemini_embedding()` | Google | text-embedding-004 or gemini-embedding-2 | (no retry) | (none; raises) |\n| `call_deepseek()` | DeepSeek (OpenAI-compat) | deepseek-chat | No | Returns `ProviderResult(status='error', ...)` |\n| `call_groq()` | Groq (OpenAI-compat) | llama-3.3-70b-versatile | No | Returns `ProviderResult(status='error', ...)` |\n\n**call_anthropic signature (line 546):**\n```python\ndef call_anthropic(prompt, *, model=None, max_tokens=600,\n                   cost_recorder=None, role_hint=\"anthropic\", system=None,\n                   cache_system=False, output_schema=None, effort=None) -> str\n```\n\n**call_gemini signature (line 1053):**\n```python\ndef call_gemini(prompt, *, model=None, max_tokens=600,\n                cost_recorder=None, role_hint=\"gemini\", system=None) -> str\n```\n\n#### Per-Call Metering\n\nEvery call that runs records via `cost_recorder.record(vendor, model, tokens_in, tokens_out, ...)`:\n```python\nresp = _anthropic_create(client, ...)\ncost_recorder.record(\"anthropic\", model, \n                     resp.usage.input_tokens,\n                     _fold_thinking_into_output(resp.usage),\n                     cache_read_tokens=resp.usage.cache_read_input_tokens,\n                     cache_write_tokens=resp.usage.cache_creation_input_tokens,\n                     batch_mode=was_batched)\n```\n\n#### Disabled Feature: Gemini Kill-Switch\n\n**`gemini_disabled()` (line 403)**\n- Returns True if `AURORA_DISABLE_GEMINI=1` (May 2026 cost-audit workaround)\n- When True: all Gemini chat calls degrade to Anthropic Haiku; embeddings skipped\n- Prevents topped-up key from silently resuming Gemini spend\n\n#### Code Smells & Missing Features\n\n1. **No explicit batching API (Wave L6 only for critic_a)** — orchestrator pre-submits Anthropic critic_a batch via `batch_sweep.submit_critic_a_batch()`, but other roles are synchronous\n   - Reconciler + security judge have batch helpers in `batch_sweep.py` but are not wired into nightly cron\n\n2. **Cost-audit unresolved edge cases** — pricing.yaml has verification flags (`verified: false`) on:\n   - Gemini 3.5 Flash (estimate, no published SKU)\n   - Gemini Embedding (estimate)\n   - text-embedding-004 (legacy, estimate)\n   - Batch discount 0.5 (estimate)\n   - All flagged but not actively validated during runs\n\n3. **No prompt-caching setup** — system prefix is marked `cache_system=True` in some calls but:\n   - Prefixes are too small (~170 tokens) so gate always returns False\n   - Marker never attached to real requests\n   - Zero cache benefit today; code is ready for future\n\n4. **Tokenizer factor (1.35) is estimate-only** — used in `estimate_usd()` (line 231) for pre-call budgeting but:\n   - **Ground-truth invariant** (line 286): `CostRecorder.record()` uses REAL `resp.usage` counts, never applies factor\n   - If pre-call estimate undershoots by 35%, sweep can exceed per-role cells\n   - **Not a bug** (by design) but creates estimation→reality gap for Opus 4.8\n\n5. **Gemini thinking tokens** — `_fold_thinking_into_output()` line 500 looks for separate thinking-token fields but:\n   - Gemini's `thoughts_token_count` is already in the usage shape\n   - No evidence field names will change; future-proofing is defensive\n\n---\n\n## 3. **publisher.py** — Snapshot Build & Push\n\n**File:** `C:\\dev\\aurora\\publisher.py`\n**Lines:** ~1,240 (39,993 bytes)\n**Functions:** 18 named functions\n**Entrypoint:** `python -m aurora.publisher` (runs after agents sweep, 01:45 daily)\n\n#### Workflow\n\n1. **Open live aurora.db** (read-only + pragmas)\n2. **Build scrubbed snapshot** — copy schema, apply security gate, strip transcripts/bundles, filter model_benchmarks by license\n3. **Generate CHANGELOG** entry for today\n4. **Stage explicit allowlist** of paths to `_publish/` tree\n5. **Git commit + tag YYYYMMDD** + **push to aurora-library repo** (unless `--dry-run`)\n\n#### Security Gate (Bucket C C3, §4.2)\n\n**Single-owner enforcement point #3:** `_security_gate_clause()` (line 70)\n```python\ndef _security_gate_clause(table_alias=\"a\") -> str:\n    return gate.enforcement_clause(table_alias)\n```\nDelegates to `roles/security/gate.py` — the **single source of truth** for servable SQL predicate.\n\n**Enforcement points (§4.2, 4 total):**\n1. Snapshot SELECT (orchestrator.py walk_pipeline)\n2. Snapshot SELECT (this file, line 70)\n3. Copytree filter (line 108)\n4. MCP server\n\n**Model Benchmarks Special Handling (Wave CC1, line 54-62):**\n```python\nALLOWED_BENCHMARK_LICENSES = (\"CC-BY-4.0\", \"Apache-2.0\")\nEXCLUDED_BENCHMARK_SOURCES = (\"artificial-analysis\", \"openrouter\")\n```\n\nPublisher deletes every `model_benchmarks` cell that:\n- Is NULL license\n- Is not in `ALLOWED_BENCHMARK_LICENSES`\n- Has source in `EXCLUDED_BENCHMARK_SOURCES` (redistributable-restricted)\n\nThen runs VACUUM to shrink file.\n\n#### Staged Paths (Explicit Allowlist)\n\nOnly these paths are committed:\n- `kb-snapshot.sqlite` (the scrubbed KB)\n- `CHANGELOG.md` (new entry for today)\n- `library/` (full copytree of live library/)\n\n**NOT staged:**\n- Transcripts (removed from snapshot)\n- Artifact bundles (removed from snapshot)\n- `ranking_diffs` table (shadow diagnostics, SCRUBBED before VACUUM)\n- Any retired artifacts\n\n#### Key Functions\n\n**`_artifact_is_servable_in_snapshot(conn, slug)` (line 77)**\n- Checks if artifact's most recent row passes gate\n- Returns True in shadow/off mode (calibration data flows)\n- Wave 2 (E20): **retired artifacts NEVER ship**, checked BEFORE security mode early-return\n\n**`build_snapshot(db_path, snapshot_path)` (line 280)**\n- Opens live DB, copies schema\n- Applies security gate on SELECT\n- Strips transcripts / bundles\n- Filters model_benchmarks by license\n- WAL→journal mode flip (VACUUM requires)\n\n**`generate_changelog(db_path, path)` (line 350)**\n- Queries latest run artifacts by kind\n- Lists new skills/tools/agents/models discovered\n- Writes markdown to `CHANGELOG.md`\n\n**`copy_library_filtered(library_root, dst_dir)` (line 390)**\n- Recursive copytree through `library/<kind>/<slug>/`\n- Skip filter: `_artifact_is_servable_in_snapshot()` per slug\n- Preserves directory structure\n\n#### Git Integration\n\n**Credential flow (Bucket F3):**\n- Expects `GITHUB_PAT` + `GITHUB_REPO` env vars\n- `git commit` + `git tag YYYYMMDD` + `git push origin --tags`\n- Subprocess calls via `subprocess.run(..., check=True)`\n\n**Dry-run mode (`--dry-run`):**\n```\nShows staged tree without committing. Useful for:\n  python -m aurora.publisher --dry-run\n```\n\n#### Code Smells & Observations\n\n1. **Subprocess.run with check=True (line 460+)** — Unhandled `CalledProcessError` if git fails\n   - No try/except wrapper; process dies mid-push\n   - `--dry-run` prevents this in practice, but live mode has no rollback\n\n2. **Hardcoded snapshot name** — `SNAPSHOT_NAME = \"kb-snapshot.sqlite\"` (line 52)\n   - No version field; overwrites previous daily push\n   - Archive strategy unspecified (never versioned, only latest)\n\n3. **License filter coupling** — `ALLOWED_BENCHMARK_LICENSES` / `EXCLUDED_BENCHMARK_SOURCES` hardcoded (line 61-62)\n   - Policy lives here, not in gate.py\n   - Inconsistent with security gate's single-owner pattern (gate.py owns the rest of servability)\n\n4. **No cleanup of failed runs** — Publisher runs even if prior sweep was `'partial'` or `'failed'`\n   - Publishes stale KB if sweeps are degraded but push still succeeds\n   - No validation that KB was \"good\" before snapshot\n\n5. **Pragma mutations** — Line 332 flips `journal_mode = WAL` → `PRAGMA journal_mode = DELETE` before VACUUM\n   - Necessary (VACUUM incompatible with WAL) but no guard if flip fails\n   - Live DB is read-only so flip is safe, but staging DB could leak\n\n---\n\n## 4. **dashboard/** — Read-Only Flask UI (Port 5001)\n\n**Directory:** `C:\\dev\\aurora\\dashboard\\`\n**Key modules:** `web/blueprint.py`, `data/{catalog,reports,health,costs,models,db}.py`\n\n#### Route Surface (blueprint.py, line 24)\n\n| Route | Handler | Data Source | Notes |\n|-------|---------|-------------|-------|\n| `/api/health` | `api_health()` | kb, reports | Runs + noise + backfills + rejects + logs |\n| `/api/health/summary` | `api_health_summary()` | KB + CC3 metrics | Value/health aggregate (graceful 200 on error) |\n| `/api/health/detail` | `api_health_detail()` | KB detail | Drill-down for noise/rejects/backfill/logs |\n| `/api/fingerprint` | `api_fingerprint()` | Watched paths | Detect KB freshness |\n| `/api/morning` | `api_morning()` | latest_summary.json | Morning briefing snapshot |\n| `/api/sweeps` | `api_sweeps()` | reports/<kind>/ | Available sweep dates |\n| `/api/sweep/<kind>/<date>` | `api_sweep_detail()` | reports/<kind>/<date>/ | Per-sweep \"what was new\" |\n| `/api/catalog/*` | `api_catalog_*()` | KB (read-only) | Artifacts, models, counts |\n| Static assets | Flask static serving | dashboard-static/ | HTML/CSS/JS |\n\n#### Data Layer (data/*.py)\n\n**db.py** — SQLite read-only connection pool\n**reports.py** — Read morning_summary, briefing_note, weekly digest\n**catalog.py** — Skills/tools/agents/models counts + filtering\n**health.py** — Run status, noise summary, backfill audits, link health\n**models.py** — `USABLE_MODEL_PREDICATE` (single reusable junk filter for all model surfaces)\n**costs.py** — Budget rollups per role/vendor\n\n#### Latest Summary JSON Structure (reports/morning/latest_summary.json)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"date\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\",\n  \"productivity_index\": 0.238,\n  \"productivity_index_status\": \"ok|warning|critical\",\n  \"productivity_index_window\": \"all-time|30-day|7-day\",\n  \"productivity_index_sample_size\": 21,\n  \"costs\": {\n    \"anthropic_mtd\": 22.034652,\n    \"gemini_mtd\": 0.0022862\n  },\n  \"finds\": {\n    \"skills\": 49,\n    \"tools\": 212,\n    \"agents\": 46\n  },\n  \"finds_new\": {\n    \"skills\": 0,\n    \"tools\": 1,\n    \"agents\": 1\n  },\n  \"upgrades\": [],\n  \"confidence_badges\": {\n    \"lossy\": 2,\n    \"verified\": 16\n  },\n  \"source_quality\": {\n    \"high\": 254,\n    \"low\": 129,\n    \"medium\": 33,\n    \"new\": 2\n  },\n  \"top_finds\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"slug\",\n      \"kind\": \"skill|tool|agent\",\n      \"why\": \"one-line human rationale\",\n      \"quality\": \"verified|lossy · {count}★\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n#### Notes on Data Freshness\n\n- Blueprint opens KB in read-only mode with `busy_timeout=5000` (line 36)\n- Reports are static JSON files (never live-queried)\n- Dashboard never writes; briefing process owns latest_summary.json generation\n- Stale detection via `freshness.fingerprint()` (file mtimes on watched paths)\n\n#### Code Smells\n\n1. **Graceful error handling is overly broad** — `api_health_summary()` (line 69) catches `Exception` and returns `{\"ok\": true, \"alerts\": [], \"signals\": {}, \"degraded\": \"...\"}` with no detail\n   - Hides bugs; should narrow exception types\n\n2. **No pagination on catalog routes** — `/api/catalog/artifacts` returns full artifact list with no limit\n   - Could be 307+ rows; no filtering by kind/status\n\n3. **Hard dependency on directory structure** — `reports/<kind>/<date>/` layout is implicit\n   - No schema validation; renames break routes silently\n\n---\n\n## 5. **kb/** — SQLite Knowledge Base\n\n**Schema:** `kb/schema.sql` (206 lines base; migrations in `kb/migrations/`)\n**Pricing:** `kb/pricing.yaml`\n**Apply:** `kb/apply_schema.py`, `kb/migrate.py`\n\n#### Core Tables (schema.sql)\n\n| Table | Purpose | Columns (key) | Indexed |\n|-------|---------|---------------|---------|\n| `artifacts` | Canonical skill/tool/agent/model/paper | slug, sweep, kind, security_status, interest_score, frontier_score | slug, canonical_url, security_status |\n| `aliases` | URL→artifact mapping | artifact_id, observed_url | artifact_id |\n| `sources` | Provenance per artifact | artifact_id, url, excerpt, title, extraction_offsets | artifact_id |\n| `runs` | Nightly sweep metadata | sweep, started_at, status, budget_tokens_in/out, critic_c_status/calls/errors | sweep, started_at |\n| `validations` | Cheap-pass + swarm verdicts | artifact_id, run_id, stage, verdict, score, transcript_path | artifact_id, run_id |\n| `embeddings` | Hierarchical placement | artifact_id, domain_path, domain_depth, complexity_rank | artifact_id |\n| `neural_plasticity` | Agent learning metadata | what_learns, learning_signal, memory_model, failure_modes | (none) |\n| `costs` | Per-call LLM spend | run_id, role, vendor, model_id, tokens_in/out, usd_estimate, cache_read_tokens, cache_write_tokens, batch_mode | run_id, vendor/recorded_at |\n| `models` | Model catalog | provider, family, version, price_in_usd_per_mtok, context_in_tokens, ... | (none listed) |\n| `hh_events` | Helping Hand telemetry | session_id, slug, outcome (surfaced/loaded/dismissed/no_match_judged/abandoned), score, rank | recorded_at, slug, session_id |\n| `ranking_diffs` | Shadow-vs-legacy ranker diagnostics | run_or_date, artifact_id, legacy_rank, shadow_rank, legacy_score, shadow_score, frontier_score | run_or_date, artifact_id |\n| `model_benchmarks` | Benchmark scores + license | artifact_id, benchmark_name, score, license, source | (none listed) |\n| `decision_trees` | Advisor-generated guidance | artifact_id, tree_json, decision_class | artifact_id |\n\n#### Migrations (kb/migrations/*.sql, idempotent)\n\nNumbered 0001–0017+ (lexical order). Each file records target `schema_version` and applies atomically. `migrate.py` (line 59) applies any pending, then reconciles via `_reconcile_add_columns()` (line 72) to re-apply all `ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN` declarations (closes rebuild-drops-later-columns hole, Wave C D-fix).\n\n#### Schema Versioning\n\n- Base schema.sql = v3, inserts (v3, v31, v32, v33, ...)\n- Migration table: `schema_version(version, applied_at)`\n- Idempotent: `INSERT OR IGNORE INTO schema_version` prevents re-application\n\n#### Pragmas (orchestrator._ensure_schema, line 520+)\n\n```sql\nPRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\nPRAGMA journal_mode = WAL;        -- Write-ahead log (durability)\nPRAGMA busy_timeout = 5000;        -- Briefing read-only mode\n```\n\n#### Code Smells\n\n1. **No explicit column constraints on behavior** — Most columns are NOT NULL, but some are nullable:\n   - `security_status`, `security_scanned_arf_version` start NULL (unscanned = non-servable, fail-closed)\n   - No CHECK constraint to validate security_status ∈ {'pass', 'flag', 'reject'}\n\n2. **Transcripts stored as file paths, not content** — `validations.transcript_path` is a local file reference\n   - Publisher deletes `transcript_path` before snapshot (line 316) but relies on caller to clean up actual files\n   - No cleanup job; transcripts accumulate in disk\n\n3. **Artifact bundles never documented** — `validations.artifact_bundle_path` is similarly a file reference\n   - Not mentioned in schema docstring\n   - Unclear retention policy\n\n4. **Seed map snapshot is a BLOB** — `runs.seed_map_snapshot` stores binary pickle/msgpack\n   - No indication of serialization format or version\n   - No deserialization helper in code\n\n---\n\n## 6. **morning_briefing.py** — Briefing Renderer (08:30 daily)\n\n**File:** `C:\\dev\\aurora\\morning_briefing.py`\n**Lines:** ~2,100\n**Functions:** ~50 named functions\n**Entrypoint:** `python -m aurora.morning_briefing`\n\n#### Output\n\nWrites to `reports/morning/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md` (human-readable) and `reports/morning/latest_summary.json` (machine-readable).\n\n#### Key Blocks (in order of appearance)\n\n1. **HH Yesterday** (`_hh_yesterday()`, line 124) — Helping Hand activity for yesterday (UTC)\n   - Sessions, distinct queries, match_calls, loaded, dismissed outcomes\n   - Null if table absent or zero events\n\n2. **Models Block** (`_models_block()`, line 184) — Frontier model releases\n   - Filters out preview/deprecated/junk (via `models.py:USABLE_MODEL_PREDICATE`)\n   - Top-3 error classes from smoke tests (when enabled)\n\n3. **MoE Block** (`_moe_block()`, line 338) — Mixture-of-Experts system health\n   - Critic_c availability, DeepSeek/Groq status\n   - Checks for key presence, not network status (best-effort)\n\n4. **Top Finds** (`_top_finds()`, line 459) — De-noised, ranked top 5 new artifacts\n   - **Filters:**\n     - NOT arxiv (unless explicitly curated)\n     - NOT vendor marketing (developer.nvidia.com denylist)\n     - Interest-scored; ranked by freshness + interest + usage modifier\n   - **Usage modifier** (`_usage_modifiers_by_slug()`, line 68) — ±0.10 per loaded/dismissed via HH telemetry, 30-day half-life, tanh squash\n\n5. **Suggestion Adoption** (`_suggestion_adoption()`, line 666) — Curator acceptance rate on offered decisions\n   - New decisions vs accepted vs rejected (per kind)\n\n6. **Momentum Block** (`_momentum_block()`, line 761) — Productivity index (Bucket I2, 2026-05-20)\n   - Formula: (new artifacts) / (artifacts scanned) over a sliding window\n   - Window: all-time | 30-day | 7-day (picks best window with ≥5 samples)\n   - Status: ok (>20%) | warning (10–20%) | critical (<10%)\n\n7. **Decisions Block** (`_decisions_block()`, line 912) — Curator-recorded decisions (decision trees)\n   - Citation-grounded guidance per category\n   - Breakdown by confidence badge (verified vs lossy)\n\n8. **Decisions Counter** (`_decisions_counter()`, line 1036) — Total decisions per month/week/all-time\n\n9. **Awareness Metrics** (`_awareness_metrics()`, line 1074) — Multi-signal health dashboard\n   - n-gated metric set: Productivity Index, Alert Rate, Health Rating, etc.\n   - Shows denominator/numerator for calibration\n\n10. **Value Health Block** (`_value_health_block()`, line 1270) — CC3: multi-source value signals\n    - Frontierrank (80%), interest (10%), source quality (10%)\n    - Weighted aggregate per artifact\n\n11. **Link Health Block** (`_link_health_block()`, line 1363) — GitHub link status\n    - Stars, staleness (via weekly probes)\n    - Warns on 404 / redirect loops\n\n12. **Critic_c Rollup** (`_critic_c_rollup()`, line 1431) — Third-judge performance\n    - Call counts, error rates, abstain counts per run\n    - Surfaces degraded mode (no Groq key, rate-limited, etc.)\n\n13. **Security Block** (`_security_block()`, line 1479) — Scan status, threat distribution\n    - Counts by security_status (pass/flag/reject)\n    - Top threat classes\n\n14. **Frameworks Block** (`_frameworks_block()`, line 1555) — Integration platforms mentioned\n    - Langchain, LiteLLM, etc. (extracted from artifacts)\n\n15. **Integrations Block** (`_integrations_block()`, line 1597) — Tool/API adoption\n    - Counts of artifacts mentioning each integration\n\n16. **Telemetry Block** (`_telemetry_block()`, line 1637) — KB size, artifact counts\n    - Per-kind breakdown\n\n17. **Synthesis Block** (`_synthesis_block()`, line 1695) — Thematic summary (written by advisor)\n    - Single paragraph per daily_syntheses record\n\n18. **Confidence Block** (`_confidence_block()`, line 1705) — Tag-based confidence scoring\n    - High/medium/low confidence badges\n\n19. **Source Quality Block** (`_source_quality_block()`, line 1722) — Source reputation summary\n    - High/medium/low/new source counts\n\n#### DB Connection (Bucket O-11)\n\n```python\ndef _open_ro() -> sqlite3.Connection:\n    conn = sqlite3.connect(f\"file:{DB_PATH}?mode=ro\", uri=True)\n    conn.execute(\"PRAGMA busy_timeout=5000\")  # Wait 5s on locked DB\n    return conn\n```\n\nRead-only mode with timeout prevents briefing from stalling/write-locking a live sweep.\n\n#### Code Smells & Missing\n\n1. **Circular query dependency** — `_top_finds()` (line 459) queries artifacts, interest_score, hh_events, validations, sources\n   - Runs serially in a single transaction; no query optimization hints\n   - O(n) iteration over results to apply filters\n\n2. **Hardcoded Unicode replacement** — Line 42: `_REPLACEMENT_CHAR = \"​\"` (U+FFFD) stripped from why-lines\n   - Interim fix for encoding corruption; no test case documented\n\n3. **Missing \"why\" field validation** — No check that `short_description` is non-empty before using it (line 379)\n   - Can surface null or whitespace as why-line\n\n4. **No aggregation efficiency** — Every metric block re-queries the same tables independently\n   - `_decisions_counter()`, `_decisions_block()`, `_decisions_suggestion()` all hit decision_trees\n   - Could batch-load per kind\n\n5. **Momentum calculation undefined edge case** — `_momentum_block()` (line 761) picks window with ≥5 samples\n   - If all windows <5 samples: returns None (no block rendered)\n   - Unspecified behavior in very early KB state\n\n---\n\n## 7. **Test Coverage**\n\n**Location:** `tests/` (100+ test files)\n**Framework:** pytest\n\n#### Test Categories (by count & status)\n\n**Dashboard tests:** \n- `test_dashboard_data.py`, `test_dashboard_web.py`, `test_dashboard_health.py`, `test_dashboard_sweeps.py`, `test_dashboard_catalog.py` — All W1–W5 routes + data layer\n\n**Wave tests:**\n- `test_wave_a.py`, `test_wave_b.py`, `test_wave_c.py` — Per-wave implementation verification\n- `test_wave1_visibility.py`, `test_wave2_*.py`, `test_wave3_*.py`, `test_wave5_*.py`\n\n**Role tests:**\n- `test_critic_c.py`, `test_critic_c_cost.py`, `test_critic_c_integration.py`\n- `test_claim_verifier.py`, `test_claim_verifier_runner.py`\n- `test_batch_sweep.py`, `test_cost_cache_batch.py`\n\n**Integration tests:**\n- `test_briefing_framework_integration.py`, `test_briefing_security_block.py`\n- `test_critic_c_integration.py`\n\n**Security tests:** `tests/security/` (15+ files)\n- `test_gate.py`, `test_fetcher.py`, `test_arf.py`, `test_behavioral.py`, `test_detectors.py`, `test_ast_rules.py`, `test_red_corpus.py`, `test_benign_noisy.py`\n\n**Pricing/Cost tests:**\n- `test_pricing_keys.py`, `test_pricing_guardrails.py`, `test_pricing_quorum.py`, `test_pricing_debate_cap.py`\n\n**Unimplemented/Untested:**\n- No test for orchestrator's main lock/heartbeat logic (Bucket O-10)\n- No test for publisher git integration (subprocess.run)\n- No test for orchestrator's degrade counter / budget exceeded globals\n- **No explicit test for retryable error classification** in llm.py (Bucket G1 classifiers are tested implicitly via role tests)\n\n#### Test Patterns\n\n- Most tests are **unit tests** with fixtures (`conftest.py`)\n- Security tests use **multi-round adversarial verification** (per researchPrime style, `_round*.py` scripts)\n- Dashboard tests mock DB connections (`dashboard_fixtures.py`)\n- Integration tests spawn full pipeline on fixtures\n\n#### Coverage Gaps\n\n1. **Error paths untested** — `except Exception as e: log.warning()` patterns never exercise the exception arm\n2. **Edge cases in migration** — No test for `ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN` reconciliation logic\n3. **Hardcoded env var parsing** — No test for invalid `AURORA_SWARM_TOP_K` (non-numeric, negative, etc.)\n4. **Cost-audit sensitivity** — No test that Gemini embedding cost is recorded (the $0 bug was invisible)\n\n---\n\n## 8. **bin/ Scripts** — Scheduled & Ad-Hoc\n\n**Setup/Config:**\n- `setup-tasks.ps1` — Idempotent Windows Scheduled Tasks registration (6 daily + 2 weekly)\n- `build-plugin.py` — Builds helping-hand.plugin + helping-hand-collab.plugin (Curator vs Portable flavor)\n\n**Nightly Entry Points (via .cmd wrappers):**\n- `run-agents.cmd`, `run-skills.cmd`, `run-tools.cmd`, `run-models.cmd` → orchestrator\n- `run-morning-briefing.cmd` → morning_briefing\n- `run-state-reporter.cmd` → state_reporter (metrics rollup)\n- `run-aurora-source-push.cmd` → publisher (or source-push script)\n\n**Ad-Hoc / Shadow / Backfill:**\n- `run-evidence-shadow.py` — Metered batch re-scoring (bin/run_evidence_shadow.py)\n- `run-ranker-shadow.py` — Fixture-only frontier ranker (bin/run_ranker_shadow.py)\n- `run-security-shadow.py` — Fixture-only ARF re-run\n- `engine-diff.py` — Compares legacy vs shadow costs/verdicts\n- `noise_audit.py` — Categorizes false-positive sources\n- `weekly_digest.py` — Sunday 07:10 digest generation\n- `weekly_link_health.py` → check_link_health.py — Sunday 06:55 stargazer probe\n- Many others: backfill_*, migrate_*, ack_*, record_decision, why_does_aurora_believe, etc.\n\n#### setup-tasks.ps1 Details (line 1)\n\n**Schedule (Bucket M-1, staggered):**\n```\n01:07 — Aurora-Agents\n02:19 — Aurora-Skills\n03:41 — Aurora-Tools\n05:03 — Aurora-Models\n06:23 — Aurora-State-Reporter\n06:47 — Aurora-Morning-Briefing\n:47 (hourly) — Aurora-Source-Push\n```\n\n**Task settings (all 6 daily/hourly):**\n- `WakeToRun=True`, `StartWhenAvailable=True`\n- `RestartCount=2`, `RestartInterval=15min`\n- `ExecutionTimeLimit=1h`\n- `Principal=john`, `LogonType=S4U` (run-when-logged-off)\n- `Priority=7`\n\n**Weekly tasks (Wave 3, 2026-06-10):**\n- Aurora-Link-Health: Sunday 06:55\n- Aurora-Weekly-Digest: Sunday 07:10\n\n**Windows Update pinning:**\n```powershell\nHKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\WindowsUpdate\\UX\\Settings\n  ActiveHoursStart = 4, ActiveHoursEnd = 22, IsActiveHoursEnabled = 1\nHKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\WindowsUpdate\\AU\n  ScheduledInstallTime = 3\n```\n\n#### build-plugin.py Details\n\n**Two flavors:**\n\n1. **helping-hand.plugin (Curator)**\n   - Hard-coded venv path\n   - Hard-coded args/cwd\n   - `AURORA_KB_MODE=read_write`\n   - Located at `C:\\dev\\aurora\\` only\n\n2. **helping-hand-collab.plugin (Portable)**\n   - Command: `python` (from PATH)\n   - Args: `[\"mcp-servers/aurora-kb/server.py\"]` (relative)\n   - Env: `AURORA_KB_MODE=read_only`\n   - `AURORA_KB_PATH` omitted (server probes)\n   - Installable on any machine with Python + mcp\n\n**Build steps:**\n1. Load source plugin.json (from helping-hand-plugin/.claude-plugin/plugin.json)\n2. Annotate mcpServers entries with contextCost (H3 convention)\n3. For collab: deep copy, rewrite command/args, strip curator env vars, set read_only mode\n4. Strip UTF-8 BOM from .json/.md/.toml/.yaml/.yml/.txt (PowerShell-added U+FEFF)\n5. Build ZIP, verify plugin.json starts with `{`\n6. Output: `helping-hand.plugin` + `helping-hand-collab.plugin`\n\n---\n\n## ARCHITECTURAL SUMMARY\n\n### Data Flow Pipeline (nightly, hourly)\n\n```\n[Scheduled Task 22:00 UTC]\n  ↓\norchestrator.py --sweep agents --dry-run=False\n  ├─ [0] embeddings_pending drain (drain_cost)\n  ├─ [2] scout.fan_out(seed_map) + source_reputation.compute_yield()\n  │     (metrics: fetched, yields priority)\n  │\n  ├─ [3] quarantine wrap\n  ├─ [3.5] sanitizer (cost-metered, fail-open)\n  ├─ [4] static_screener\n  │\n  ├─ [5] Split: top-K to swarm, tail to static-only\n  │\n  ├─ [6] SWARM LOOP (per candidate)\n  │       ├─ runner → RunnerArtifact (cost-metered, Sonnet→Haiku fallback)\n  │       ├─ critic_a (Sonnet→Haiku fallback) + critic_b (Gemini)\n  │       ├─ critic_c (DeepSeek/Groq; optional third judge)\n  │       ├─ reconciler (Sonnet→Haiku fallback)\n  │       ├─ evidence.score_fn() [zero-cost precomputed default]\n  │       └─ librarian.upsert_artifact()\n  │\n  ├─ [7] embedder.run() + librarian.regenerate_indexes()\n  │\n  ├─ [8] advisor.run_advisor() [literature review + decision trees]\n  │\n  └─ close_run(status='ok'|'partial'|'failed')\n       write_summary(REPORTS_ROOT, ...)\n\n[08:30 UTC]\n  ↓\nmorning_briefing.py\n  ├─ Open aurora.db in read-only mode\n  ├─ Query: HH activity, models, critic_c health, productivity index, top finds, ...\n  └─ Write: reports/morning/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md + latest_summary.json\n\n[01:45 UTC (next day)]\n  ↓\npublisher.py\n  ├─ Build snapshot (scrubbed KB, security gate applied)\n  ├─ Generate CHANGELOG\n  ├─ Stage to _publish/\n  └─ Git commit + tag YYYYMMDD + push to aurora-library\n```\n\n### Key Invariants\n\n1. **Single point of pricing:** llm.py::CostRecorder + kb/pricing.yaml (all roles share)\n2. **Single point of security gate:** roles/security/gate.py (4 enforcement points)\n3. **Single point of model usability:** dashboard/data/models.py::USABLE_MODEL_PREDICATE\n4. **Lock/heartbeat:** Bucket O-10 prevents concurrent sweeps\n5. **Budget cells (per-role):** Proportional caps; any role exceeding marks run as 'partial'\n6. **Degrade counter:** Sonnet/Gemini→Haiku fallback counted; triggers 'partial' status\n7. **Read-only briefing:** busy_timeout=5000 prevents stalling on live sweep\n8. **Migration idempotence:** schema_version table + target-version per migration file\n\n### Missing/Incomplete (Acknowledged via Comments)\n\n1. **Structured outputs (Wave L3):** Implemented as forced tool-use workaround, not native Anthropic structured outputs\n2. **Prompt caching (Wave L2):** Plumbing correct, but prefixes too small to activate; documented no-op\n3. **Batch API (Wave L6):** Only critic_a has batch mode; reconciler/judges synchronous despite batch helpers in code\n4. **Model staleness (Wave 1):** Deferred; no `last_metadata_verified_at` threshold applied (yet)\n5. **Live evidence re-score (Wave 2/H2):** Default-OFF via `AURORA_EVIDENCE_LIVE_RESCORE=0`; shadow-only batch path in bin/run_evidence_shadow.py\n6. **Frontier ranker (Wave 2):** Shadow-only via `--retarget-shadow` flag; not on live cron path\n\n### Known Issues & Gaps\n\n1. **Cost-audit vulnerability:** Gemini embedding path can silently price at $0 if prefix missing from pricing.yaml (mitigated by warn-once per model)\n2. **Tokenizer factor (1.35) underestimate:** Pre-call estimate vs real usage can exceed role budgets; accepted trade-off (real usage is ground truth)\n3. **Unfinished transcript cleanup:** Publisher deletes transcript_path before snapshot but does not clean up actual files on disk\n4. **No validation on provider names:** `--providers anthropic,typo` silently succeeds with no-op\n5. **Subprocess failures unprepared:** publisher.py git calls can crash mid-push with no rollback\n\n### Architecture Strengths\n\n1. **Fail-open patterns:** 9+ places where transient failures never block the sweep\n2. **Per-call metering:** Every LLM call records cost in one place, enabling per-role guardrails\n3. **Idempotent migrations:** Schema can be re-applied without side effects\n4. **Read-only briefing:** Decoupled from live sweep; never blocks\n5. **Security gate single-owner:** All servability checks route through one source (roles/security/gate.py)\n6. **Retry resilience:** Tenacity full-jitter retry + Haiku fallback catches transient errors\n\n---\n\n**Report date:** 2026-06-23  \n**Codebase scope:** Aurora nightly multi-agent sweep system (~300K LOC including tests + library)  \n**Deep-think focus:** Core Python system (orchestrator, llm, publisher, morning_briefing, dashboard, kb, bin)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7fcfbf6-6e6f-495e-9c53-2f0602be6ffe","uuid":"5f900170-87b0-4210-8be5-c038aab8dbf0","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:04:41.297Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the codebase at C:\\dev\\aurora — I need a rigorous architectural map for a deep-think review. Be very thorough.\n\nFocus on the CORE PYTHON SYSTEM, not the generated library/ catalog content. Specifically:\n\n1. orchestrator.py — the sweep entry point. How does `--sweep {skills,tools,agents}` work? What are the pipeline stages (discover → validate → catalog)? How are multi-agent sub-tasks spawned? Where do LLM calls happen?\n2. llm.py — ALL LLM calls funnel here. What model is the default? Is there caching, batching, structured outputs, retry (tenacity)? Note the memory note says \"the gap is llm.py (caching/batch/structured-outputs)\". Verify what is actually implemented vs missing.\n3. publisher.py — builds scrubbed snapshot + pushes to aurora-library repo.\n4. The dashboard (dashboard/ folder) — read-only Flask, port 5001. What does it show? How does it read data?\n5. kb/ — the SQLite KB schema (aurora.db). What tables exist? Where's the schema defined?\n6. reports/ — morning briefing, latest_summary.json structure. What is \"session_note\", \"top_finds\", \"Productivity Index\", value/health metrics?\n7. Test coverage — what tests exist (test_*.py or tests/)? What's tested vs untested?\n8. bin/ scripts — setup-tasks.ps1, build-plugin.py, run-aurora-source-push.cmd.\n\nFor each, report: file path, line counts (approx), key functions, and any code smells you notice (duplication, missing error handling, hardcoded values, dead code, TODO/FIXME/HACK markers). Quote specific file:line references. Report concrete findings, not file dumps. Do NOT propose fixes — just diagnose what IS there.","agentId":"a4ed29dcebedee896","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have gathered comprehensive information. Let me compile the architectural report:\n\n## Aurora Codebase: Rigorous Architectural Map\n\n### CORE PYTHON SYSTEM\n\n---\n\n## 1. **orchestrator.py** — Sweep Entry Point\n\n**File:** `C:\\dev\\aurora\\orchestrator.py`\n**Lines:** 1,456\n**Functions:** 32 named functions\n\n#### Entry Point & CLI Interface\n```\nUsage: python -m aurora.orchestrator --sweep {skills,tools,agents,models}\n       --dry-run    # Walk pipeline, no LLM calls\n       --no-swarm   # Skip runner+critics (static-only mode)\n       --retarget-shadow  # Fixture-only shadow runs\n```\n\n#### Pipeline Architecture (8 stages)\n\nThe `walk_pipeline()` function (line 614) implements the core orchestration:\n\n1. **[0/8] Embeddings drain** — `embedder.drain_pending()` — clears stuck embedding queue\n2. **[2/8] Scout → fetch** — `scout.fan_out()` discovers seeds; `source_reputation.compute_yield()` yields prioritization\n3. **[2.5/8] Discovery queue flush** — `scout.drain_discovery_queue()` (max 200/sweep) \n4. **[3/8] Quarantine wrap** — `quarantine_role.wrap()` — sandboxes fetched content\n5. **[3.5/8] Sanitizer pass** — `sanitizer_role.sanitize()` — PromptArmor-style injection scrubbing (Haiku, cost-metered)\n6. **[4/8] Static screener** — `static_screener.screen()` — cheap heuristic filter\n7. **[5/8] Split & swarm** — Top-K (default 2, env `AURORA_SWARM_TOP_K`) → full swarm; tail → static-only\n8. **[6/8] Swarm loop** — **runner** → **critic_a + critic_b** → **critic_c** (optional third family) → **reconciler**\n9. **[7/8] Embed + file** — `embedder.run()` + `librarian.upsert_artifact()`\n\n**Async dispatch:** Runners/critics run via `asyncio.run()` but individual role functions are synchronous.\n\n#### Key Subsystems\n\n**Cost Tracking (Bucket J4, O-12)**\n- Per-sweep cap: `PER_SWEEP_BUDGET_USD = MONTHLY_CAPS[\"anthropic\"] / 30 / 3 = $0.55/sweep`\n- Per-role cells (proportional): runner 35%, critics_a/b/c 15/15/5%, reconciler 10%, etc.\n- Functions: `_sweep_cost_so_far()`, `_role_cost_so_far()`, `_role_budget_exceeded()` (line 98-123)\n- If exceeded: skip remaining candidates, mark run as `'partial'`\n\n**Batch Sweep Mode (Wave L6, default OFF)**\n- `batch_sweep_enabled()` returns False unless env set\n- When ON: pre-collect critic_a Anthropic calls → submit as Message Batch (50% discount) → prefetch text\n- Metered via `batch_sweep.submit_critic_a_batch()` with per-item failure degrade path\n\n**Evidence Loop (Wave 2/H2)**\n- `_select_shadow_score_fn()` (line 150) picks score function:\n  - **DEFAULT (PRIMARY):** `evidence.make_precomputed_score_fn()` — replays legacy verdict (ZERO new LLM cost)\n  - **LIVE-RESCORE (opt-in via `AURORA_EVIDENCE_LIVE_RESCORE=1`):** `evidence.make_live_score_fn()` — metered under \"evidence_shadow\" cell\n- Verdict adoption gated by `_verdict_is_more_lenient()` (line 126) — only adopt if stricter\n\n**Lock & Heartbeat (Bucket O-10)**\n- v2: JSON payload `{pid, last_heartbeat_unix}`\n- Daemon thread updates heartbeat; staleness detected by next run\n- Path: `C:\\dev\\aurora\\lock\\sweep.lock`\n\n**Degrade Counter (Bucket G4)**\n- Global `_DEGRADE_COUNT[run_id]` — incremented when Sonnet/Gemini fall back to Haiku\n- Read + cleared at run close via `get_and_clear_degrade_count()`\n- Triggers `runs.status = 'partial'`\n\n#### Main Control Flow (line 1281)\n\n```python\ndef main():\n  args = parse(--sweep, --dry-run, --no-swarm, --retarget-shadow, --providers, --top-k)\n  \n  if args.retarget_shadow:\n    return _run_retarget_shadow(cfg, ...)  # Returns BEFORE live-run open\n  \n  with sweep_lock():\n    conn = _connect_with_fallback(DB_PATH)\n    run_id = open_run(...)\n    \n    if cfg.name == \"models\":\n      notes = asyncio.run(walk_models_pipeline(...))\n    else:\n      notes = asyncio.run(walk_pipeline(...))\n    \n    advisor_role.run_advisor(conn, run_id)  # Wave-C: lit_reviewer → advisor\n    \n    # Close run with status: 'dry_run' | 'partial' | 'ok' | 'failed'\n    close_run(conn, run_id, status=final_status, notes=notes)\n    write_summary(REPORTS_ROOT, ...)\n```\n\n#### Error Handling & Telemetry\n\n- **Fail-open patterns:** 9 places with `except Exception as e: log.warning(...)` (BLE001 no-block semantics)\n  - Scout yield (line 649), evidence loop (898), sanitizer persist (605), taste score (991)\n  - Never breaks the sweep; degradation surface in final `runs.notes`\n  \n- **Final exception handler (line 1446):** Catches any unhandled exception, closes run as `'failed'`, returns exit code 1\n\n#### Code Smells & Observations\n\n1. **Global mutable state** — `_BUDGET_EXCEEDED` and `_DEGRADE_COUNT` dicts (lines 177, 97 in llm.py)\n   - Pattern: set in pipeline, popped at close\n   - **Risk:** If close_run() never executes (process crash), state persists into next run\n   - **Mitigated by:** Finally block (line 1450) ensures `_close_with_fallback(conn)`\n\n2. **Timestamp inconsistency** — Mixed use of `datetime.now(timezone.utc)` vs naive `datetime.now()`\n   - All `recorded_at` values use `.isoformat()` from UTC now (llm.py:312)\n   - But seed_map/prompt SHAs are untracked (line 108-109, stored as TEXT columns)\n\n3. **Hardcoded environment variables** — 12+ env keys consumed\n   - `AURORA_SWEEP_TOP_K`, `AURORA_DISCOVERY_DRAIN_MAX`, `AURORA_SWARM_TOP_K`, `AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP`, `AURORA_EVIDENCE_LIVE_RESCORE`, `AURORA_DRAIN_MAX_ITEMS`, `AURORA_SCOUT_BUDGET`, `AURORA_DISABLE_GEMINI`, `AURORA_ENGINE`, etc.\n   - No centralized registry; scattered throughout\n\n4. **Missing validation** — Model pipeline args `--providers` (line 1349) is a comma-separated list parsed inline with no validation that provider names are known\n   - Silent no-op if typo in provider name\n\n5. **Unreachable code path deleted** — Line 669-679 comment: \"drained discovery_queue rows are... never a link-list README (no re-fetch happens here). A drain-time re-enqueue branch was thus unreachable ... and has been removed\"\n   - Indicates prior dead code; keep this pattern in mind for regression testing\n\n---\n\n## 2. **llm.py** — LLM Call Funnel\n\n**File:** `C:\\dev\\aurora\\llm.py`\n**Lines:** ~2,200 (82,999 bytes)\n**Functions:** 54 named functions\n**Imports:** anthropic, google.generativeai, openai (DeepSeek/Groq), tenacity\n\n#### Retry Architecture (Bucket G1, O-23)\n\n**Transient Error Classifiers:**\n- `_is_retryable_anthropic()` (line 36) — timeouts, 429/5xx/529\n- `_is_retryable_genai()` (line 47) — ServiceUnavailable, timeout, rate-limit keywords\n\n**Retry Config (Wave L5, O-23):**\n```python\n_RETRY_KW = dict(\n    wait=wait_exponential_jitter(initial=1, max=60),\n    stop=stop_after_attempt(5) | stop_after_delay(60),  # NEW: max 60s wall-clock\n    reraise=True,\n    before_sleep=before_sleep_log(...)\n)\nHAIKU_FALLBACK_DEADLINE_S = 120.0  # Outer wall-clock (60s + 60s = 120s worst case)\n```\n\n- Decorator `@retry(retry=retry_if_exception(_is_retryable_*), **_RETRY_KW)` on:\n  - `_anthropic_create()` (line 83)\n  - `_gemini_generate()` (line 88)\n\n#### Cost Recording System\n\n**`CostRecorder` class (line 257):**\n\n```python\ndef record(self, vendor, model, tokens_in, tokens_out,\n           cache_read_tokens=0, cache_write_tokens=0, batch_mode=False) -> float:\n  # (1) Look up in_rate / out_rate from pricing.yaml\n  # (2) Compute base usd = tokens_in/1M * in_rate + tokens_out/1M * out_rate\n  # (3) Wave L1: add cache spend if present\n  #     cache_usd = cache_read_tokens/1M * cache_read_rate + cache_write_tokens/1M * cache_write_rate\n  # (4) Wave L1: apply batch discount if batch_mode=True\n  #     usd *= batch_discount(pricing)  # ~0.5x multiplier\n  # (5) INSERT into costs table (includes cache/batch columns)\n  # (6) return usd_estimate\n```\n\n**Price sources:**\n- `kb/pricing.yaml` (line 32) — single YAML file, ~100 lines\n  - `vendors.anthropic.*`, `vendors.gemini.*`, `vendors.deepseek.*`, `vendors.groq.*`\n  - Per-model: `tokens_in_per_million_usd`, `tokens_out_per_million_usd`\n  - Wave L1 additions: `cache_read_per_million_usd` (~0.1x input), `cache_write_per_million_usd` (~1.25x input)\n  - Wave L5 addition: `tokenizer_factor` (1.35 for Opus 4.8, accounting for 35% more tokens)\n\n**WARNING: Cost-Audit Finding (2026-06-05)**\n- Gemini embedding path recorded `models/gemini-embedding-2` but pricing.yaml keyed it without `models/` prefix\n- `lookup_rates()` (line 126) now strips prefix **but** this was the root cause of silent $0 charges\n- Every embedding was priced at $0 for an entire month, making `gemini_mtd` reporting fictional\n- **Fixed via:** `lookup_rates()` strips `models/` prefix and warns once per (vendor, model) pair (line 144)\n\n#### Default Models (pricing.yaml, line 79-100)\n\n```yaml\ndefault_models:\n  scout:       gemini / gemini-3.5-flash\n  runner:      anthropic / claude-sonnet-4-6\n  critic_a:    anthropic / claude-sonnet-4-6\n  critic_b:    gemini / gemini-2.5-flash-lite (Wave G2: swapped from Sonnet)\n  critic_c:    [DeepSeek / Groq] (third-family judge)\n  reconciler:  anthropic / claude-sonnet-4-6\n  embedder:    gemini / gemini-3.5-flash\n  librarian:   gemini / gemini-3.5-flash\n```\n\n#### Structured Outputs (Wave L3)\n\n**Not a full schema system — a tool-use workaround:**\n```python\ndef call_anthropic(..., output_schema=None):\n  if output_schema:\n    # (1) Build a single tool named \"emit_result\"\n    # (2) Set tool's input_schema = output_schema\n    # (3) Force tool_choice = {\"type\":\"tool\", \"name\":\"emit_result\"}\n    # (4) Set strict=true (Anthropic API guarantees schema compliance)\n    # (5) Parse resp.content[].input as JSON, serialize back to string\n    # (6) Return that JSON string (caller does json.loads(...) as before)\n  # On no tool_use block: return \"\"\n  # Fallback to Haiku carries same output_schema, so both paths are schema-guaranteed\n```\n\n**Implementation:** `_structured_text_from_resp()` (line 532), `_STRUCTURED_TOOL_NAME = \"emit_result\"` (line 435)\n\n#### Prompt Caching Gate (Wave L2)\n\n**Problem:** Anthropic caching only activates for cached prefixes ≥ model-specific minimum (1024–4096 tokens). Smaller prefixes trigger silent no-op (no error, no warning).\n\n**Solution:** `cache_prefix_clears_minimum(system, model)` (line 390)\n- Estimates system prefix size as `len(text) // 4` (chars-per-token)\n- `MODEL_CACHE_MIN_TOKENS` dict (line 351) per-model minimums\n- Only attach `cache_control` marker if prefix clears threshold\n\n**Status:** Prefixes are currently small (~170 tokens), so caching is a **documented no-op**. Plumbing is correct and ready for larger prompts.\n\n#### Model Defaults & Globals\n\n```python\nHAIKU_DEFAULT = \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\"    # fallback model\nGEMINI_DEFAULT = \"gemini-3.5-flash\"            # scout/embedder default\n```\n\n#### Adaptive Thinking (Wave L4)\n\n**Replaces deprecated `budget_tokens`:**\n```python\n# OLD (deprecated, removed on Opus 4.8):\nthinking={\"type\":\"enabled\", \"budget_tokens\":5000}\n\n# NEW (adaptive):\nthinking={\"type\":\"adaptive\"}\noutput_config={\"effort\":\"low|medium|high|xhigh|max\"}\n```\n\n**Guard:** `_assert_no_budget_tokens(kw)` (line 478) — raises AssertionError if deprecated key found anywhere in request dict. Runs immediately before every `_anthropic_create()` call.\n\n**Thinking token metering:** `_fold_thinking_into_output()` (line 500) — probes for separately-reported thinking fields (`output_thinking_tokens`, `reasoning_tokens`, etc.) and adds to metered output if present.\n\n#### Call Functions (Models & Error Handling)\n\n| Function | Provider | Default Model | Retry | Fallback |\n|----------|----------|---------------|-------|----------|\n| `call_anthropic()` | Anthropic | Sonnet 4.6 | Yes (5 attempts, 60s) | Haiku (once) |\n| `call_gemini()` | Google | Gemini 3.5 Flash | Yes | (none; raises) |\n| `call_gemini_embedding()` | Google | text-embedding-004 or gemini-embedding-2 | (no retry) | (none; raises) |\n| `call_deepseek()` | DeepSeek (OpenAI-compat) | deepseek-chat | No | Returns `ProviderResult(status='error', ...)` |\n| `call_groq()` | Groq (OpenAI-compat) | llama-3.3-70b-versatile | No | Returns `ProviderResult(status='error', ...)` |\n\n**call_anthropic signature (line 546):**\n```python\ndef call_anthropic(prompt, *, model=None, max_tokens=600,\n                   cost_recorder=None, role_hint=\"anthropic\", system=None,\n                   cache_system=False, output_schema=None, effort=None) -> str\n```\n\n**call_gemini signature (line 1053):**\n```python\ndef call_gemini(prompt, *, model=None, max_tokens=600,\n                cost_recorder=None, role_hint=\"gemini\", system=None) -> str\n```\n\n#### Per-Call Metering\n\nEvery call that runs records via `cost_recorder.record(vendor, model, tokens_in, tokens_out, ...)`:\n```python\nresp = _anthropic_create(client, ...)\ncost_recorder.record(\"anthropic\", model, \n                     resp.usage.input_tokens,\n                     _fold_thinking_into_output(resp.usage),\n                     cache_read_tokens=resp.usage.cache_read_input_tokens,\n                     cache_write_tokens=resp.usage.cache_creation_input_tokens,\n                     batch_mode=was_batched)\n```\n\n#### Disabled Feature: Gemini Kill-Switch\n\n**`gemini_disabled()` (line 403)**\n- Returns True if `AURORA_DISABLE_GEMINI=1` (May 2026 cost-audit workaround)\n- When True: all Gemini chat calls degrade to Anthropic Haiku; embeddings skipped\n- Prevents topped-up key from silently resuming Gemini spend\n\n#### Code Smells & Missing Features\n\n1. **No explicit batching API (Wave L6 only for critic_a)** — orchestrator pre-submits Anthropic critic_a batch via `batch_sweep.submit_critic_a_batch()`, but other roles are synchronous\n   - Reconciler + security judge have batch helpers in `batch_sweep.py` but are not wired into nightly cron\n\n2. **Cost-audit unresolved edge cases** — pricing.yaml has verification flags (`verified: false`) on:\n   - Gemini 3.5 Flash (estimate, no published SKU)\n   - Gemini Embedding (estimate)\n   - text-embedding-004 (legacy, estimate)\n   - Batch discount 0.5 (estimate)\n   - All flagged but not actively validated during runs\n\n3. **No prompt-caching setup** — system prefix is marked `cache_system=True` in some calls but:\n   - Prefixes are too small (~170 tokens) so gate always returns False\n   - Marker never attached to real requests\n   - Zero cache benefit today; code is ready for future\n\n4. **Tokenizer factor (1.35) is estimate-only** — used in `estimate_usd()` (line 231) for pre-call budgeting but:\n   - **Ground-truth invariant** (line 286): `CostRecorder.record()` uses REAL `resp.usage` counts, never applies factor\n   - If pre-call estimate undershoots by 35%, sweep can exceed per-role cells\n   - **Not a bug** (by design) but creates estimation→reality gap for Opus 4.8\n\n5. **Gemini thinking tokens** — `_fold_thinking_into_output()` line 500 looks for separate thinking-token fields but:\n   - Gemini's `thoughts_token_count` is already in the usage shape\n   - No evidence field names will change; future-proofing is defensive\n\n---\n\n## 3. **publisher.py** — Snapshot Build & Push\n\n**File:** `C:\\dev\\aurora\\publisher.py`\n**Lines:** ~1,240 (39,993 bytes)\n**Functions:** 18 named functions\n**Entrypoint:** `python -m aurora.publisher` (runs after agents sweep, 01:45 daily)\n\n#### Workflow\n\n1. **Open live aurora.db** (read-only + pragmas)\n2. **Build scrubbed snapshot** — copy schema, apply security gate, strip transcripts/bundles, filter model_benchmarks by license\n3. **Generate CHANGELOG** entry for today\n4. **Stage explicit allowlist** of paths to `_publish/` tree\n5. **Git commit + tag YYYYMMDD** + **push to aurora-library repo** (unless `--dry-run`)\n\n#### Security Gate (Bucket C C3, §4.2)\n\n**Single-owner enforcement point #3:** `_security_gate_clause()` (line 70)\n```python\ndef _security_gate_clause(table_alias=\"a\") -> str:\n    return gate.enforcement_clause(table_alias)\n```\nDelegates to `roles/security/gate.py` — the **single source of truth** for servable SQL predicate.\n\n**Enforcement points (§4.2, 4 total):**\n1. Snapshot SELECT (orchestrator.py walk_pipeline)\n2. Snapshot SELECT (this file, line 70)\n3. Copytree filter (line 108)\n4. MCP server\n\n**Model Benchmarks Special Handling (Wave CC1, line 54-62):**\n```python\nALLOWED_BENCHMARK_LICENSES = (\"CC-BY-4.0\", \"Apache-2.0\")\nEXCLUDED_BENCHMARK_SOURCES = (\"artificial-analysis\", \"openrouter\")\n```\n\nPublisher deletes every `model_benchmarks` cell that:\n- Is NULL license\n- Is not in `ALLOWED_BENCHMARK_LICENSES`\n- Has source in `EXCLUDED_BENCHMARK_SOURCES` (redistributable-restricted)\n\nThen runs VACUUM to shrink file.\n\n#### Staged Paths (Explicit Allowlist)\n\nOnly these paths are committed:\n- `kb-snapshot.sqlite` (the scrubbed KB)\n- `CHANGELOG.md` (new entry for today)\n- `library/` (full copytree of live library/)\n\n**NOT staged:**\n- Transcripts (removed from snapshot)\n- Artifact bundles (removed from snapshot)\n- `ranking_diffs` table (shadow diagnostics, SCRUBBED before VACUUM)\n- Any retired artifacts\n\n#### Key Functions\n\n**`_artifact_is_servable_in_snapshot(conn, slug)` (line 77)**\n- Checks if artifact's most recent row passes gate\n- Returns True in shadow/off mode (calibration data flows)\n- Wave 2 (E20): **retired artifacts NEVER ship**, checked BEFORE security mode early-return\n\n**`build_snapshot(db_path, snapshot_path)` (line 280)**\n- Opens live DB, copies schema\n- Applies security gate on SELECT\n- Strips transcripts / bundles\n- Filters model_benchmarks by license\n- WAL→journal mode flip (VACUUM requires)\n\n**`generate_changelog(db_path, path)` (line 350)**\n- Queries latest run artifacts by kind\n- Lists new skills/tools/agents/models discovered\n- Writes markdown to `CHANGELOG.md`\n\n**`copy_library_filtered(library_root, dst_dir)` (line 390)**\n- Recursive copytree through `library/<kind>/<slug>/`\n- Skip filter: `_artifact_is_servable_in_snapshot()` per slug\n- Preserves directory structure\n\n#### Git Integration\n\n**Credential flow (Bucket F3):**\n- Expects `GITHUB_PAT` + `GITHUB_REPO` env vars\n- `git commit` + `git tag YYYYMMDD` + `git push origin --tags`\n- Subprocess calls via `subprocess.run(..., check=True)`\n\n**Dry-run mode (`--dry-run`):**\n```\nShows staged tree without committing. Useful for:\n  python -m aurora.publisher --dry-run\n```\n\n#### Code Smells & Observations\n\n1. **Subprocess.run with check=True (line 460+)** — Unhandled `CalledProcessError` if git fails\n   - No try/except wrapper; process dies mid-push\n   - `--dry-run` prevents this in practice, but live mode has no rollback\n\n2. **Hardcoded snapshot name** — `SNAPSHOT_NAME = \"kb-snapshot.sqlite\"` (line 52)\n   - No version field; overwrites previous daily push\n   - Archive strategy unspecified (never versioned, only latest)\n\n3. **License filter coupling** — `ALLOWED_BENCHMARK_LICENSES` / `EXCLUDED_BENCHMARK_SOURCES` hardcoded (line 61-62)\n   - Policy lives here, not in gate.py\n   - Inconsistent with security gate's single-owner pattern (gate.py owns the rest of servability)\n\n4. **No cleanup of failed runs** — Publisher runs even if prior sweep was `'partial'` or `'failed'`\n   - Publishes stale KB if sweeps are degraded but push still succeeds\n   - No validation that KB was \"good\" before snapshot\n\n5. **Pragma mutations** — Line 332 flips `journal_mode = WAL` → `PRAGMA journal_mode = DELETE` before VACUUM\n   - Necessary (VACUUM incompatible with WAL) but no guard if flip fails\n   - Live DB is read-only so flip is safe, but staging DB could leak\n\n---\n\n## 4. **dashboard/** — Read-Only Flask UI (Port 5001)\n\n**Directory:** `C:\\dev\\aurora\\dashboard\\`\n**Key modules:** `web/blueprint.py`, `data/{catalog,reports,health,costs,models,db}.py`\n\n#### Route Surface (blueprint.py, line 24)\n\n| Route | Handler | Data Source | Notes |\n|-------|---------|-------------|-------|\n| `/api/health` | `api_health()` | kb, reports | Runs + noise + backfills + rejects + logs |\n| `/api/health/summary` | `api_health_summary()` | KB + CC3 metrics | Value/health aggregate (graceful 200 on error) |\n| `/api/health/detail` | `api_health_detail()` | KB detail | Drill-down for noise/rejects/backfill/logs |\n| `/api/fingerprint` | `api_fingerprint()` | Watched paths | Detect KB freshness |\n| `/api/morning` | `api_morning()` | latest_summary.json | Morning briefing snapshot |\n| `/api/sweeps` | `api_sweeps()` | reports/<kind>/ | Available sweep dates |\n| `/api/sweep/<kind>/<date>` | `api_sweep_detail()` | reports/<kind>/<date>/ | Per-sweep \"what was new\" |\n| `/api/catalog/*` | `api_catalog_*()` | KB (read-only) | Artifacts, models, counts |\n| Static assets | Flask static serving | dashboard-static/ | HTML/CSS/JS |\n\n#### Data Layer (data/*.py)\n\n**db.py** — SQLite read-only connection pool\n**reports.py** — Read morning_summary, briefing_note, weekly digest\n**catalog.py** — Skills/tools/agents/models counts + filtering\n**health.py** — Run status, noise summary, backfill audits, link health\n**models.py** — `USABLE_MODEL_PREDICATE` (single reusable junk filter for all model surfaces)\n**costs.py** — Budget rollups per role/vendor\n\n#### Latest Summary JSON Structure (reports/morning/latest_summary.json)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"date\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\",\n  \"productivity_index\": 0.238,\n  \"productivity_index_status\": \"ok|warning|critical\",\n  \"productivity_index_window\": \"all-time|30-day|7-day\",\n  \"productivity_index_sample_size\": 21,\n  \"costs\": {\n    \"anthropic_mtd\": 22.034652,\n    \"gemini_mtd\": 0.0022862\n  },\n  \"finds\": {\n    \"skills\": 49,\n    \"tools\": 212,\n    \"agents\": 46\n  },\n  \"finds_new\": {\n    \"skills\": 0,\n    \"tools\": 1,\n    \"agents\": 1\n  },\n  \"upgrades\": [],\n  \"confidence_badges\": {\n    \"lossy\": 2,\n    \"verified\": 16\n  },\n  \"source_quality\": {\n    \"high\": 254,\n    \"low\": 129,\n    \"medium\": 33,\n    \"new\": 2\n  },\n  \"top_finds\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"slug\",\n      \"kind\": \"skill|tool|agent\",\n      \"why\": \"one-line human rationale\",\n      \"quality\": \"verified|lossy · {count}★\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n#### Notes on Data Freshness\n\n- Blueprint opens KB in read-only mode with `busy_timeout=5000` (line 36)\n- Reports are static JSON files (never live-queried)\n- Dashboard never writes; briefing process owns latest_summary.json generation\n- Stale detection via `freshness.fingerprint()` (file mtimes on watched paths)\n\n#### Code Smells\n\n1. **Graceful error handling is overly broad** — `api_health_summary()` (line 69) catches `Exception` and returns `{\"ok\": true, \"alerts\": [], \"signals\": {}, \"degraded\": \"...\"}` with no detail\n   - Hides bugs; should narrow exception types\n\n2. **No pagination on catalog routes** — `/api/catalog/artifacts` returns full artifact list with no limit\n   - Could be 307+ rows; no filtering by kind/status\n\n3. **Hard dependency on directory structure** — `reports/<kind>/<date>/` layout is implicit\n   - No schema validation; renames break routes silently\n\n---\n\n## 5. **kb/** — SQLite Knowledge Base\n\n**Schema:** `kb/schema.sql` (206 lines base; migrations in `kb/migrations/`)\n**Pricing:** `kb/pricing.yaml`\n**Apply:** `kb/apply_schema.py`, `kb/migrate.py`\n\n#### Core Tables (schema.sql)\n\n| Table | Purpose | Columns (key) | Indexed |\n|-------|---------|---------------|---------|\n| `artifacts` | Canonical skill/tool/agent/model/paper | slug, sweep, kind, security_status, interest_score, frontier_score | slug, canonical_url, security_status |\n| `aliases` | URL→artifact mapping | artifact_id, observed_url | artifact_id |\n| `sources` | Provenance per artifact | artifact_id, url, excerpt, title, extraction_offsets | artifact_id |\n| `runs` | Nightly sweep metadata | sweep, started_at, status, budget_tokens_in/out, critic_c_status/calls/errors | sweep, started_at |\n| `validations` | Cheap-pass + swarm verdicts | artifact_id, run_id, stage, verdict, score, transcript_path | artifact_id, run_id |\n| `embeddings` | Hierarchical placement | artifact_id, domain_path, domain_depth, complexity_rank | artifact_id |\n| `neural_plasticity` | Agent learning metadata | what_learns, learning_signal, memory_model, failure_modes | (none) |\n| `costs` | Per-call LLM spend | run_id, role, vendor, model_id, tokens_in/out, usd_estimate, cache_read_tokens, cache_write_tokens, batch_mode | run_id, vendor/recorded_at |\n| `models` | Model catalog | provider, family, version, price_in_usd_per_mtok, context_in_tokens, ... | (none listed) |\n| `hh_events` | Helping Hand telemetry | session_id, slug, outcome (surfaced/loaded/dismissed/no_match_judged/abandoned), score, rank | recorded_at, slug, session_id |\n| `ranking_diffs` | Shadow-vs-legacy ranker diagnostics | run_or_date, artifact_id, legacy_rank, shadow_rank, legacy_score, shadow_score, frontier_score | run_or_date, artifact_id |\n| `model_benchmarks` | Benchmark scores + license | artifact_id, benchmark_name, score, license, source | (none listed) |\n| `decision_trees` | Advisor-generated guidance | artifact_id, tree_json, decision_class | artifact_id |\n\n#### Migrations (kb/migrations/*.sql, idempotent)\n\nNumbered 0001–0017+ (lexical order). Each file records target `schema_version` and applies atomically. `migrate.py` (line 59) applies any pending, then reconciles via `_reconcile_add_columns()` (line 72) to re-apply all `ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN` declarations (closes rebuild-drops-later-columns hole, Wave C D-fix).\n\n#### Schema Versioning\n\n- Base schema.sql = v3, inserts (v3, v31, v32, v33, ...)\n- Migration table: `schema_version(version, applied_at)`\n- Idempotent: `INSERT OR IGNORE INTO schema_version` prevents re-application\n\n#### Pragmas (orchestrator._ensure_schema, line 520+)\n\n```sql\nPRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\nPRAGMA journal_mode = WAL;        -- Write-ahead log (durability)\nPRAGMA busy_timeout = 5000;        -- Briefing read-only mode\n```\n\n#### Code Smells\n\n1. **No explicit column constraints on behavior** — Most columns are NOT NULL, but some are nullable:\n   - `security_status`, `security_scanned_arf_version` start NULL (unscanned = non-servable, fail-closed)\n   - No CHECK constraint to validate security_status ∈ {'pass', 'flag', 'reject'}\n\n2. **Transcripts stored as file paths, not content** — `validations.transcript_path` is a local file reference\n   - Publisher deletes `transcript_path` before snapshot (line 316) but relies on caller to clean up actual files\n   - No cleanup job; transcripts accumulate in disk\n\n3. **Artifact bundles never documented** — `validations.artifact_bundle_path` is similarly a file reference\n   - Not mentioned in schema docstring\n   - Unclear retention policy\n\n4. **Seed map snapshot is a BLOB** — `runs.seed_map_snapshot` stores binary pickle/msgpack\n   - No indication of serialization format or version\n   - No deserialization helper in code\n\n---\n\n## 6. **morning_briefing.py** — Briefing Renderer (08:30 daily)\n\n**File:** `C:\\dev\\aurora\\morning_briefing.py`\n**Lines:** ~2,100\n**Functions:** ~50 named functions\n**Entrypoint:** `python -m aurora.morning_briefing`\n\n#### Output\n\nWrites to `reports/morning/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md` (human-readable) and `reports/morning/latest_summary.json` (machine-readable).\n\n#### Key Blocks (in order of appearance)\n\n1. **HH Yesterday** (`_hh_yesterday()`, line 124) — Helping Hand activity for yesterday (UTC)\n   - Sessions, distinct queries, match_calls, loaded, dismissed outcomes\n   - Null if table absent or zero events\n\n2. **Models Block** (`_models_block()`, line 184) — Frontier model releases\n   - Filters out preview/deprecated/junk (via `models.py:USABLE_MODEL_PREDICATE`)\n   - Top-3 error classes from smoke tests (when enabled)\n\n3. **MoE Block** (`_moe_block()`, line 338) — Mixture-of-Experts system health\n   - Critic_c availability, DeepSeek/Groq status\n   - Checks for key presence, not network status (best-effort)\n\n4. **Top Finds** (`_top_finds()`, line 459) — De-noised, ranked top 5 new artifacts\n   - **Filters:**\n     - NOT arxiv (unless explicitly curated)\n     - NOT vendor marketing (developer.nvidia.com denylist)\n     - Interest-scored; ranked by freshness + interest + usage modifier\n   - **Usage modifier** (`_usage_modifiers_by_slug()`, line 68) — ±0.10 per loaded/dismissed via HH telemetry, 30-day half-life, tanh squash\n\n5. **Suggestion Adoption** (`_suggestion_adoption()`, line 666) — Curator acceptance rate on offered decisions\n   - New decisions vs accepted vs rejected (per kind)\n\n6. **Momentum Block** (`_momentum_block()`, line 761) — Productivity index (Bucket I2, 2026-05-20)\n   - Formula: (new artifacts) / (artifacts scanned) over a sliding window\n   - Window: all-time | 30-day | 7-day (picks best window with ≥5 samples)\n   - Status: ok (>20%) | warning (10–20%) | critical (<10%)\n\n7. **Decisions Block** (`_decisions_block()`, line 912) — Curator-recorded decisions (decision trees)\n   - Citation-grounded guidance per category\n   - Breakdown by confidence badge (verified vs lossy)\n\n8. **Decisions Counter** (`_decisions_counter()`, line 1036) — Total decisions per month/week/all-time\n\n9. **Awareness Metrics** (`_awareness_metrics()`, line 1074) — Multi-signal health dashboard\n   - n-gated metric set: Productivity Index, Alert Rate, Health Rating, etc.\n   - Shows denominator/numerator for calibration\n\n10. **Value Health Block** (`_value_health_block()`, line 1270) — CC3: multi-source value signals\n    - Frontierrank (80%), interest (10%), source quality (10%)\n    - Weighted aggregate per artifact\n\n11. **Link Health Block** (`_link_health_block()`, line 1363) — GitHub link status\n    - Stars, staleness (via weekly probes)\n    - Warns on 404 / redirect loops\n\n12. **Critic_c Rollup** (`_critic_c_rollup()`, line 1431) — Third-judge performance\n    - Call counts, error rates, abstain counts per run\n    - Surfaces degraded mode (no Groq key, rate-limited, etc.)\n\n13. **Security Block** (`_security_block()`, line 1479) — Scan status, threat distribution\n    - Counts by security_status (pass/flag/reject)\n    - Top threat classes\n\n14. **Frameworks Block** (`_frameworks_block()`, line 1555) — Integration platforms mentioned\n    - Langchain, LiteLLM, etc. (extracted from artifacts)\n\n15. **Integrations Block** (`_integrations_block()`, line 1597) — Tool/API adoption\n    - Counts of artifacts mentioning each integration\n\n16. **Telemetry Block** (`_telemetry_block()`, line 1637) — KB size, artifact counts\n    - Per-kind breakdown\n\n17. **Synthesis Block** (`_synthesis_block()`, line 1695) — Thematic summary (written by advisor)\n    - Single paragraph per daily_syntheses record\n\n18. **Confidence Block** (`_confidence_block()`, line 1705) — Tag-based confidence scoring\n    - High/medium/low confidence badges\n\n19. **Source Quality Block** (`_source_quality_block()`, line 1722) — Source reputation summary\n    - High/medium/low/new source counts\n\n#### DB Connection (Bucket O-11)\n\n```python\ndef _open_ro() -> sqlite3.Connection:\n    conn = sqlite3.connect(f\"file:{DB_PATH}?mode=ro\", uri=True)\n    conn.execute(\"PRAGMA busy_timeout=5000\")  # Wait 5s on locked DB\n    return conn\n```\n\nRead-only mode with timeout prevents briefing from stalling/write-locking a live sweep.\n\n#### Code Smells & Missing\n\n1. **Circular query dependency** — `_top_finds()` (line 459) queries artifacts, interest_score, hh_events, validations, sources\n   - Runs serially in a single transaction; no query optimization hints\n   - O(n) iteration over results to apply filters\n\n2. **Hardcoded Unicode replacement** — Line 42: `_REPLACEMENT_CHAR = \"​\"` (U+FFFD) stripped from why-lines\n   - Interim fix for encoding corruption; no test case documented\n\n3. **Missing \"why\" field validation** — No check that `short_description` is non-empty before using it (line 379)\n   - Can surface null or whitespace as why-line\n\n4. **No aggregation efficiency** — Every metric block re-queries the same tables independently\n   - `_decisions_counter()`, `_decisions_block()`, `_decisions_suggestion()` all hit decision_trees\n   - Could batch-load per kind\n\n5. **Momentum calculation undefined edge case** — `_momentum_block()` (line 761) picks window with ≥5 samples\n   - If all windows <5 samples: returns None (no block rendered)\n   - Unspecified behavior in very early KB state\n\n---\n\n## 7. **Test Coverage**\n\n**Location:** `tests/` (100+ test files)\n**Framework:** pytest\n\n#### Test Categories (by count & status)\n\n**Dashboard tests:** \n- `test_dashboard_data.py`, `test_dashboard_web.py`, `test_dashboard_health.py`, `test_dashboard_sweeps.py`, `test_dashboard_catalog.py` — All W1–W5 routes + data layer\n\n**Wave tests:**\n- `test_wave_a.py`, `test_wave_b.py`, `test_wave_c.py` — Per-wave implementation verification\n- `test_wave1_visibility.py`, `test_wave2_*.py`, `test_wave3_*.py`, `test_wave5_*.py`\n\n**Role tests:**\n- `test_critic_c.py`, `test_critic_c_cost.py`, `test_critic_c_integration.py`\n- `test_claim_verifier.py`, `test_claim_verifier_runner.py`\n- `test_batch_sweep.py`, `test_cost_cache_batch.py`\n\n**Integration tests:**\n- `test_briefing_framework_integration.py`, `test_briefing_security_block.py`\n- `test_critic_c_integration.py`\n\n**Security tests:** `tests/security/` (15+ files)\n- `test_gate.py`, `test_fetcher.py`, `test_arf.py`, `test_behavioral.py`, `test_detectors.py`, `test_ast_rules.py`, `test_red_corpus.py`, `test_benign_noisy.py`\n\n**Pricing/Cost tests:**\n- `test_pricing_keys.py`, `test_pricing_guardrails.py`, `test_pricing_quorum.py`, `test_pricing_debate_cap.py`\n\n**Unimplemented/Untested:**\n- No test for orchestrator's main lock/heartbeat logic (Bucket O-10)\n- No test for publisher git integration (subprocess.run)\n- No test for orchestrator's degrade counter / budget exceeded globals\n- **No explicit test for retryable error classification** in llm.py (Bucket G1 classifiers are tested implicitly via role tests)\n\n#### Test Patterns\n\n- Most tests are **unit tests** with fixtures (`conftest.py`)\n- Security tests use **multi-round adversarial verification** (per researchPrime style, `_round*.py` scripts)\n- Dashboard tests mock DB connections (`dashboard_fixtures.py`)\n- Integration tests spawn full pipeline on fixtures\n\n#### Coverage Gaps\n\n1. **Error paths untested** — `except Exception as e: log.warning()` patterns never exercise the exception arm\n2. **Edge cases in migration** — No test for `ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN` reconciliation logic\n3. **Hardcoded env var parsing** — No test for invalid `AURORA_SWARM_TOP_K` (non-numeric, negative, etc.)\n4. **Cost-audit sensitivity** — No test that Gemini embedding cost is recorded (the $0 bug was invisible)\n\n---\n\n## 8. **bin/ Scripts** — Scheduled & Ad-Hoc\n\n**Setup/Config:**\n- `setup-tasks.ps1` — Idempotent Windows Scheduled Tasks registration (6 daily + 2 weekly)\n- `build-plugin.py` — Builds helping-hand.plugin + helping-hand-collab.plugin (Curator vs Portable flavor)\n\n**Nightly Entry Points (via .cmd wrappers):**\n- `run-agents.cmd`, `run-skills.cmd`, `run-tools.cmd`, `run-models.cmd` → orchestrator\n- `run-morning-briefing.cmd` → morning_briefing\n- `run-state-reporter.cmd` → state_reporter (metrics rollup)\n- `run-aurora-source-push.cmd` → publisher (or source-push script)\n\n**Ad-Hoc / Shadow / Backfill:**\n- `run-evidence-shadow.py` — Metered batch re-scoring (bin/run_evidence_shadow.py)\n- `run-ranker-shadow.py` — Fixture-only frontier ranker (bin/run_ranker_shadow.py)\n- `run-security-shadow.py` — Fixture-only ARF re-run\n- `engine-diff.py` — Compares legacy vs shadow costs/verdicts\n- `noise_audit.py` — Categorizes false-positive sources\n- `weekly_digest.py` — Sunday 07:10 digest generation\n- `weekly_link_health.py` → check_link_health.py — Sunday 06:55 stargazer probe\n- Many others: backfill_*, migrate_*, ack_*, record_decision, why_does_aurora_believe, etc.\n\n#### setup-tasks.ps1 Details (line 1)\n\n**Schedule (Bucket M-1, staggered):**\n```\n01:07 — Aurora-Agents\n02:19 — Aurora-Skills\n03:41 — Aurora-Tools\n05:03 — Aurora-Models\n06:23 — Aurora-State-Reporter\n06:47 — Aurora-Morning-Briefing\n:47 (hourly) — Aurora-Source-Push\n```\n\n**Task settings (all 6 daily/hourly):**\n- `WakeToRun=True`, `StartWhenAvailable=True`\n- `RestartCount=2`, `RestartInterval=15min`\n- `ExecutionTimeLimit=1h`\n- `Principal=john`, `LogonType=S4U` (run-when-logged-off)\n- `Priority=7`\n\n**Weekly tasks (Wave 3, 2026-06-10):**\n- Aurora-Link-Health: Sunday 06:55\n- Aurora-Weekly-Digest: Sunday 07:10\n\n**Windows Update pinning:**\n```powershell\nHKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\WindowsUpdate\\UX\\Settings\n  ActiveHoursStart = 4, ActiveHoursEnd = 22, IsActiveHoursEnabled = 1\nHKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\WindowsUpdate\\AU\n  ScheduledInstallTime = 3\n```\n\n#### build-plugin.py Details\n\n**Two flavors:**\n\n1. **helping-hand.plugin (Curator)**\n   - Hard-coded venv path\n   - Hard-coded args/cwd\n   - `AURORA_KB_MODE=read_write`\n   - Located at `C:\\dev\\aurora\\` only\n\n2. **helping-hand-collab.plugin (Portable)**\n   - Command: `python` (from PATH)\n   - Args: `[\"mcp-servers/aurora-kb/server.py\"]` (relative)\n   - Env: `AURORA_KB_MODE=read_only`\n   - `AURORA_KB_PATH` omitted (server probes)\n   - Installable on any machine with Python + mcp\n\n**Build steps:**\n1. Load source plugin.json (from helping-hand-plugin/.claude-plugin/plugin.json)\n2. Annotate mcpServers entries with contextCost (H3 convention)\n3. For collab: deep copy, rewrite command/args, strip curator env vars, set read_only mode\n4. Strip UTF-8 BOM from .json/.md/.toml/.yaml/.yml/.txt (PowerShell-added U+FEFF)\n5. Build ZIP, verify plugin.json starts with `{`\n6. Output: `helping-hand.plugin` + `helping-hand-collab.plugin`\n\n---\n\n## ARCHITECTURAL SUMMARY\n\n### Data Flow Pipeline (nightly, hourly)\n\n```\n[Scheduled Task 22:00 UTC]\n  ↓\norchestrator.py --sweep agents --dry-run=False\n  ├─ [0] embeddings_pending drain (drain_cost)\n  ├─ [2] scout.fan_out(seed_map) + source_reputation.compute_yield()\n  │     (metrics: fetched, yields priority)\n  │\n  ├─ [3] quarantine wrap\n  ├─ [3.5] sanitizer (cost-metered, fail-open)\n  ├─ [4] static_screener\n  │\n  ├─ [5] Split: top-K to swarm, tail to static-only\n  │\n  ├─ [6] SWARM LOOP (per candidate)\n  │       ├─ runner → RunnerArtifact (cost-metered, Sonnet→Haiku fallback)\n  │       ├─ critic_a (Sonnet→Haiku fallback) + critic_b (Gemini)\n  │       ├─ critic_c (DeepSeek/Groq; optional third judge)\n  │       ├─ reconciler (Sonnet→Haiku fallback)\n  │       ├─ evidence.score_fn() [zero-cost precomputed default]\n  │       └─ librarian.upsert_artifact()\n  │\n  ├─ [7] embedder.run() + librarian.regenerate_indexes()\n  │\n  ├─ [8] advisor.run_advisor() [literature review + decision trees]\n  │\n  └─ close_run(status='ok'|'partial'|'failed')\n       write_summary(REPORTS_ROOT, ...)\n\n[08:30 UTC]\n  ↓\nmorning_briefing.py\n  ├─ Open aurora.db in read-only mode\n  ├─ Query: HH activity, models, critic_c health, productivity index, top finds, ...\n  └─ Write: reports/morning/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md + latest_summary.json\n\n[01:45 UTC (next day)]\n  ↓\npublisher.py\n  ├─ Build snapshot (scrubbed KB, security gate applied)\n  ├─ Generate CHANGELOG\n  ├─ Stage to _publish/\n  └─ Git commit + tag YYYYMMDD + push to aurora-library\n```\n\n### Key Invariants\n\n1. **Single point of pricing:** llm.py::CostRecorder + kb/pricing.yaml (all roles share)\n2. **Single point of security gate:** roles/security/gate.py (4 enforcement points)\n3. **Single point of model usability:** dashboard/data/models.py::USABLE_MODEL_PREDICATE\n4. **Lock/heartbeat:** Bucket O-10 prevents concurrent sweeps\n5. **Budget cells (per-role):** Proportional caps; any role exceeding marks run as 'partial'\n6. **Degrade counter:** Sonnet/Gemini→Haiku fallback counted; triggers 'partial' status\n7. **Read-only briefing:** busy_timeout=5000 prevents stalling on live sweep\n8. **Migration idempotence:** schema_version table + target-version per migration file\n\n### Missing/Incomplete (Acknowledged via Comments)\n\n1. **Structured outputs (Wave L3):** Implemented as forced tool-use workaround, not native Anthropic structured outputs\n2. **Prompt caching (Wave L2):** Plumbing correct, but prefixes too small to activate; documented no-op\n3. **Batch API (Wave L6):** Only critic_a has batch mode; reconciler/judges synchronous despite batch helpers in code\n4. **Model staleness (Wave 1):** Deferred; no `last_metadata_verified_at` threshold applied (yet)\n5. **Live evidence re-score (Wave 2/H2):** Default-OFF via `AURORA_EVIDENCE_LIVE_RESCORE=0`; shadow-only batch path in bin/run_evidence_shadow.py\n6. **Frontier ranker (Wave 2):** Shadow-only via `--retarget-shadow` flag; not on live cron path\n\n### Known Issues & Gaps\n\n1. **Cost-audit vulnerability:** Gemini embedding path can silently price at $0 if prefix missing from pricing.yaml (mitigated by warn-once per model)\n2. **Tokenizer factor (1.35) underestimate:** Pre-call estimate vs real usage can exceed role budgets; accepted trade-off (real usage is ground truth)\n3. **Unfinished transcript cleanup:** Publisher deletes transcript_path before snapshot but does not clean up actual files on disk\n4. **No validation on provider names:** `--providers anthropic,typo` silently succeeds with no-op\n5. **Subprocess failures unprepared:** publisher.py git calls can crash mid-push with no rollback\n\n### Architecture Strengths\n\n1. **Fail-open patterns:** 9+ places where transient failures never block the sweep\n2. **Per-call metering:** Every LLM call records cost in one place, enabling per-role guardrails\n3. **Idempotent migrations:** Schema can be re-applied without side effects\n4. **Read-only briefing:** Decoupled from live sweep; never blocks\n5. **Security gate single-owner:** All servability checks route through one source (roles/security/gate.py)\n6. **Retry resilience:** Tenacity full-jitter retry + Haiku fallback catches transient errors\n\n---\n\n**Report date:** 2026-06-23  \n**Codebase scope:** Aurora nightly multi-agent sweep system (~300K LOC including tests + library)  \n**Deep-think focus:** Core Python system (orchestrator, llm, publisher, morning_briefing, dashboard, kb, bin)"}],"resolvedModel":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","totalDurationMs":223126,"totalTokens":87707,"totalToolUseCount":63,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":892,"cache_read_input_tokens":73425,"output_tokens":13383,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":892},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":7,"output_tokens":13383,"cache_read_input_tokens":73425,"cache_creation_input_tokens":892,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":892,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":22,"searchCount":26,"bashCount":15,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
